WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.440
The SCP Foundation does their best to live
up to their famous namesake: They secure and

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.870
contain anomalies and monsters from all around
the world - or sometimes even off-world - and

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:15.540
protect the public from the dangers that these
strange entities might pose.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.789
However, despite their efforts to maintain
security and keep their subjects under lock

00:00:19.789 --> 00:00:25.779
and key, there are sometimes creatures so
clever, so devious, and so determined to escape

00:00:25.779 --> 00:00:30.650
their captivity and wreak havoc on the world,
that even the SCP foundation struggles to

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.860
keep them from getting free.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:38.030
One example is SCP-035, or the Possessive
Mask.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:44.140
SCP-035 is one of the most dangerous test
subjects in SCP Foundation custody, and its

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:50.200
mere presence at the Foundation has resulted
in untold damage, death, and destruction.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.820
It seems innocent enough, to the untrained
eye.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:57.390
The mask, which resembles a classic white
porcelain “comedy” mask - though it occasionally

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:02.400
changes its expression to “tragedy” - has
been in existence since at least the 1800s.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:08.060
In the late 19th century the Foundation discovered
the mask in a sealed crypt beneath an abandoned

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.390
home in Venice.

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:13.130
It is unknown how it got there, or how the
Foundation knew to look for it.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:17.979
If there ever was an explanation for its discovery,
it has long since been removed or redacted

00:01:17.979 --> 00:01:19.829
from the Foundation’s archives.

00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:24.729
You’re probably wondering: How can a simple
mask leave multiple seasoned Foundation employees

00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:25.729
dead?

00:01:25.729 --> 00:01:30.270
Well, like everything at the SCP foundation,
this mask is not what it seems.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:35.090
There is a reason its classification is “keter”,
a designation that refers to an entity that’s

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:39.110
excessively difficult to contain - and it
couples this difficulty with a pronounced

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:43.990
hostility toward human life, and the ability
to cause widespread destruction in the event

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:45.939
of a containment breach.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:51.210
These are qualities that the poor unfortunate
souls assigned to guard SCP-035 would come

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.840
to understand all too well.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:58.469
The Possessive Mask is a parasitic entity,
constantly seeking out a host willing to put

00:01:58.469 --> 00:01:59.549
it on.

00:01:59.549 --> 00:02:04.170
Any human being in the mask’s proximity
experiences a sudden, unexplainable urge to

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:08.560
put it on and once they do, there’s no going
back.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.849
SCP Foundation research has determined that
once a host has put on the mask, their brain

00:02:12.849 --> 00:02:17.780
waves are replaced with an alternative pattern,
this one coming from the mask, rendering the

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.000
host effectively brain dead.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.300
Once the host’s brain function has been
eliminated, the mask takes over, piloting

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.360
their body and even speaking through them.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:30.739
However, the mask can only occupy a host for
a small amount of time before the body begins

00:02:30.739 --> 00:02:36.209
to decay and decompose, eventually rotting
away completely, leaving nothing but desiccated

00:02:36.209 --> 00:02:40.350
flesh and bones where there once was a person.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:45.319
SCP-035 is capable of possessing any humanoid
being, whether that’s an actual human being

00:02:45.319 --> 00:02:48.010
or a lifeless humanoid shape.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:53.180
Despite all their research, the SCP Foundation
unknowingly gave the Mask all the tools and

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:59.280
resources it needed to break containment...
and leave a trail of bodies in its wake.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:04.379
For a time, the mask was given “host privileges,”
meaning that it was purposely allowed to occupy

00:03:04.379 --> 00:03:07.659
a host in order to speak with the scientists
studying it.

00:03:07.659 --> 00:03:11.580
In order to avoid murky ethical issues, the
host was usually something inanimate like

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.550
a mannequin or a statue.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:17.659
These conditions, however unsettling, allowed
the researchers to carry out interviews with

00:03:17.659 --> 00:03:22.100
the consciousness housed inside the mask,
in the hope of beginning to understand it

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.240
and its motivations.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:30.629
However, SCP-035 lost all access to its host
privileges after it almost pulled off an unprecedented,

00:03:30.629 --> 00:03:34.349
shocking, and nearly catastrophic escape attempt.

00:03:34.349 --> 00:03:38.319
In its early days at the facility, when it
was still allowed host privileges, it was

00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:42.860
contained in a triple locked room and monitored
by several research personnel.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:46.349
These were experienced researchers who had
been with the Foundation for a minimum of

00:03:46.349 --> 00:03:51.260
five years each, an unusually long tenure
in such a dangerous and mentally corrosive

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:52.519
line of work.

00:03:52.519 --> 00:03:56.349
These research staff members were thought
to be the most capable of handling interactions

00:03:56.349 --> 00:04:00.379
with the mask, and be able to resist its attempts
at manipulation.

00:04:00.379 --> 00:04:06.230
Unfortunately, these assumptions were naive,
and seriously underestimated the mask’s

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:07.230
power.

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:11.670
Research on the mask indicates that the mask
is incredibly intelligent and a skilled manipulator.

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:15.880
It has a photographic memory, intelligence
that would rank in the 99th percentile of

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:21.280
humans, and the ability to incite dramatic
changes in the behavior in people that it

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:22.280
talks to.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:27.910
One particularly infamous interview, between
the entity and an unnamed Doctor at the Foundation,

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:31.520
suggested that the mask may even possess telepathic
abilities.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.380
The mask was able to give details about the
Doctor’s life that no one else was privy

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:38.920
to, including knowledge of an affair that
his wife was having.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:43.570
Following the interview, the Doctor suffered
a psychotic break and committed suicide just

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:45.070
24 hours later.

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:50.250
The mask is able to use its superior intelligence,
charismatic personality, and mind reading

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:53.590
abilities to get inside the heads of those
it speaks with.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:58.910
It will pull out any and all psychological
stops to get what it wants, leaving broken

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.940
minds and spirits in its wake.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:06.470
It was really only a matter of time before
it used this skill set to its advantage and

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:09.150
attempted to escape its confinement.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:11.570
The day of the escape attempt was like any
other.

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:16.590
The research staff, a team of three intelligent,
experienced men, checked into the facility,

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:20.500
measured the conditions of the mask’s containment
unit, and began the process of interviewing

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.340
the mask like normal.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:26.780
Its motions were slow and looked to require
great effort, as its current host was beginning

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:29.000
to degrade beyond use.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:33.210
The mask was attached to the blank face of
a mannequin, and corrosive black liquid could

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:36.050
be seen oozing from its eye and mouth holes.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:41.190
This liquid is excreted by the mask at a near-constant
rate, and is thought to be at least partially

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:44.310
responsible for the accelerated decay of the
host bodies.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:49.431
In spite of the entity’s unsettling, nightmarish
appearance, it was just another day’s work

00:05:49.431 --> 00:05:56.600
for the men assigned to monitor SCP-035, and
so they carried on with their daily routine.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:06:00.840
Everything was going according to plan until
one of the men, Dr. Jones, began to behave

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:01.840
erratically.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.321
He demanded that his fellow scientists leave
him alone with the mask for a while, and allow

00:06:05.321 --> 00:06:08.020
him to engage in a private conversation with
it.

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:12.900
It is unknown what exactly the two spoke about
while the other two scientists were absent,

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:15.940
as the security footage captured has no sound.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:20.210
However, several minutes into the conversation
in the footage, Dr. Jones can be seen dissolving

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:25.910
into a fit of tears, laying on the ground
and shaking with sobs as the mask dispassionately

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:27.070
watches.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:32.150
He then climbs onto his knees, begging the
mask for something, before he embraces it.

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:37.870
He holds the mannequin in his arms for five
straight minutes, weeping again, before they

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:38.870
separate.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:43.030
After this disturbing emotional display, Dr.
Jones brought the other scientists back into

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:44.990
the room with him.

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:49.300
What happened next is still uncertain, but
there are a few things that we know for sure.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.380
The other scientists began to speak with the
mask.

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:55.660
In later interviews, the other scientists
were bordering on incoherent, babbling about

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:57.910
various traumas from their lives.

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:01.930
One repeatedly referred to a drunk driving
accident where a dear friend was killed, and

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:03.560
he was at fault.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.470
Another simply cried out for his mother again
and again.

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:11.620
Whatever the mask said to them, it was enough
to completely destroy their mental health.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:16.300
After the other two scientists had been emotionally
devastated by the mask, Dr. Jones escalated

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:17.860
the situation further.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:23.110
Dr. Jones removed the mask from the decaying
mannequin body, and, shocking everyone who

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:28.320
would later review the security footage, placed
it onto his own face.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.539
Once the mask was in place, Dr. Jones went
unnaturally still for several moments, as

00:07:29.539 --> 00:07:30.539
his colleagues looked on.

00:07:30.539 --> 00:07:31.539
This is where the security footage ends.

00:07:31.539 --> 00:07:36.050
At the command of the mask which was now speaking
through Dr. Jones, the other two men switched

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:38.870
off all security cameras monitoring SCP-035’s
containment facility.

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:46.310
The mask, piloting the body of Dr. Jones like
a horrible fleshy puppet, made its way through

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:50.990
the facility, avoiding detection until it
reached the exit doors, where it was finally

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:54.430
stopped by a team of over a dozen security
guards.

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:58.530
Knowing the dangers of touching the mask,
all Foundation employees involved in the re-containment

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:02.710
of SCP-035 refused to remove it from Dr. Jones’
face.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:07.430
Instead, he was placed in the locked room
with the mask still on, left alone to be observed

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:12.020
over the security cameras until his body had
decomposed beyond use.

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:16.840
His body paced back and forth in its cell
for days, flesh rotting and dropping away

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:19.330
until only sinew and bone remained.

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:24.180
Only when the bones began to turn black and
brittle, crumbling apart into dust, did the

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:25.580
body finally stop moving.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:30.840
His family was notified, the mask was carefully
removed from what was left of his body, and

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:32.599
his remains were destroyed.

00:08:32.599 --> 00:08:37.750
The other two scientists involved in the SCP-035
escape attempt were terminated, and their

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.250
files destroyed.

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:43.710
After this incident, a few more failed escape
attempts, and the acknowledgement of the devastation

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:48.470
that could have been caused if the mask had
made its way out into the general population,

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:52.399
SCP-035 lost its host privileges altogether.

00:08:52.399 --> 00:08:56.310
Several research staff protested this decision,
insisting that there was more to be learned

00:08:56.310 --> 00:09:00.680
from speaking with the entity, and citing
valuable information that it had given about

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:01.830
other SCP’s.

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:06.720
However, the risk was determined to considerably
outweigh the potential reward, and the request

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:10.790
to reinstate 035’s host privileges was denied.

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:16.310
Several staff members went so far as to erupt
into violent outbursts on 035’s behalf,

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:20.839
attacking their superiors who refused to provide
the mask with a new host, clawing at them

00:09:20.839 --> 00:09:22.900
with animalistic rage.

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:26.970
Any staff members that submitted a request
to reinstate said privileges were considered

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:32.950
a security threat, and reassigned to a different
SCP or in some cases terminated.

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:38.470
Any staff member who had direct contact with
SCP-035 was also terminated, in order to avoid

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:41.880
the risk of any more staff-aided escape attempts.

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:46.170
The mask is now kept in a hermetically-sealed
glass case, and there is a psychologist on

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:50.820
call to provide assistance to anyone guarding
it, in case of adverse effects on their mental

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:53.390
health from the mask’s presence.

00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:57.600
Personnel that work around the mask, even
in its current dormant state, experience frequent

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:00.940
violent outbursts and a higher rate of suicide.

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:05.040
Even without a host, the mask’s corrosive
effects have spread across its containment

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.060
facility.

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:10.360
The walls of the room have begun to secrete
the same black liquid that emanates from the

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:15.240
mask, which tests have revealed to be highly
contaminated human blood, that damages the

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:18.820
structural integrity of the walls following
prolonged contact.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:24.040
This blood has begun to form patterns on the
walls, spelling out words and phrases in Italian,

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:30.640
Latin, Greek, and Sanskrit, as well as depicting
drawings of ritual sacrifice and mutilation.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:35.020
Staff members also report hearing unintelligible
whispering and horrifying, high-pitched laughter

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:37.050
when in proximity to the mask.

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:42.630
Further exposure to the mask results in migraines,
hemorrhaging around the eyes, mouth, and nose,

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:45.190
and an eventual psychotic break.

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:48.870
Between the corrosive substance appearing
on the walls, and the physical and psychological

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:55.960
damage to employees, SCP-035 is becoming increasingly
difficult to contain and there are debates

00:10:55.960 --> 00:11:00.920
among staff as to whether the entity can,
in fact, be contained at all.

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:06.480
As soon as possible, SCP-035 will be moved
into a new containment facility, and its previous

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:10.170
cell will be isolated from the rest of the
foundation’s property and destroyed for

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:11.769
the safety of all involved.

00:11:11.769 --> 00:11:15.510
We can only hope that the new containment
procedures are more effective than the last

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:19.680
ones, and that this mask never makes its way
into the world again.

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:23.770
If it does, who knows how many lives it will
claim?

00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:28.399
In the meantime, if you ever come across a
strange mask and feel a nearly uncontrollable

00:11:28.399 --> 00:11:34.170
urge to put it on…ignore the whispered pleas
to just try it, ignore the echoing laugher

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:38.600
and the sensation of something older and more
powerful than you can imagine rummaging through

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:42.160
your deepest, darkest secret thoughts.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:46.070
Turn around, and run as fast as you can in
the other direction.

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:48.450
You’ll be glad that you did.

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:50.779
The desert is still.

00:11:50.779 --> 00:11:57.730
The night seems endless, silent, and at peace…
until it’s pierced by the sound of gunshots

00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:59.579
and screams.

00:11:59.579 --> 00:12:05.070
Deep in the Sahara, the SCP Foundation is
waging war against a newly discovered enemy.

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:10.060
A squad of foundation agents is retreating,
trying to get away from the ones who massacred

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:11.950
their allies.

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:16.470
They were attempting to eliminate the threat
using conventional means, but their rifles

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:21.740
were no match for the reality bending entities
of the Kingdom of Abaddon.

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:25.350
The retreating agents cover one another as
they make their way back to the extraction

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:26.350
point.

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:28.180
The enemy force advances.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:32.620
Agents that are caught too close to the sorcerers
of Abaddon disintegrate into thin air.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:34.459
This is not an enemy they can defeat.

00:12:34.459 --> 00:12:40.410
The SCP agents need to get back to base and
relay what they have found to their superiors.

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:45.019
Out of the hundreds of agents sent into the
Sahara that night, only a handful make it

00:12:45.019 --> 00:12:46.019
out alive.

00:12:46.019 --> 00:12:50.160
They are debriefed by their superiors at the
Foundation who classify the anomalous humanoids

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.310
under the highest of threat levels.

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:54.970
The Kingdom of Abaddon is a threat.

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:59.410
The Kingdom of Abaddon must be eliminated.

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:02.680
Reconnaissance done prior to the disastrous
mission had alerted the Foundation to the

00:13:02.680 --> 00:13:07.370
presence of anomalies in the region, but they
had no idea how strong the anomalous humanoids

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:08.490
would be.

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:12.810
From data gathered through old reports, it
seemed that the Abaddon humanoids were responsible

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:18.550
for the deaths of no fewer than 75 Foundation
personnel, and had stolen at least 12 different

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:20.709
items from the Foundation.

00:13:20.709 --> 00:13:25.620
The leaders of the SCP Foundation tasked research
team Omega-5 with developing a weapon that

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:29.530
would be capable of destroying the Kingdom
of Abaddon once and for all.

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:34.240
The weapon they are researching must be capable
of long range destruction, because the moment

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:38.829
any Foundation agent gets close to the area,
they are vaporized by the reality manipulating

00:13:38.829 --> 00:13:44.010
powers of its inhabitants The project is given
the name “Twins of God” and is led by

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:48.070
a Foundation doctor known only by the designation
“O5-1.”

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:54.520
O5-1 is popular in the SCP Foundation, well
known for his in-depth research and charismatic

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:58.520
personality, making him the perfect person
to lead such a project.

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:03.710
And O5-1 recently came across an anomaly that
he believes holds the solution the Foundation

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:06.980
has been looking for to defeat the Kingdom
of Abaddon…

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:11.360
Item-001.And so the Omega-5 team gets to work.

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:16.019
They discover that the anomaly has incredible
powers when put inside a host, which they

00:14:16.019 --> 00:14:20.690
refer to as an Item-001 entity, and set up
a series of experiments using different people

00:14:20.690 --> 00:14:25.630
to harness its energy The first series of
tests all end in tragedy.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:30.160
The anomaly causes the entity it inhabits
to become intensely radioactive.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:35.600
Anyone who gets close to it succumbs to immediate
radiation sickness, and eventually death.

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:39.750
To stop the radiation problems the Omega-5
research group intensifies the containment

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:40.830
procedures.

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:45.089
O5-1 receives reports from the higher ups
that the Kingdom of Abaddon has attacked another

00:14:45.089 --> 00:14:47.470
Foundation facility in Sudan.

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:49.130
Long-range defense is needed A.S.A.P.

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:55.470
The administrator puts more pressure on Omega-5,
and especially its leader O5-1, to solve the

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:59.959
problems of Item-001 and develop a weapon
that can save the Foundation.

00:14:59.959 --> 00:15:05.589
He stays awake for days on end, working tirelessly
to create a safe and controllable Item-001

00:15:05.589 --> 00:15:07.019
entity.

00:15:07.019 --> 00:15:11.900
Although there are signs that the weapon will
work, it is still unpredictable.

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:18.000
When Item-001 is initiated, the host entity
becomes paralyzed, suffers severe cerebral

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:22.820
hemorrhaging, and soon a new host is needed
before testing can begin again.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:26.200
And that’s not the only thing going wrong.

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:30.760
Whenever the anomaly is put into a new host,
sudden and random destruction of on-site structures

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:32.370
and personnel takes place.

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:37.270
O5-1 knows though, that if this power can
be harnessed and controlled in the right way,

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:41.319
that it could be the weapon that the Foundation
needs to wipe out the Kingdom of Abaddon once

00:15:41.319 --> 00:15:42.700
and for all.

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:49.120
In order to control Item-001, O5-1 has a mind-kill
switch implanted in its hosts’ brains.

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:54.910
O5-1 can activate the implant to incapacitate
the host and immediately stop the unwanted

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:55.910
destruction.

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:59.829
Countless hosts are terminated by this mind-kill
switch in the early trials conducted by the

00:15:59.829 --> 00:16:06.270
Omega-5 team, but progress continues to be
made and eventually a hypothesis is formulated.

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:11.079
Perhaps the disastrous side effects of Item-001
can be offset by spreading the anomaly across

00:16:11.079 --> 00:16:12.449
multiple subjects.

00:16:12.449 --> 00:16:17.000
They theorize that the immense mental load
of the anomaly can be distributed among several

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:21.970
hosts, thus reducing the toll it takes on
each and giving them the ability to control

00:16:21.970 --> 00:16:23.320
its immense power.

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:29.740
But O5-1 and the Omega-5 team need more data,
and for that, they need more bodies.

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:34.160
They consult with the director of Site-17
and it is concluded that the nearby town of

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:39.100
San Marco would be an appropriate place to
get the additional test subjects they require.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:44.699
On a quiet Sunday morning, Omega-5 along with
support from a squad of armed SCP agents storm

00:16:44.699 --> 00:16:48.639
into the San Marcos de la Vida Sterna Church
during the middle of mass.

00:16:48.639 --> 00:16:53.139
They gather up a number of the younger congregants
and bring them back to the site where Item-001

00:16:53.139 --> 00:16:54.839
is housed.

00:16:54.839 --> 00:16:59.519
The researchers quickly ran through their
new supply of test subjects though, and Omega-5

00:16:59.519 --> 00:17:03.709
would need to get even more if their research
was to continue.

00:17:03.709 --> 00:17:08.510
Instead of going back and forth between the
testing facility and San Marco, O5-1 decides

00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:12.829
to move the entire Item-001 operation to the
town itself.

00:17:12.829 --> 00:17:18.610
He renames the town, Testing Site-001, and
Omega-5 rounds up 23 of the healthiest subjects

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:22.370
they can find for use in the next series of
research tests.

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:27.049
A few weeks after occupying the town of San
Marco, Omega-5 makes it’s most substantial

00:17:27.049 --> 00:17:28.740
progress yet.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:33.570
Just as they theorized, by spreading out the
anomaly of Item-001 across a specific group

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:36.330
of hosts, they can control its powers.

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:40.960
The tests may have cost the lives of almost
everyone in the town, but the ends certainly

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:42.900
justify the means.

00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:47.580
The Kingdom of Abaddon poses an existential
threat to the SCP Foundation after all, and

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:52.370
thanks to this research they will soon have
a weapon capable of bringing them victory.

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:58.950
The Foundation administrator criticizes O5-1’s
methods, but can’t argue with his results.

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:01.559
Unfortunately, O5-1 has a dark secret.

00:18:01.559 --> 00:18:05.690
A secret that disturbs even the most hardened
and loyal members of Omega-5.

00:18:05.690 --> 00:18:10.220
A secret that has to do with the Item-001
hosts.

00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:15.550
The hosts that Omega-5 has made its major
progress with are not the ordinary test subjects

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:17.960
normally used by the Foundation.

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:22.600
No, the test subjects O5-1 makes his breakthrough
with… are children.

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:28.250
Nine of them to be exact, all between four
and eleven years old.

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:33.510
Despite being told specifically by the Foundation
administrator to only test on adults, the

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:38.490
research required O5-1 to break the chain
of command and follow the science down the

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:39.700
path it led.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:44.320
The children are contained in a reinforced
bunker where only O5-1, and a select few,

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:45.320
have access.

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:49.200
They are technically alive, but are functionally
brain dead.

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:54.270
The group of nine children share a hive mind
that can process information, and more importantly,

00:18:54.270 --> 00:19:00.520
can unleash the full potential of the implanted
anomaly, creating and controlling a devastating

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:01.580
power.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:04.650
But not everyone is thrilled with what they’ve
achieved.

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:08.110
Members of Omega-5 are haunted by the screams
of the children that they’ve forced to be

00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:10.370
part of their weapon development program.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:15.559
They describe their merging with Item-001
as being a process that rips out their souls

00:19:15.559 --> 00:19:18.659
and replaces them with something much more
sinister.

00:19:18.659 --> 00:19:26.720
In fact all of Omega-5 regret what they have
been a part of and what they’ve done, all

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:27.899
except O5-1.

00:19:27.899 --> 00:19:32.809
The nine children can channel unprecedented
amounts of energy from an unknown origin that

00:19:32.809 --> 00:19:39.230
Omega-5 hypothesizes comes from an extradimensional
source, which is then used to unbind atoms

00:19:39.230 --> 00:19:40.630
at the quantum level.

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:45.039
When the right activation words are spoken,
it appears as though this tremendous power

00:19:45.039 --> 00:19:49.410
gives the children the ability to annihilate
anything in the entire universe.

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:53.140
It’s the gun to end all guns.

00:19:53.140 --> 00:19:57.350
And only O5-1 has the key to control it.

00:19:57.350 --> 00:20:02.520
The nine children work so well within Item-001
that Omega-5 reclassifies it to include the

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:04.080
nine children themselves.

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:12.360
They are not just the entity housing or controlling
Item-001, they permanently become Item-001.

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:16.890
Once Omega-5 has a better understanding of
Item-001, they begin to run tests to find

00:20:16.890 --> 00:20:19.169
out the full extent of its abilities.

00:20:19.169 --> 00:20:21.990
First they test the distance Item-001 can
reach.

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:27.299
The initial test that Omega-5 carries out
is on a steel rod placed 5 kilometers away.

00:20:27.299 --> 00:20:30.710
O5-1 orders the children to destroy the target.

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:34.190
Moments later the phone next to O5-1 begins
to ring.

00:20:34.190 --> 00:20:38.070
When he picks it up the observer tasked with
watching the pole is on the other end.

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:42.000
He informs O5-1 that the steel rod has been
completely vaporized.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:44.210
O5-1 is not satisfied though.

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:49.730
He has another pole set out, this time placed
8,000 kilometers away from the nine children.

00:20:49.730 --> 00:20:53.550
O5-1 asks the children to destroy that rod.

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:56.090
Almost immediately, the phone rings again.

00:20:56.090 --> 00:20:58.430
The target has been vaporized.

00:20:58.430 --> 00:21:01.030
O5-1 smiles.

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:06.210
The next series of tests Omega-5 runs on Item-001
are to determine the maximum size of an object

00:21:06.210 --> 00:21:07.610
that can be destroyed.

00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:12.320
The tests start out with a steel sphere, 3
meters in diameter, placed 1,000 kilometers

00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:13.320
from Item-001.

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:17.020
O5-1 orders the children to destroy the object.

00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:19.220
It is instantly vaporized.

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:21.500
O5-1 has seen enough small tests.

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:24.150
It’s time for something big.

00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:28.200
So he does something that will later be questioned
by everyone at the SCP Foundation.

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:34.080
He orders the nine children to destroy a Church
of the Broken God worship site in Turkey.

00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:39.130
Not long after the destruction order is given
to Item-001, reports begin coming in.

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:44.720
The worship site has been obliterated with
no observable damage to the surrounding area.

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:46.540
Deadly and precise.

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:49.309
O5-1 closes his eyes and takes a deep breath.

00:21:49.309 --> 00:21:52.940
He looks as if he is overcome by an immense
spiritual experience.

00:21:52.940 --> 00:21:58.429
He opens his eyes, leans over to the children,
and whispers the name of someone.

00:21:58.429 --> 00:22:03.890
Later that day, O5-1 finds out that the target
he had named has been vaporized.

00:22:03.890 --> 00:22:08.240
The success of Omega-5 and Item-001 is relayed
to the administration of the Foundation.

00:22:08.240 --> 00:22:14.410
They are so impressed that they make plans
to use Item-001 to eliminate the Abaddon threat

00:22:14.410 --> 00:22:16.010
once and for all.

00:22:16.010 --> 00:22:21.220
However, one of the heads of the foundation,
Administrator Williams, has major concerns

00:22:21.220 --> 00:22:24.350
about the way O5-1 is running the program.

00:22:24.350 --> 00:22:31.789
The updates that O5-1 has been sending have
become less scientific, and more philosophical…

00:22:31.789 --> 00:22:33.049
more…

00:22:33.049 --> 00:22:34.299
spiritual.

00:22:34.299 --> 00:22:38.669
Administrator Williams sends a letter to O5-1
reassuring him that he is doing good work,

00:22:38.669 --> 00:22:44.029
but once the mission to destroy the Kingdom
of Abaddon is completed, O5-1 will be promoted

00:22:44.029 --> 00:22:46.929
to director, and reassigned to the newly constructed
Site-19.

00:22:46.929 --> 00:22:53.620
For the good of the Foundation, and maybe
the world, he’ll be permanently moved away

00:22:53.620 --> 00:22:55.429
from Item-001.

00:22:55.429 --> 00:23:01.390
O5-1’s response is short and to the point,
“I am fine, Administrator.

00:23:01.390 --> 00:23:02.559
The project is finished.

00:23:02.559 --> 00:23:06.799
We will complete our task when you arrive.”

00:23:06.799 --> 00:23:09.799
Administrator Williams arrives at Site-001
a few days later.

00:23:09.799 --> 00:23:13.809
He is greeted by O5-1 and the Omega-5 team.

00:23:13.809 --> 00:23:17.570
Williams can’t help but notice that O5-1
has a strange look in his eyes.

00:23:17.570 --> 00:23:23.960
It is the look of a crazed man who has been
lost in his work, and who has, perhaps, lost

00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:25.480
himself.

00:23:25.480 --> 00:23:30.150
Williams puts the thought away though and
walks with O5-1 and his accompanying agents

00:23:30.150 --> 00:23:35.680
to the viewing area where the powers of Item-001
will be demonstrated.

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:40.369
Administrator Williams and the other agents
watch from a protected viewing room as O5-1

00:23:40.369 --> 00:23:42.740
enters the chamber of his new super weapon.

00:23:42.740 --> 00:23:47.559
It’s time to see if their weapon that has
had so much time, effort, sweat, tears, and

00:23:47.559 --> 00:23:52.059
especially blood poured into it, will have
been worth it.

00:23:52.059 --> 00:23:56.340
Everyone watches as O5-1 leans over and says
the name of the Abaddon Citadel to the nine

00:23:56.340 --> 00:23:57.559
children.

00:23:57.559 --> 00:23:59.750
All at once, they start to glow.

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:04.060
No one observing can see what has happened
in the far off Kingdom, but they know something

00:24:04.060 --> 00:24:05.490
big has happened.

00:24:05.490 --> 00:24:09.120
The administrator is thrilled, but notices
something.

00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:13.010
O5-1 hesitated a moment while leaning over
the children before standing back up.

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:15.820
Did he whisper something else to them?

00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:20.309
And then Administrator Williams vaporizes,
pulled apart at an atomic level before he

00:24:20.309 --> 00:24:21.840
has the chance to scream.

00:24:21.840 --> 00:24:23.490
What’s going on?

00:24:23.490 --> 00:24:27.370
The agents standing next to where Administrator
Williams previously existed begin to yell

00:24:27.370 --> 00:24:28.400
and pull out their guns.

00:24:28.400 --> 00:24:32.789
They burst through the door of the observation
room and run down the hallway towards where

00:24:32.789 --> 00:24:35.390
O5-1 and the nine children are located.

00:24:35.390 --> 00:24:39.289
The armed agents rush into the room, but O5-1
is gone.

00:24:39.289 --> 00:24:42.149
The nine children are still.

00:24:42.149 --> 00:24:47.429
Over the next few weeks O5-1 is reported to
be seen several times by SCP agents.

00:24:47.429 --> 00:24:51.190
However, no one is able to catch him, and
it appears as though other members of the

00:24:51.190 --> 00:24:55.990
SCP Foundation have also gone AWOL as well,
perhaps joining him on the run.

00:24:55.990 --> 00:25:00.960
It is unclear what his plan is, but reports
from the reconnaissance team sent into the

00:25:00.960 --> 00:25:05.510
Sahara make it obvious what the result of
his first command to the children was.

00:25:05.510 --> 00:25:09.299
There isn’t a single humanoid or building
left in the Kingdom of Abaddon.

00:25:09.299 --> 00:25:15.159
But even with this victory, the highest levels
of the SCP Foundation have an ominous thought

00:25:15.159 --> 00:25:17.070
lurking in the back of their minds.

00:25:17.070 --> 00:25:21.799
Where did O5-1 go, and what is he planning
to do next?

00:25:21.799 --> 00:25:26.600
Following the improper use of Item-001 leading
to the untimely death of a high ranking Foundation

00:25:26.600 --> 00:25:32.830
Staff member, the weapon was deemed too dangerous
and containment procedures were implemented.

00:25:32.830 --> 00:25:36.520
Due to the high amount of radiation they were
found to emit, the nine children were placed

00:25:36.520 --> 00:25:41.649
into lead lined bags and buried under 50 meters
of concrete beneath the church of San Marcos

00:25:41.649 --> 00:25:43.330
de la Vida Eterna.

00:25:43.330 --> 00:25:48.320
Though all of the children continue to be
functionally braindead, they still display

00:25:48.320 --> 00:25:53.720
signs of life despite their containment, and
by order of the Overseer Council, have been

00:25:53.720 --> 00:25:56.049
classified as a Thaumiel entity.

00:25:56.049 --> 00:26:01.100
It’s a natural instinct in many species
to protect their young - and sometimes it's

00:26:01.100 --> 00:26:05.860
not just their own babies, but any young that
look like them.

00:26:05.860 --> 00:26:11.090
Regardless of your personal feelings on human’s
earliest stage, it is a scientific fact that

00:26:11.090 --> 00:26:16.700
human babies are designed to emphasize their
own adorable helplessness to make sure that

00:26:16.700 --> 00:26:19.070
other, older humans take care of them.

00:26:19.070 --> 00:26:24.830
A baby’s cry is an inherently distressing
sound, and when we hear it, some deep, primal

00:26:24.830 --> 00:26:30.500
part of us feels the urge to comfort and care
for the child until the sound stops.

00:26:30.500 --> 00:26:35.131
But of course, we’re talking about the world
of the SCP Foundation here - where there are

00:26:35.131 --> 00:26:39.950
bunnies that can eat anything, teddy bears
that might steal your organs to make duplicates

00:26:39.950 --> 00:26:45.750
of themselves, and chocolate fountains filled
with trillions of murderous insects.

00:26:45.750 --> 00:26:50.900
Nothing is what it seems here, and even the
most innocent and cute creatures may be hiding

00:26:50.900 --> 00:26:55.710
a deadly secret - SCP-734 being no exception.

00:26:55.710 --> 00:26:58.850
Today, we’re talking about The Baby.

00:26:58.850 --> 00:27:04.140
This anomaly proves that dangerous things
can come in small packages, but where others

00:27:04.140 --> 00:27:10.690
only saw misery and death, the SCP Foundation
saw a certain potential…

00:27:10.690 --> 00:27:15.930
Our story begins in the maternity ward of
a hospital in the USA, where every medical

00:27:15.930 --> 00:27:20.990
professional’s worst nightmare was unfolding:
An unknown but incredibly fast-acting flesh-eating

00:27:20.990 --> 00:27:25.429
pathogen seemed to be running rampant across
the hospital’s population.

00:27:25.429 --> 00:27:29.440
It began when patients who weren’t even
admitted for dermatological issues started

00:27:29.440 --> 00:27:33.370
complaining of severe itches and extreme skin
pain.

00:27:33.370 --> 00:27:38.280
Some nurses and doctors in the maternity ward
began to experience similar symptoms, as well

00:27:38.280 --> 00:27:42.200
as one of the infants, leading to a massive
quarantine effort.

00:27:42.200 --> 00:27:46.679
While the initial symptoms first appeared
to be limited to severe pain and discomfort

00:27:46.679 --> 00:27:51.740
on isolated parts of the skin, the condition
of the afflicted soon escalated.

00:27:51.740 --> 00:27:57.100
Their skin began to messily flake off as the
cells comprising it lost physical cohesion

00:27:57.100 --> 00:27:58.179
and died.

00:27:58.179 --> 00:28:03.840
It was a kind of strange, anomalous rot that
seemed to work inwards, first destroying the

00:28:03.840 --> 00:28:08.929
integrity of the outer layer of skin and then
causing further disintegration to deeper parts

00:28:08.929 --> 00:28:10.170
of the body.

00:28:10.170 --> 00:28:16.169
Once the skin had shed off, the pathogen would
turn its attention to what was lying beneath.

00:28:16.169 --> 00:28:22.250
Against all odds, the disease affected organs,
muscle tissue, the vascular system, and even

00:28:22.250 --> 00:28:23.960
bones.

00:28:23.960 --> 00:28:25.559
Nothing was spared.

00:28:25.559 --> 00:28:29.960
The victims’ bodies would completely break
down, and they would be dead within a few

00:28:29.960 --> 00:28:31.230
hours.

00:28:31.230 --> 00:28:35.720
By the time the pathogen had finished ravaging
its victims, what was left didn’t even look

00:28:35.720 --> 00:28:37.360
human anymore.

00:28:37.360 --> 00:28:42.610
Not only patients but doctors and nurses that
had been walking the wards mere hours before

00:28:42.610 --> 00:28:46.919
were now little more than piles of human tissue
sitting in what had previously been their

00:28:46.919 --> 00:28:48.659
hospital beds.

00:28:48.659 --> 00:28:54.750
Whatever this was, it seemed like the fastest
progressing infection in recorded history.

00:28:54.750 --> 00:29:00.690
Hospital staff and administrators were terrified
- this appeared to be an entirely new disease,

00:29:00.690 --> 00:29:05.779
with a mysterious form of transmission and,
worst of all, no cure.

00:29:05.779 --> 00:29:10.370
They were even more confused when several
black vans pulled up outside the hospital,

00:29:10.370 --> 00:29:14.679
and mysterious men in hazmat suits spilled
out and began setting up a quarantine zone

00:29:14.679 --> 00:29:16.710
around the entire building.

00:29:16.710 --> 00:29:21.679
Whoever these strange people were, they definitely
weren’t the CDC - little did the hospital

00:29:21.679 --> 00:29:26.260
personnel know that this was the group you
never want showing up and putting your location

00:29:26.260 --> 00:29:30.350
on lockdown - it was the SCP Foundation.

00:29:30.350 --> 00:29:35.090
The infected remains of the victims were taken
away for research purposes, and the Foundation

00:29:35.090 --> 00:29:39.250
operatives immediately began conducting debriefing
interviews with witnesses.

00:29:39.250 --> 00:29:44.399
They soon determined from a mix of eyewitness
accounts and hospital surveillance footage

00:29:44.399 --> 00:29:48.960
that everyone infected with the mysterious
pathogen had all been in a particular section

00:29:48.960 --> 00:29:51.690
of the maternity ward earlier in the day.

00:29:51.690 --> 00:29:56.840
And when the operatives investigated this
area, they found another strange detail.

00:29:56.840 --> 00:30:01.220
An infant had no registered mother present
in the hospital.

00:30:01.220 --> 00:30:05.220
The Foundation would later learn that this
was likely because the baby’s mother was

00:30:05.220 --> 00:30:08.200
the first victim of the deadly disease.

00:30:08.200 --> 00:30:13.490
After eliminating all other possible options,
it seemed that the only anomalous element

00:30:13.490 --> 00:30:18.299
that could have caused all of this was the
mysterious baby, though just how the mother

00:30:18.299 --> 00:30:23.530
even survived carrying the baby to term was
a mystery in and of itself.

00:30:23.530 --> 00:30:28.640
The baby was a caucasian male human infant
between seven and eight months of age.

00:30:28.640 --> 00:30:32.970
Nothing appeared outwardly anomalous about
the child, but they could confirm that every

00:30:32.970 --> 00:30:37.529
single victim of the anomalous pathogen had
come into physical contact with the child

00:30:37.529 --> 00:30:39.419
earlier that day.

00:30:39.419 --> 00:30:43.350
Everyone who had been at the hospital was
given amnestic treatment, and the Foundation

00:30:43.350 --> 00:30:47.550
constructed plausible cover stories for the
deaths that had occurred that day.

00:30:47.550 --> 00:30:52.720
Like so many others before it, the child was
secured and spirited away to the nearest applicable

00:30:52.720 --> 00:30:54.830
Foundation containment site.

00:30:54.830 --> 00:31:00.889
There it was reclassified as SCP-734, and
finally the real testing into what precisely

00:31:00.889 --> 00:31:04.120
this infant was capable of could begin.

00:31:04.120 --> 00:31:08.679
Physiologically, SCP-734 appeared mostly non-anomalous.

00:31:08.679 --> 00:31:13.419
The infant had above-average intelligence
and physical aptitude for a child his age

00:31:13.419 --> 00:31:18.480
but otherwise showed no mutations or abnormalities
that would suggest a divergence from typical

00:31:18.480 --> 00:31:20.250
human biology.

00:31:20.250 --> 00:31:24.590
Despite a vast array of tests performed by
the Foundation into essentially every aspect

00:31:24.590 --> 00:31:30.049
of 734’s biology, they couldn’t find anything
that hinted at the origin of the mysterious

00:31:30.049 --> 00:31:31.220
pathogen.

00:31:31.220 --> 00:31:36.750
But through some trial and extremely costly
error, the Foundation was able to learn more

00:31:36.750 --> 00:31:39.530
about how exactly the pathogen worked.

00:31:39.530 --> 00:31:44.191
The only vector for transmission seemed to
be direct contact with the baby itself, up

00:31:44.191 --> 00:31:48.419
to and including the fluids and residues it
leaves behind.

00:31:48.419 --> 00:31:52.520
Those affected cannot transmit the anomalous
“flaking” effect to others, meaning that

00:31:52.520 --> 00:31:55.640
the risk of an epidemic is relievingly minimal.

00:31:55.640 --> 00:32:00.539
But of course, accidents still happen, as
was discovered when one agent misplaced her

00:32:00.539 --> 00:32:05.179
sympathy for the baby and decided to remove
her mask while interacting with him.

00:32:05.179 --> 00:32:10.460
Her logic was that her masked face might have
caused the baby some kind of distress, and

00:32:10.460 --> 00:32:15.531
as long as she was only coming into contact
with him via her own gloved hands, everything

00:32:15.531 --> 00:32:16.980
would be fine.

00:32:16.980 --> 00:32:22.990
But some dust particles were floating in the
air at the time, and SCP-734 sneezed in her

00:32:22.990 --> 00:32:23.990
face.

00:32:23.990 --> 00:32:29.049
The agent began screaming in pain and recoiling
from the baby, but it was already too late.

00:32:29.049 --> 00:32:31.019
Her fate was sealed.

00:32:31.019 --> 00:32:35.179
She was taken to the infirmary and given sedatives
so that she could hopefully die in as little

00:32:35.179 --> 00:32:36.630
pain as possible.

00:32:36.630 --> 00:32:42.370
In roughly 72% of cases, amputation of the
affected areas has prevented the entire body

00:32:42.370 --> 00:32:48.280
from succumbing to the anomalous effects of
SCP-734, but this isn’t exactly feasible

00:32:48.280 --> 00:32:51.580
when the point of contact is the victim’s
head.

00:32:51.580 --> 00:32:56.029
Within hours, the agent’s flesh had flaked
off of her face, leaving her looking like

00:32:56.029 --> 00:32:57.830
a red, bloody skull.

00:32:57.830 --> 00:33:01.799
A few hours after that, she didn’t have
a head at all.

00:33:01.799 --> 00:33:06.960
Throughout the disintegration process of this
unfortunate agent, the Foundation took grisly

00:33:06.960 --> 00:33:07.960
photographs.

00:33:07.960 --> 00:33:13.750
These photographs are shown to anyone preparing
to work on the SCP-734 research project to

00:33:13.750 --> 00:33:19.140
teach them a hard lesson on the importance
of adhering to proper safety protocols.

00:33:19.140 --> 00:33:23.630
And these protocols about how to deal with
the Baby are incredibly tight, given that

00:33:23.630 --> 00:33:27.750
even incidental contact is often a death sentence.

00:33:27.750 --> 00:33:32.399
Anyone entering the Baby’s containment chamber
needs to wear contained-atmosphere hazmat

00:33:32.399 --> 00:33:33.399
suits.

00:33:33.399 --> 00:33:37.240
Anyone who makes physical contact with the
Baby, even when suited up, is immediately

00:33:37.240 --> 00:33:42.409
removed from the area and subject to several
hours of quarantine and observation.

00:33:42.409 --> 00:33:46.760
Even inanimate objects that have been inside
the containment chamber need to be thoroughly

00:33:46.760 --> 00:33:49.690
sterilized before being removed.

00:33:49.690 --> 00:33:55.809
Given that even anomalous children like SCP-734
have very delicate needs, a handler is always

00:33:55.809 --> 00:33:59.780
standing by in full hazmat gear to take care
of the baby.

00:33:59.780 --> 00:34:04.390
These handlers are rotated every hour to maintain
alertness and safety.

00:34:04.390 --> 00:34:10.520
These handlers feed and change SCP-734 regularly
and sometimes even provide toys that have

00:34:10.520 --> 00:34:12.940
been approved by the O5 Council.

00:34:12.940 --> 00:34:18.359
The Foundation has gone to great lengths to
keep SCP-734 alive and comfortable because

00:34:18.359 --> 00:34:23.800
they believe that SCP-734 could be an important
asset for them in the future.

00:34:23.800 --> 00:34:30.690
Or, more specifically, they see great strategic
value in SCP-734’s blood.

00:34:30.690 --> 00:34:36.000
As mentioned earlier, contact with any matter
from SCP-734 triggers its deadly anomalous

00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:39.200
effects, including bodily fluids like blood.

00:34:39.200 --> 00:34:44.589
But, unlike many toxic pathogens, in this
case there is no risk of the infection getting

00:34:44.589 --> 00:34:49.470
out of control since the infected do not become
vectors for transmission.

00:34:49.470 --> 00:34:54.260
Because of this, the blood of SCP-734 can
act as a powerful weapon for both terminating

00:34:54.260 --> 00:35:00.099
anomalies deemed unviable by the O5 Council
and assassinating dangerous people who belong

00:35:00.099 --> 00:35:02.050
to rival groups.

00:35:02.050 --> 00:35:06.300
Contact with the blood would completely destroy
the target’s body, with no other anomalous

00:35:06.300 --> 00:35:11.260
effects and no evidence of who exactly conducted
the hit.

00:35:11.260 --> 00:35:16.460
SCP-734 has been fitted with an arterial catheter
so that the Foundation can collect large quantities

00:35:16.460 --> 00:35:21.390
of blood from the anomalous infant every single
week for storage and research.

00:35:21.390 --> 00:35:24.430
But it isn’t just the blood that the Foundation
sees potential in.

00:35:24.430 --> 00:35:31.829
SCP-734 himself has scored incredibly well
on the Aeslinger Loyalty Index, the test the

00:35:31.829 --> 00:35:36.830
Foundation uses to judge the loyalty of potential
applicants to the Foundation cause.

00:35:36.830 --> 00:35:42.910
As SCP-734 matures, if these scores remain
consistent, he will likely be trained to become

00:35:42.910 --> 00:35:45.430
a Foundation field agent in the future.

00:35:45.430 --> 00:35:50.349
An agent capable of killing someone with a
touch would, needless to say, be an asset

00:35:50.349 --> 00:35:55.640
to certain covert missions that the Foundation
would probably prefer to keep off the books.

00:35:55.640 --> 00:36:00.260
Of course, the SCP Foundation recruiting certain
compliant anomalies to perform missions for

00:36:00.260 --> 00:36:02.589
them is far from unprecedented.

00:36:02.589 --> 00:36:10.510
The most infamous of these is SCP-076, also
known as Able, a supernatural, eternally-resurrecting

00:36:10.510 --> 00:36:14.130
swordsman and perhaps one of the finest warriors
who ever lived.

00:36:14.130 --> 00:36:18.359
The Foundation took note of this and channeled
his eternal thirst for battle into working

00:36:18.359 --> 00:36:20.850
with his very own Mobile Task Force.

00:36:20.850 --> 00:36:25.130
He could assist in missions by taking out
his bloodlust on enemy groups of interest

00:36:25.130 --> 00:36:27.060
and dangerous anomalies.

00:36:27.060 --> 00:36:31.930
However, this ended up working a little too
well and led to disaster.

00:36:31.930 --> 00:36:36.770
Able was so good at his job that he burned
through all his allotted missions at astonishing

00:36:36.770 --> 00:36:37.770
speed.

00:36:37.770 --> 00:36:42.500
Left with nothing more to do, Able got antsy,
which led to him turning his murderous desires

00:36:42.500 --> 00:36:47.010
on his fellow team members and then the Foundation
as a whole.

00:36:47.010 --> 00:36:52.190
It was an all-out massacre before his colleagues
were finally able to kill him and return him

00:36:52.190 --> 00:36:53.190
to containment.

00:36:53.190 --> 00:36:57.690
The failure of this initiative gave the very
idea of letting anomalies work for the Foundation

00:36:57.690 --> 00:36:59.849
in the field a bad name.

00:36:59.849 --> 00:37:06.380
But since then, things have changed, especially
with the establishment of MTF Alpha-9, aka

00:37:06.380 --> 00:37:11.880
Last Hope, a new mobile task force formed
entirely of anomalous individuals and their

00:37:11.880 --> 00:37:12.880
handlers.

00:37:12.880 --> 00:37:19.380
These consist of somewhat more stable anomalies,
such as Able’s counterpart, SCP-073, also

00:37:19.380 --> 00:37:20.869
known as Cain.

00:37:20.869 --> 00:37:26.210
Cain cannot be harmed, with any harm befalling
him simply being mirrored back on his attacker,

00:37:26.210 --> 00:37:31.010
and his vast array of knowledge makes him
an incredibly useful intelligence asset.

00:37:31.010 --> 00:37:36.710
Another of the several members of Last Hope
is Iris, also known as SCP-105.

00:37:36.710 --> 00:37:41.400
Much like Cain, Iris not only has anomalous
powers that make her immensely valuable for

00:37:41.400 --> 00:37:46.841
missions in the field, she’s also compliant
and capable of listening to reason, unlike

00:37:46.841 --> 00:37:47.869
Cain.

00:37:47.869 --> 00:37:52.849
Her abilities include being able to actively
surveil and even interact with photos of any

00:37:52.849 --> 00:37:56.640
location, especially when taken with her anomalous
camera.

00:37:56.640 --> 00:38:02.970
Someday, SCP-734 could count himself among
other anomalous Foundation agents like these,

00:38:02.970 --> 00:38:07.210
providing he continues to show promise and
doesn’t develop a dislike of the Foundation

00:38:07.210 --> 00:38:11.660
as he ages, since after all, he won’t be
a baby forever.

00:38:11.660 --> 00:38:16.830
So if ever you find yourself on the Foundation’s
bad side, you have a good reason to be paranoid.

00:38:16.830 --> 00:38:22.109
You’ll have no idea that one day, the man
who’s going to kill you will approach and

00:38:22.109 --> 00:38:24.350
shake your hand with a smile.

00:38:24.350 --> 00:38:29.090
It won’t be until later when you feel that
strange tingle on your palm and feel the skin

00:38:29.090 --> 00:38:35.089
starting to flake away that you’ll realize
you’ve been a dead man walking for hours.

00:38:35.089 --> 00:38:41.109
“There’s an app for that!”

00:38:41.109 --> 00:38:46.631
It was a phrase so ubiquitous in the early
days of the smartphone craze that it’s hard

00:38:46.631 --> 00:38:49.460
to believe Apple actually has it trademarked.

00:38:49.460 --> 00:38:54.349
It was a testament to a simple and immutable
truth about the world these new touchscreen

00:38:54.349 --> 00:38:59.750
phones were creating: No matter how strange
and obscure the need, there would be an app

00:38:59.750 --> 00:39:01.300
to fulfill it.

00:39:01.300 --> 00:39:04.800
Perhaps you remember iBeer - The app that
allowed you to pretend you were drinking a

00:39:04.800 --> 00:39:06.490
tall glass of beer…

00:39:06.490 --> 00:39:08.160
For some reason.

00:39:08.160 --> 00:39:11.890
There was Carrr Matey, an app that reminded
you where you parked your car…

00:39:11.890 --> 00:39:13.690
In a pirate voice.

00:39:13.690 --> 00:39:18.730
And who could forget “I Am Bread”, a surreal
game about controlling a sentient slice of

00:39:18.730 --> 00:39:21.280
bread on a quest to become toast.

00:39:21.280 --> 00:39:26.600
But there’s one app out there somewhere
on the market that you probably didn’t download.

00:39:26.600 --> 00:39:32.000
And if you did, well, you have our sincerest
apologies, because even seeing this video

00:39:32.000 --> 00:39:37.230
pop out onto your feed probably sent a chill
down your spine - Well, if that chill ever

00:39:37.230 --> 00:39:38.580
even left.

00:39:38.580 --> 00:39:43.230
Take it from one gentleman whose life took
a very strange turn after downloading a certain

00:39:43.230 --> 00:39:49.130
app that the SCP Foundation calls SCP-1471.

00:39:49.130 --> 00:39:53.430
Because the sentiment “There’s an app
for that” doesn’t exclude experiencing

00:39:53.430 --> 00:39:54.900
mortal terror…

00:39:54.900 --> 00:40:00.930
Joe Lillis, an insurance salesman from Milwaukee,
had just gone through another atrocious date.

00:40:00.930 --> 00:40:06.140
After a mediocre meal and an uncomfortable
35 minutes of inane babble, sensing the whole

00:40:06.140 --> 00:40:11.240
time that she really wasn’t that interested,
his date excused herself to take a quick phone

00:40:11.240 --> 00:40:12.510
call outside.

00:40:12.510 --> 00:40:17.190
Sadly for Joe, she never returned, leaving
him to pick up the check.

00:40:17.190 --> 00:40:22.160
Of all the many words you could use to describe
poor Joe Lillis, the most pertinent would

00:40:22.160 --> 00:40:23.710
be “lonely.”

00:40:23.710 --> 00:40:28.190
Ever since Carol, his wife of ten years, had
passed away in a freak accident, he’d been

00:40:28.190 --> 00:40:31.010
trying to find some kind of way to fill the
void.

00:40:31.010 --> 00:40:35.410
They’d been high school sweethearts, intent
on spending the rest of their lives with one

00:40:35.410 --> 00:40:36.410
another.

00:40:36.410 --> 00:40:40.339
As fate would have it, only Carol would get
that tainted luxury.

00:40:40.339 --> 00:40:44.550
Joe would be forced to endure life after the
joy of living had run its course.

00:40:44.550 --> 00:40:48.060
He only hoped he might be lucky enough to
find love again.

00:40:48.060 --> 00:40:53.380
However, Joe was on the wrong side of forty,
and as so many others his age were already

00:40:53.380 --> 00:40:56.980
hitched, he could feel his options going out
one by one.

00:40:56.980 --> 00:41:00.359
Would he be destined to live out the rest
of his days alone?

00:41:00.359 --> 00:41:04.680
Joe didn’t feel like spending the back half
of his life catching reruns of Seinfeld and

00:41:04.680 --> 00:41:07.980
tending to his fish; he needed to get out
of there.

00:41:07.980 --> 00:41:14.180
And thankfully, like the rest of us, he lived
in the internet age - He had more apps, websites,

00:41:14.180 --> 00:41:18.950
online services, and hot russian singles in
his area than he knew what to do with.

00:41:18.950 --> 00:41:22.450
So, surely, one would have the right person
for him!

00:41:22.450 --> 00:41:29.920
He’d tried them all: Tinder, Hinge, Match.com,
Plenty of Fish, eHarmony, Bumble, Zoosk, OKCupid,

00:41:29.920 --> 00:41:34.970
Friend Finder, Deeply Lonely Singles with
Low Expectations.com, and so much more.

00:41:34.970 --> 00:41:39.750
However, all it seemed to achieve was setting
him up for more disappointment.

00:41:39.750 --> 00:41:44.430
None of the dates he’d managed to get ever
resulted in anything getting serious.

00:41:44.430 --> 00:41:49.610
Heck, it was a minor miracle if he managed
to get any of them on a second date.

00:41:49.610 --> 00:41:50.610
Was this it?

00:41:50.610 --> 00:41:52.420
Was this his life now?

00:41:52.420 --> 00:41:57.720
Had he only ever gotten one shot at love,
and the grasping claws of fate yanked it away

00:41:57.720 --> 00:41:59.950
from him without a second thought?

00:41:59.950 --> 00:42:05.240
Would life continue on the hamster wheel of
loneliness - sleeping, getting up, eating,

00:42:05.240 --> 00:42:10.530
working, and sleeping again, every day getting
somehow both faster and slower as life trudged

00:42:10.530 --> 00:42:13.920
on to a disappointing yet inevitable conclusion?

00:42:13.920 --> 00:42:17.319
What a terrible fate to find yourself trapped
in…

00:42:17.319 --> 00:42:21.569
Whenever Joe started feeling maudlin like
this, he knew it was time to get proactive

00:42:21.569 --> 00:42:22.569
again.

00:42:22.569 --> 00:42:26.670
Maybe the right woman was out there - there
were billions of them, after all, surely at

00:42:26.670 --> 00:42:30.090
least one of them would be the perfect person
for him.

00:42:30.090 --> 00:42:31.850
He just needed the perfect app…

00:42:31.850 --> 00:42:36.530
He’d burned through all the most reputable
apps already, and was now perusing some of

00:42:36.530 --> 00:42:42.160
the slightly seedier options - most of which
were likely data mining fronts from the Balkans.

00:42:42.160 --> 00:42:47.730
However, as generic app after generic app
passed, something different caught his eye.

00:42:47.730 --> 00:42:53.849
The icon was a smiling cartoon dog, and its
name was MalO Version.

00:42:53.849 --> 00:42:55.530
1.0.0.

00:42:55.530 --> 00:42:57.339
This gave him a little chuckle.

00:42:57.339 --> 00:43:02.470
At the very least, it was very different branding
from the rest of the dating apps he’d seen.

00:43:02.470 --> 00:43:05.660
Maybe it’d just been sorted into the wrong
section of the app store?

00:43:05.660 --> 00:43:09.100
He decided he’d click it and take a look
at the app’s description.

00:43:09.100 --> 00:43:10.350
The description read:

00:43:10.350 --> 00:43:14.180
“Never settle for those awkward feelings
of being alone ever again.

00:43:14.180 --> 00:43:19.609
MalO is an exciting and interactive experience
that will keep you engaged and intrigued.

00:43:19.609 --> 00:43:25.560
The anxiety of social situations can be nerve-racking,
but after just a few hours of MalO you will

00:43:25.560 --> 00:43:29.410
soon forget all about those painful emotions
of disappointment.

00:43:29.410 --> 00:43:33.890
Be part of the new craze that is quickly becoming
the next social substitute.

00:43:33.890 --> 00:43:38.930
Remember, the more you participate, the more
MalO will engage you.

00:43:38.930 --> 00:43:41.970
Your experience is completely up to you.

00:43:41.970 --> 00:43:44.059
Absolutely NO ADS.

00:43:44.059 --> 00:43:45.059
Enjoy!”

00:43:45.059 --> 00:43:46.059
Well…

00:43:46.059 --> 00:43:48.660
It certainly provoked Joe’s curiosity, at
the very least.

00:43:48.660 --> 00:43:53.619
He did want to banish his feelings of loneliness,
and seeing as the app was free and apparently

00:43:53.619 --> 00:43:58.310
had no ads, he’d surely be foolish to not
at least give it a whirl.

00:43:58.310 --> 00:43:59.740
What’s the worst that could happen?

00:43:59.740 --> 00:44:04.780
He began the installation and only then noticed
that the app had no listed developer.

00:44:04.780 --> 00:44:10.950
It took up 9.8 MB of memory, which he wasn’t
tech savvy enough to see any issues with.

00:44:10.950 --> 00:44:15.670
More than anything, Joe was just enticed by
the prospect of finally having another chance

00:44:15.670 --> 00:44:18.180
at companionship with MalO.

00:44:18.180 --> 00:44:22.849
After all, it is the “next social substitute”,
whatever that means.

00:44:22.849 --> 00:44:27.510
However, Joe’s excitement was quickly quashed
when he hit the home screen button, and noticed

00:44:27.510 --> 00:44:30.190
that the icon for the app never actually materialized.

00:44:30.190 --> 00:44:31.190
Strange.

00:44:31.190 --> 00:44:36.559
He checked the app store portal again and
saw that, according to them, the app had completely

00:44:36.559 --> 00:44:37.559
downloaded.

00:44:37.559 --> 00:44:38.559
What gives?

00:44:38.559 --> 00:44:41.270
Was it a glitch, or was MalO actually just
malware?

00:44:41.270 --> 00:44:45.780
Either way, he was disheartened by the fact
that this immaterial app certainly wouldn’t

00:44:45.780 --> 00:44:48.190
be getting him any companionship.

00:44:48.190 --> 00:44:50.329
Or so he thought, anyway.

00:44:50.329 --> 00:44:54.490
Joe was used to disappointment by now, so
he didn’t take the hit too personally.

00:44:54.490 --> 00:44:58.910
He decided to just play out the rest of his
evening on autopilot: Making himself some

00:44:58.910 --> 00:45:04.010
soup, doing the laundry, watching more Seinfeld
reruns, taking a cold shower, and preparing

00:45:04.010 --> 00:45:06.089
to cry himself to sleep again.

00:45:06.089 --> 00:45:11.650
MalO was already becoming a distant memory,
just like all deceptive sources of hope.

00:45:11.650 --> 00:45:17.210
But one strange thing happened that disrupted
Joe’s finely-tuned evening routine.

00:45:17.210 --> 00:45:19.809
He received a text message.

00:45:19.809 --> 00:45:23.869
This was incredibly strange, because nobody
ever seemed to text him.

00:45:23.869 --> 00:45:28.460
The last text he got was from Carol, just
before her accident, so it was almost surreal

00:45:28.460 --> 00:45:32.640
to hear that alert sound now, after everything
that’d happened.

00:45:32.640 --> 00:45:37.370
He checked and saw that the text was an image
attachment sent from an unknown number.

00:45:37.370 --> 00:45:40.559
Perplexed yet curious, he decided to open
it.

00:45:40.559 --> 00:45:45.640
His curiosity soon gave way to a kind of melancholy
nostalgia when he saw that the photo was of

00:45:45.640 --> 00:45:48.460
his and Carol’s favorite cafe in town.

00:45:48.460 --> 00:45:52.130
They’d spent many a morning there, back
when she was alive.

00:45:52.130 --> 00:45:56.150
Treating themselves to a nice cup of coffee
and perhaps a croissant.

00:45:56.150 --> 00:46:00.050
Just seeing it again caused an involuntary
smile to spread across his face.

00:46:00.050 --> 00:46:04.930
It never even occurred to him, as it probably
would have to others, that this could be seen

00:46:04.930 --> 00:46:06.270
as a little creepy.

00:46:06.270 --> 00:46:09.440
He hadn’t frequented the bakery since Carol
died.

00:46:09.440 --> 00:46:13.890
How would anyone even know that the place
held any significance for him?

00:46:13.890 --> 00:46:14.990
Was it a stalker?

00:46:14.990 --> 00:46:16.100
A ghost?

00:46:16.100 --> 00:46:18.440
Or just a spooky coincidence?

00:46:18.440 --> 00:46:21.220
None of these thoughts even crossed Joe’s
mind.

00:46:21.220 --> 00:46:25.720
He was just grateful for the surprising reminder
of the happiness he’d once had.

00:46:25.720 --> 00:46:28.130
For the next couple hours, things seemed…

00:46:28.130 --> 00:46:29.130
Lighter.

00:46:29.130 --> 00:46:34.570
He went about his evening, checking the photo
every so often and smiling, until eventually

00:46:34.570 --> 00:46:38.730
he found himself in bed, still looking into
the glow of his phone.

00:46:38.730 --> 00:46:40.890
It was such a beautiful little cafe…

00:46:40.890 --> 00:46:42.630
Then, he froze.

00:46:42.630 --> 00:46:44.349
He noticed something in the picture.

00:46:44.349 --> 00:46:49.300
It’d been there the whole time, but only
now was he seeing rather than just looking.

00:46:49.300 --> 00:46:53.490
It was in the corner, staring through the
glass of the cafe’s door.

00:46:53.490 --> 00:46:56.860
So faint he almost wanted to dismiss it as
a trick of the light.

00:46:56.860 --> 00:47:01.559
It was a face - Well, not a face, more like
a skull.

00:47:01.559 --> 00:47:05.260
Not human, not anywhere near human.

00:47:05.260 --> 00:47:11.130
Long, slender, and canine, with protruding
fangs and vacant white eyes.

00:47:11.130 --> 00:47:14.970
The pure white of the skull was buried in
a nest of thick, black hair.

00:47:14.970 --> 00:47:20.240
It looked like it was crouching behind the
door, looking out, and grinning, whatever

00:47:20.240 --> 00:47:22.030
the hell it was.

00:47:22.030 --> 00:47:25.059
Just seeing it changed the entire tone of
the picture.

00:47:25.059 --> 00:47:28.020
It was no longer a simple reminder of bygone
joy.

00:47:28.020 --> 00:47:33.410
Now, all that was radiating out of that image
was a palpable sense of dread.

00:47:33.410 --> 00:47:36.339
Was someone playing some kind of awful prank
on him?

00:47:36.339 --> 00:47:38.961
Just then, he was jogged from his contemplation
by another alert.

00:47:38.961 --> 00:47:42.750
A new message from the same number as before.

00:47:42.750 --> 00:47:47.840
With great hesitation, he hovered his thumb
over the push notification and clicked.

00:47:47.840 --> 00:47:51.090
That’s when everything got a lot worse.

00:47:51.090 --> 00:47:53.079
It was a photo of a bus stop.

00:47:53.079 --> 00:47:59.160
Not just any bus stop, of course, it was Stop
C16 - The one that Joe always took to get

00:47:59.160 --> 00:48:00.160
to work.

00:48:00.160 --> 00:48:04.670
It looked like it was taken relatively early
in the morning, but nobody was there.

00:48:04.670 --> 00:48:05.670
Well…

00:48:05.670 --> 00:48:07.540
Not quite nobody.

00:48:07.540 --> 00:48:09.670
There was that figure again.

00:48:09.670 --> 00:48:14.410
It stood at full height, behind the partially
frosted glass that makes up the back of the

00:48:14.410 --> 00:48:15.410
bus stop.

00:48:15.410 --> 00:48:20.559
That same large, black humanoid shape, with
a white, grinning dog skull where the face

00:48:20.559 --> 00:48:21.559
should be.

00:48:21.559 --> 00:48:26.060
Something about it terrified him on such a
primal level, like the way our lizard brain

00:48:26.060 --> 00:48:28.859
reacts to some ancient apex predator.

00:48:28.859 --> 00:48:33.450
And whatever this thing was, it clearly knew
something about him.

00:48:33.450 --> 00:48:36.520
How else could it stage all these photos?

00:48:36.520 --> 00:48:41.110
Joe got out of bed and looked out the window,
down onto his dark front street.

00:48:41.110 --> 00:48:46.510
Empty, thankfully, but after this surprise
nightmare, he wasn’t going to take any chances.

00:48:46.510 --> 00:48:50.710
He grabbed a kitchen knife from downstairs
and placed it on his bedside cabinet, right

00:48:50.710 --> 00:48:54.190
next to his phone, with 911 on speed dial.

00:48:54.190 --> 00:48:59.020
Joe Lillis, a 43 year old man, slept with
the lights on that night for the first time

00:48:59.020 --> 00:49:01.180
in over thirty years.

00:49:01.180 --> 00:49:04.690
Sadly for him, the nightmare was just beginning.

00:49:04.690 --> 00:49:09.140
The next morning, Joe woke up unharmed, but
he wasn’t pleased to see that he’d gotten

00:49:09.140 --> 00:49:11.640
several more texts in his sleep.

00:49:11.640 --> 00:49:15.619
There was one taken outside of the local insurance
company office where he worked.

00:49:15.619 --> 00:49:19.960
The strange creature with the skull for a
face was looming around the corner, peering

00:49:19.960 --> 00:49:22.370
at the camera with its lipless grin.

00:49:22.370 --> 00:49:24.109
Like it was mocking him.

00:49:24.109 --> 00:49:28.500
Another photo was taken at the local supermarket
where Joe did most of his grocery shopping.

00:49:28.500 --> 00:49:33.790
The frame was centralized on the cereal aisle,
bordered on both sides by walls of garish

00:49:33.790 --> 00:49:35.040
mascots, endlessly repeated.

00:49:35.040 --> 00:49:41.180
Down at the far end of the aisle was a looming,
dark figure, with that cold, canine skull

00:49:41.180 --> 00:49:43.400
where a human face should be.

00:49:43.400 --> 00:49:46.650
There were a few more, but worst of all was
the last one.

00:49:46.650 --> 00:49:49.280
It was taken at the cemetery.

00:49:49.280 --> 00:49:54.740
In the foreground, a headstone, reading “Carol
Lillis - Beloved Wife and Daughter.”

00:49:54.740 --> 00:50:00.130
Joe was horrified to see that skull-faced
beast was rising up behind his wife’s grave,

00:50:00.130 --> 00:50:04.220
long, clawed fingers curling around the top
of the headstone.

00:50:04.220 --> 00:50:08.990
That was the moment that Joe decided to go
to the police about all this, before things

00:50:08.990 --> 00:50:10.530
got even more out of hand.

00:50:10.530 --> 00:50:15.190
He called an Uber to get down to the station
- He certainly didn’t feel like going anywhere

00:50:15.190 --> 00:50:17.590
near his regular bus stop after last night.

00:50:17.590 --> 00:50:22.400
He showed the photos he’d been sent so far
to an officer posted at the station, and they

00:50:22.400 --> 00:50:25.349
agreed that there was certainly something
strange about it.

00:50:25.349 --> 00:50:30.410
While the behavior undeniably bordered on
harassment, it hadn’t yet delved into criminal

00:50:30.410 --> 00:50:34.160
territory, so he would sadly be on his own
until then.

00:50:34.160 --> 00:50:38.609
The best they could do was stay in touch and
keep abreast of any new developments.

00:50:38.609 --> 00:50:43.290
The only sage advice they could give him was
not to delete the photos, as they could always

00:50:43.290 --> 00:50:47.230
be used as evidence in court later if things
escalated.

00:50:47.230 --> 00:50:50.770
This was literally the last result that Joe
wanted out of this.

00:50:50.770 --> 00:50:54.900
Considering how bizarre and threatening things
were getting already, he really didn’t want

00:50:54.900 --> 00:50:57.780
to find out what escalation looked like in
this case.

00:50:57.780 --> 00:51:03.930
But what else could he do but carry on, just
trying to exercise as much caution as he could

00:51:03.930 --> 00:51:06.660
in these strange new circumstances?

00:51:06.660 --> 00:51:10.950
He went to work and tried his best to stay
productive, despite the fact that every three

00:51:10.950 --> 00:51:14.049
or so hours, a new photo would arrive.

00:51:14.049 --> 00:51:18.730
Places that he liked to sit in the local parks,
stores he’d frequent, restaurants he liked

00:51:18.730 --> 00:51:19.730
to eat at.

00:51:19.730 --> 00:51:24.380
That nightmare skeleton dog thing would be
standing in all of them, just mugging for

00:51:24.380 --> 00:51:25.420
the camera.

00:51:25.420 --> 00:51:29.309
On one hand, every time he looked at one of
the photos, Joe felt like he was giving this

00:51:29.309 --> 00:51:31.580
freak exactly what they wanted.

00:51:31.580 --> 00:51:34.950
On the other hand, how could he possibly look
away?

00:51:34.950 --> 00:51:37.880
What if he missed something that could save
his life?

00:51:37.880 --> 00:51:41.240
It carried on much like that until later in
the evening.

00:51:41.240 --> 00:51:45.050
Joe may not have been a genius, but he was
no fool, either.

00:51:45.050 --> 00:51:49.569
He’d seen too many of those seedy True Crime
documentaries about kidnapping to take his

00:51:49.569 --> 00:51:50.910
normal route home.

00:51:50.910 --> 00:51:56.130
He took a real detour, frequently checking
over his shoulder the entire time.

00:51:56.130 --> 00:51:59.470
Much to his relief, he didn’t see anything
out of place.

00:51:59.470 --> 00:52:00.470
Good.

00:52:00.470 --> 00:52:04.180
When he got home, he locked every door and
bolted every window.

00:52:04.180 --> 00:52:06.599
Nothing would be getting the jump on him tonight.

00:52:06.599 --> 00:52:12.130
That’s when the next picture came in: A
photograph of Joe’s empty office cubicle,

00:52:12.130 --> 00:52:15.859
with the bony face of the creature looming
over the divider with a grin.

00:52:15.859 --> 00:52:19.560
He could feel his heart pounding away in his
chest just looking at it.

00:52:19.560 --> 00:52:22.190
How did this thing get around like this?

00:52:22.190 --> 00:52:26.859
How was it able to infiltrate everywhere in
his entire goddamn life?

00:52:26.859 --> 00:52:30.730
Suddenly, he felt a smile spreading across
his face.

00:52:30.730 --> 00:52:33.480
This freak had just messed up, big time.

00:52:33.480 --> 00:52:36.740
Before, all these creepy photos had been taken
in public places.

00:52:36.740 --> 00:52:38.990
But the one taken in his office?

00:52:38.990 --> 00:52:41.869
Oh, this crossed the line into trespassing.

00:52:41.869 --> 00:52:45.000
The police would have to do something about
it now.

00:52:45.000 --> 00:52:47.760
It’d given him an ace up his sleeve.

00:52:47.760 --> 00:52:52.910
That confidence faded a few hours later when
he received another photo: This time, it was

00:52:52.910 --> 00:52:57.490
the skull-faced monster just standing on the
sidewalk - The sidewalk that Joe remembered

00:52:57.490 --> 00:53:00.700
walking on his “covert” alternative route.

00:53:00.700 --> 00:53:03.549
He felt himself break into a cold sweat.

00:53:03.549 --> 00:53:08.140
It seemed, whoever this was, he really did
hold no secrets from them.

00:53:08.140 --> 00:53:12.890
Now more than ever, Joe didn’t feel safe
in his own home.

00:53:12.890 --> 00:53:17.819
So you can only imagine how he felt when,
a few hours later, he received a photo of

00:53:17.819 --> 00:53:24.080
the skull-faced stalker standing right outside
his own front door, staring into the camera.

00:53:24.080 --> 00:53:29.580
It sent him rushing to the window again to
check outside, but of course, nobody was there.

00:53:29.580 --> 00:53:33.430
The next day, when he called the police and
updated them on the situation, they told him

00:53:33.430 --> 00:53:35.579
that they were doing all they could.

00:53:35.579 --> 00:53:39.380
The best thing he could possibly do was to
remain calm, but vigilant.

00:53:39.380 --> 00:53:44.119
He needed to keep an eye on the photos being
sent to him, so he could notify them if ever

00:53:44.119 --> 00:53:46.680
he was in any immediate danger.

00:53:46.680 --> 00:53:49.890
This put poor Joe’s paranoia at a fever
pitch.

00:53:49.890 --> 00:53:55.930
Even when he went to work, surrounded by coworkers,
by witnesses, he could scarcely tear his eyes

00:53:55.930 --> 00:53:57.660
away from his phone.

00:53:57.660 --> 00:54:02.300
He was a slave to the photos, forever waiting
for the next one.

00:54:02.300 --> 00:54:06.670
Only to experience crushing regret when that
photo actually arrived.

00:54:06.670 --> 00:54:09.760
It looked like it was taken moments before
it was sent to him.

00:54:09.760 --> 00:54:16.460
Joe saw himself, looking at his own phone
in his office cubicle, with that huge, skull-faced

00:54:16.460 --> 00:54:18.520
figure looming behind him.

00:54:18.520 --> 00:54:23.579
He screamed out loud upon seeing it, and turned
to see if anything was behind him.

00:54:23.579 --> 00:54:26.030
But of course, there was nothing there.

00:54:26.030 --> 00:54:30.940
The police inspected the office, talked to
potential witnesses, and analyzed the photo.

00:54:30.940 --> 00:54:36.441
It showed no signs of any photographic manipulation,
but there were also no witnesses around the

00:54:36.441 --> 00:54:39.809
office who claimed to see anything strange
that day.

00:54:39.809 --> 00:54:43.809
There was also no security camera footage
in the last several days that showed this

00:54:43.809 --> 00:54:46.309
figure coming in or out.

00:54:46.309 --> 00:54:52.299
Joe Lillis started to feel like he was going
insane, and perhaps he was, but that didn’t

00:54:52.299 --> 00:54:55.890
change the tangible and ever-present feeling
that he was in great danger.

00:54:55.890 --> 00:54:58.210
He didn’t come into work the next day.

00:54:58.210 --> 00:55:04.130
He’d received more photos like that in the
night: Of himself, taken in real time, with

00:55:04.130 --> 00:55:06.260
that skull-faced freak looming.

00:55:06.260 --> 00:55:08.300
He didn’t want to leave the house.

00:55:08.300 --> 00:55:10.270
He didn’t want to go anywhere anymore.

00:55:10.270 --> 00:55:12.319
He just didn’t feel safe out there.

00:55:12.319 --> 00:55:15.040
How could he, with all this madness unfolding?

00:55:15.040 --> 00:55:19.160
There was a time when he could have said something
like, “At least it only seems confined to

00:55:19.160 --> 00:55:23.400
my phone”, he might’ve even suspected
that it had something to do with that strange

00:55:23.400 --> 00:55:27.809
MalO app he downloaded a few days prior that
hadn’t seemed to do anything.

00:55:27.809 --> 00:55:30.510
But the situation had evolved since then.

00:55:30.510 --> 00:55:33.569
He wasn’t just seeing the creature in photos
anymore.

00:55:33.569 --> 00:55:34.569
It was here.

00:55:34.569 --> 00:55:38.190
He kept seeing quick flashes of it on the
other side of windows.

00:55:38.190 --> 00:55:39.360
In reflections.

00:55:39.360 --> 00:55:44.460
In the corner of his eyes, always darting
away if ever he turned towards it.

00:55:44.460 --> 00:55:46.960
It was everywhere and nowhere.

00:55:46.960 --> 00:55:49.260
It was here for him.

00:55:49.260 --> 00:55:50.720
He just knew it.

00:55:50.720 --> 00:55:52.670
The police couldn’t help.

00:55:52.670 --> 00:55:54.119
Nobody could help.

00:55:54.119 --> 00:55:59.309
Joe just sat in the corner of his bedroom,
clutching his kitchen knife, afraid to close

00:55:59.309 --> 00:56:00.309
his eyes.

00:56:00.309 --> 00:56:01.780
It could be anywhere.

00:56:01.780 --> 00:56:02.940
It could be anywhere.

00:56:02.940 --> 00:56:05.309
It could be anywhere…

00:56:05.309 --> 00:56:10.260
We know one thing for sure: Joe Lillis never
felt truly alone ever again.

00:56:10.260 --> 00:56:15.190
He always had his new friend, waiting, just
out of sight.

00:56:15.190 --> 00:56:21.520
And if ever you’re feeling lonesome, and
decide to download Mal0 version 1.0.0 yourself,

00:56:21.520 --> 00:56:24.030
then you’ll never feel lonely again, either…

00:56:24.030 --> 00:56:29.369
If you have ever taken a trip to Suntop Mountain
in the Mount Baker-Snoqualmie National Forest,

00:56:29.369 --> 00:56:35.079
Washington State, then you may have come across
an old wooden structure - The Suntop Fire

00:56:35.079 --> 00:56:36.349
Lookout.

00:56:36.349 --> 00:56:40.930
Built in the early 1930s, the building was
used by the US Forest Service to keep watch

00:56:40.930 --> 00:56:43.180
for any fires in the nearby woodland.

00:56:43.180 --> 00:56:49.750
At one point, Suntop Fire Lookout would have
been manned 365 days a year, complete with

00:56:49.750 --> 00:56:53.099
a bed for staff who were stationed there on
rotation.

00:56:53.099 --> 00:56:57.940
The single story lookout house overlooks the
scenic valleys of the White River and Huckleberry

00:56:57.940 --> 00:57:02.130
Creek, but you’re not here for an informative
tourist guide.

00:57:02.130 --> 00:57:06.569
You probably don’t care about the frankly
fascinating history of the lookout and how

00:57:06.569 --> 00:57:11.880
it was used as part of the Aircraft Warning
Service during World War 2, watching for enemy

00:57:11.880 --> 00:57:12.880
planes.

00:57:12.880 --> 00:57:19.950
No, you’re here because something much darker
lurks inside the Suntop Fire Lookout.

00:57:19.950 --> 00:57:25.220
And even though it appears to be a simple,
one-story-tall wooden structure, it certainly

00:57:25.220 --> 00:57:28.280
is not short on space.

00:57:28.280 --> 00:57:34.230
SCP-3333 refers to an anomaly that the Foundation
discovered inside the Suntop Fire Lookout

00:57:34.230 --> 00:57:35.230
house.

00:57:35.230 --> 00:57:40.310
The building’s interior is a single, square
room, measuring fourteen feet by fourteen

00:57:40.310 --> 00:57:44.430
feet, with large windows on all four sides.

00:57:44.430 --> 00:57:49.230
When standing inside Suntop Fire Lookout,
looking up at the wooden ceiling, one will

00:57:49.230 --> 00:57:51.530
immediately notice a trapdoor.

00:57:51.530 --> 00:57:52.750
No big deal, right?

00:57:52.750 --> 00:57:57.339
A lot of places have a ceiling entrance to
a small crawl space, there is probably nothing

00:57:57.339 --> 00:58:00.890
behind the trapdoor, apart from a dusty, old
attic.

00:58:00.890 --> 00:58:05.880
There’s a latch that maybe once had a padlock
there, but not anymore.

00:58:05.880 --> 00:58:09.260
Opening the trapdoor will reveal a collapsible
ladder.

00:58:09.260 --> 00:58:13.980
Should anyone be brave, or indeed foolish
enough, to begin to climb, then they’ll

00:58:13.980 --> 00:58:19.750
soon find themselves right back where they
started, inside Suntop Fire Lookout.

00:58:19.750 --> 00:58:21.970
Or so it will seem.

00:58:21.970 --> 00:58:26.130
The thing about being in a place like the
Mount Baker-Snoqualmie National Forest that

00:58:26.130 --> 00:58:31.400
surrounds Suntop Fire Lookout is that woodland
areas are teeming with life.

00:58:31.400 --> 00:58:35.819
Not just plants and trees, but birds and other
animals of the forest.

00:58:35.819 --> 00:58:41.069
You can never truly be alone in a setting
like that, there is always life everywhere

00:58:41.069 --> 00:58:42.069
around you.

00:58:42.069 --> 00:58:47.440
So, when you ascend the ladder, and climb
out right back into the Suntop Fire Lookout,

00:58:47.440 --> 00:58:50.599
that is the first, most noticeable difference
you will find.

00:58:50.599 --> 00:58:56.750
It may take a while at first, but the nagging
absence of something usually so abundant in

00:58:56.750 --> 00:58:59.380
a forest will eventually become obvious.

00:58:59.380 --> 00:59:02.380
It’s quiet, far too quiet.

00:59:02.380 --> 00:59:07.260
No birdsong, or the sound of distant calls
from woodland critters.

00:59:07.260 --> 00:59:10.619
Just silence, all around.

00:59:10.619 --> 00:59:15.860
Anyone ascending the ladder will find themselves
in a copy of Suntop Fire Lookout’s interior,

00:59:15.860 --> 00:59:20.040
one story higher than the ground level of
the small wooden building, with the stairs

00:59:20.040 --> 00:59:25.210
leading up to the front door getting taller
each time to reach up to the higher and higher

00:59:25.210 --> 00:59:26.210
building.

00:59:26.210 --> 00:59:31.760
Now, you know the SCP Foundation and the types
of bizarre, inter dimensional anomalies they’re

00:59:31.760 --> 00:59:33.010
used to dealing with.

00:59:33.010 --> 00:59:38.960
Perhaps SCP-3333 is a mirror dimension, or
a plane of existence where sound doesn’t

00:59:38.960 --> 00:59:39.960
travel.

00:59:39.960 --> 00:59:44.210
It certainly seems to be identical to the
Suntop Fire Lookout, save for the lack of

00:59:44.210 --> 00:59:46.400
any organic life outside.

00:59:46.400 --> 00:59:53.240
Of course, it’s what you’ll find living
inside SCP-3333 that you may want to worry

00:59:53.240 --> 00:59:54.440
about.

00:59:54.440 --> 00:59:59.190
Climbing higher, up the next ladder and through
the next trapdoor, every time with the same

00:59:59.190 --> 01:00:00.190
result.

01:00:00.190 --> 01:00:05.089
You appear at another copy of Suntop Fire
Lookout, each one higher up than the last.

01:00:05.089 --> 01:00:10.270
What first seemed to be an innocuous, unassuming
wooden building is now an endless ascension

01:00:10.270 --> 01:00:16.570
up into the heavens, towards the unknown in
silence, without a shred of plant or animal

01:00:16.570 --> 01:00:18.230
life outside.

01:00:18.230 --> 01:00:22.329
As you climb, perhaps you start to think how
much higher these copies go.

01:00:22.329 --> 01:00:26.300
This might even be the biblical Jacob’s
Ladder, connecting Heaven and Earth.

01:00:26.300 --> 01:00:28.260
That would be nice, wouldn’t it?

01:00:28.260 --> 01:00:32.890
If you were gradually climbing your way up
to paradise, it might make it worth the trip.

01:00:32.890 --> 01:00:36.650
But SCP-3333 is nothing that pleasant.

01:00:36.650 --> 01:00:39.700
You wouldn’t be the first to attempt this
long climb.

01:00:39.700 --> 01:00:46.530
When the SCP Foundation first discovered SCP-3333,
a research detail set up an onsite base camp

01:00:46.530 --> 01:00:48.550
to examine this spatial anomaly.

01:00:48.550 --> 01:00:53.910
Their first exploration involved sending a
member of D-class personnel, designated D-4f68a,

01:00:53.910 --> 01:00:56.369
up the ladder.

01:00:56.369 --> 01:01:01.980
His D-number is a hexadecimal code that, when
translated to text, reads ‘Oh’, so we’ll

01:01:01.980 --> 01:01:03.880
call him that for brevity’s sake.

01:01:03.880 --> 01:01:11.980
During the first day’s exploration, Oh was
able to climb 184 iterations of SCP-3333,

01:01:11.980 --> 01:01:15.040
communicating with head researcher Doctor
Williams below.

01:01:15.040 --> 01:01:20.660
On the second day, Oh could see a pair of
figures standing motionless on a nearby ridge,

01:01:20.660 --> 01:01:25.890
but the pair could not be seen by Doctor Williams
and the other researchers at the base camp.

01:01:25.890 --> 01:01:30.609
Both figures disappeared shortly after Oh
spotted them with the camera he had been issued,

01:01:30.609 --> 01:01:35.320
and he felt uneasy, almost certain that he
saw them point at him.

01:01:35.320 --> 01:01:41.980
The next day, at the 345th copy of Suntop
Fire Lookout, Oh’s behavior started to noticeably

01:01:41.980 --> 01:01:42.980
change.

01:01:42.980 --> 01:01:47.510
Previously, he had been anxious about the
long climb, and hadn’t questioned directions

01:01:47.510 --> 01:01:49.390
given to him by Doctor Williams.

01:01:49.390 --> 01:01:55.309
Now, he seemed to speak more casually, resisting
instructions, asking Williams to climb back

01:01:55.309 --> 01:01:58.740
down and even calling her ‘Doc’ instead
of ‘Doctor’.

01:01:58.740 --> 01:02:04.279
Oh also reported seeing writing on the walls,
but there was no evidence of this on his camera.

01:02:04.279 --> 01:02:07.990
It appeared that something had started to
affect him.

01:02:07.990 --> 01:02:14.030
It was when Oh reached level 527 that things
seemed to change more dramatically.

01:02:14.030 --> 01:02:20.560
Rather than SCP-3333 continuing upwards, the
copies of Suntop Fire Lookout no longer had

01:02:20.560 --> 01:02:22.730
a trapdoor or ladder.

01:02:22.730 --> 01:02:27.369
They seemed to be arranged side by side, in
a grid-like pattern.

01:02:27.369 --> 01:02:32.039
Stepping out of the main doorway, Oh remarked
on the lack of sunlight, and a walkway that

01:02:32.039 --> 01:02:37.590
connected directly to the front door of the
next iteration of SCP-3333.

01:02:37.590 --> 01:02:44.130
Oh complained about the lack of natural light,
and again requested to be allowed back down.

01:02:44.130 --> 01:02:49.059
Doctor Williams instructed Oh to use the flashlights
he was provided, but they wouldn’t activate

01:02:49.059 --> 01:02:51.109
and their spare batteries had vanished.

01:02:51.109 --> 01:02:57.140
Oh then noticed a sudden movement, and just
then his microphone and camera feed went dead,

01:02:57.140 --> 01:02:59.380
almost as if someone had turned them off.

01:02:59.380 --> 01:03:05.150
It appeared that SCP-3333 had something else
lurking up there.

01:03:05.150 --> 01:03:10.000
Doctor Williams oversaw the second expedition
into SCP-3333.

01:03:10.000 --> 01:03:15.319
This time members of Mobile Task Force Mod-0,
also known by the codename “Characteristic

01:03:15.319 --> 01:03:17.810
Eigenspaces”, were sent up the ladder.

01:03:17.810 --> 01:03:22.270
Their ascent through the various copies of
Suntop Fire Lookout were not as eventful as

01:03:22.270 --> 01:03:27.380
Oh’s, with no signs of mysterious figures,
or anxious feelings that Oh seemed to feel

01:03:27.380 --> 01:03:28.740
as he climbed.

01:03:28.740 --> 01:03:33.839
When they reached level 527, where the copies
of the lookout stop progressing upwards and

01:03:33.839 --> 01:03:38.619
spread out in a pattern instead, their lights
and equipment all seemed to be in working

01:03:38.619 --> 01:03:39.619
order.

01:03:39.619 --> 01:03:45.299
However, as the MTF team split up, one by
one they encountered some sort of anomaly,

01:03:45.299 --> 01:03:51.310
or an effect of SCP-3333 that caused each
of them to vanish into the dark.

01:03:51.310 --> 01:03:54.829
Either that, or something took them.

01:03:54.829 --> 01:04:00.720
These MTF units reappeared confused, and Mod-5,
the team’s leader, Graham Purcell, issued

01:04:00.720 --> 01:04:06.079
an order to retreat and the entire squad went
back down the ladders for several days until

01:04:06.079 --> 01:04:08.880
they finally reached the base camp again.

01:04:08.880 --> 01:04:14.671
The members of Mod-0 were adamant they did
not wish to climb SCP-3333 again, but Doctor

01:04:14.671 --> 01:04:18.670
Williams was beginning to understand more
of the anomaly’s effects.

01:04:18.670 --> 01:04:24.029
It appeared to cause abrupt changes to people’s
personalities, along with some sort of phenomenon

01:04:24.029 --> 01:04:28.380
that caused things to appear and disappear
the higher one climbed.

01:04:28.380 --> 01:04:33.020
Assuming these were the results of a memetic
effect, Doctor Williams dispatched a ‘counter

01:04:33.020 --> 01:04:35.440
memetics specialist’ for the next expedition.

01:04:35.440 --> 01:04:40.829
This specialist was a blind, deaf, and mute
woman known as Annette or the ‘Nullwalker’,

01:04:40.829 --> 01:04:46.240
who communicated via a signaling system embedded
in her hand, but was otherwise immune to any

01:04:46.240 --> 01:04:48.700
memetic influences.

01:04:48.700 --> 01:04:52.700
Observed by Doctor Williams and Graham Purcell
at base camp, Annette made her way to the

01:04:52.700 --> 01:04:58.970
top of SCP-3333, reporting that she was aware
of someone watching her from outside the copies

01:04:58.970 --> 01:05:01.319
of Suntop Fire Lookout.

01:05:01.319 --> 01:05:06.339
On her body camera, a flicker of motion occurred,
something looking through the windows that

01:05:06.339 --> 01:05:10.160
ducked out of frame when the camera passed
in its direction.

01:05:10.160 --> 01:05:15.839
At the apex of SCP-3333, Annette kept her
flashlight off, but reported that she could

01:05:15.839 --> 01:05:20.250
detect blood, following it to what she assumed
was a body.

01:05:20.250 --> 01:05:24.710
Sounds of movement surrounded her, and as
Annette switched on her flashlight, Williams

01:05:24.710 --> 01:05:27.680
and Purcell saw that it wasn’t a body in
front of her.

01:05:27.680 --> 01:05:34.080
Instead, it was a pile of rotting organs,
decomposing muscles and discarded bones.

01:05:34.080 --> 01:05:41.970
And among the pile was a metal dog tag, that
read ‘MTF Mod-5: Graham Purcell’; the

01:05:41.970 --> 01:05:45.750
same man who was sitting next to Doctor Williams
at base camp.

01:05:45.750 --> 01:05:49.589
Well, the same man on the outside at least.

01:05:49.589 --> 01:05:56.970
The explanation for everything going on inside
SCP-3333, all these strange occurrences and

01:05:56.970 --> 01:06:02.770
disappearances, finally came in a video sent
from Doctor Williams’ cell phone.

01:06:02.770 --> 01:06:07.490
In it, a panicked Williams, covered in blood,
was fleeing from something at the top of the

01:06:07.490 --> 01:06:10.859
recursive stack of SCP-3333.

01:06:10.859 --> 01:06:16.309
There was no memetic effect at the apex of
the Suntop Fire Lookout copies.

01:06:16.309 --> 01:06:21.440
Nothing was causing the people that the Foundation
sent up to act unlike themselves.

01:06:21.440 --> 01:06:24.230
They simply weren’t themselves anymore.

01:06:24.230 --> 01:06:29.210
According to her frantic video, Doctor Williams
had discovered the truth about what else was

01:06:29.210 --> 01:06:32.270
hiding within SCP-3333.

01:06:32.270 --> 01:06:36.400
With just the right amount of vagueness and
intrigue, the research team had been drawn

01:06:36.400 --> 01:06:37.400
in.

01:06:37.400 --> 01:06:42.099
It was as if they’d been lured in by the
lights of an anglerfish, realizing their grim

01:06:42.099 --> 01:06:44.630
fate only too late.

01:06:44.630 --> 01:06:49.480
The D-class ‘Oh’, the MTF team, even Annette
had been replaced.

01:06:49.480 --> 01:06:56.599
An unknown group of entities on the top level
of SCP-3333 had been carefully observing them,

01:06:56.599 --> 01:07:01.670
waiting until they would not be seen to slip
in and switch places.

01:07:01.670 --> 01:07:06.880
These entities had been creating imagined
anomalous effects, like Oh seeing figures

01:07:06.880 --> 01:07:11.960
that weren’t really there, as a way of luring
more bodies further up the stack.

01:07:11.960 --> 01:07:18.630
They wanted the Foundation to keep sending
expeditions into SCP-3333, to keep them coming

01:07:18.630 --> 01:07:19.690
back.

01:07:19.690 --> 01:07:25.000
The mass of organs, musculature, and bones
that Annette had stumbled across, revealing

01:07:25.000 --> 01:07:31.220
the ruse, had once belonged to Graham Purcell,
before he was replaced.

01:07:31.220 --> 01:07:36.400
You see, the entities residing in SCP-3333
weren’t just copying people.

01:07:36.400 --> 01:07:41.619
They weren’t possessing them or mind-controlling
them, or even shape shifting to steal a person’s

01:07:41.619 --> 01:07:42.619
likeness.

01:07:42.619 --> 01:07:44.930
They were taking skin.

01:07:44.930 --> 01:07:50.830
These creatures hollowed out Graham, Oh, Annette
and the MTF team, pulling out their innards

01:07:50.830 --> 01:07:56.380
and crawling their way inside, filling these
fleshy puppets and leaving their internal

01:07:56.380 --> 01:07:58.260
organs to rot.

01:07:58.260 --> 01:08:04.049
These hollowed out people become vessels for
the entities of SCP-3333 to hide in.

01:08:04.049 --> 01:08:12.119
The whole thing had been a trap, intentionally
exploiting human weaknesses, intrigue, unanswered

01:08:12.119 --> 01:08:13.369
questions.

01:08:13.369 --> 01:08:18.310
You know what they say about curiosity, and
these entities used it to bring more potential

01:08:18.310 --> 01:08:21.940
vessels to the top of SCP-3333.

01:08:21.940 --> 01:08:27.040
They pretended to be the people who they had
replaced, imitating them so the Foundation

01:08:27.040 --> 01:08:32.450
would send more personnel to explore the tower,
increasing their supply of skins.

01:08:32.450 --> 01:08:39.790
Graham’s dog tag had revealed the deception,
and Doctor Williams had escaped up SCP-3333.

01:08:39.790 --> 01:08:44.239
The members of the research team that had
already been replaced were hot on her tail,

01:08:44.239 --> 01:08:50.489
determined to catch and hollow her out too,
and by the end of her video, they had succeeded.

01:08:50.489 --> 01:08:55.730
A month later though, a team delivering supplies
realized what had happened and the trapdoor

01:08:55.730 --> 01:08:57.000
was sealed.

01:08:57.000 --> 01:09:01.830
Suntop Fire Lookout was put under permanent
guard, but at least fifty personnel were killed

01:09:01.830 --> 01:09:04.150
or replaced by one of the entities.

01:09:04.150 --> 01:09:09.920
A new Mobile Task Force, Lamda-1 “Maxwell’s
Demons” was created to hunt down and neutralize

01:09:09.920 --> 01:09:15.900
any of the entities that escaped SCP-3333,
but it’s still unknown how many left the

01:09:15.900 --> 01:09:22.150
tower and are still out there somewhere, waiting
to use someone’s curiosity about the strange

01:09:22.150 --> 01:09:24.640
and unknown against them.

01:09:24.640 --> 01:09:30.339
On a cold October night in 2003, Shirley Yeats
of Seattle, Washington, was just about to

01:09:30.339 --> 01:09:33.390
get ready for bed when she heard a knock at
the door.

01:09:33.390 --> 01:09:37.390
She approached the door and asked the person
on the other side to identify themselves.

01:09:37.390 --> 01:09:42.509
The voice outside responded immediately, it
was a salesman who wanted just a few moments

01:09:42.509 --> 01:09:44.380
of Ms. Yeats' time.

01:09:44.380 --> 01:09:49.440
This was odd for two reasons - First, it was
almost 10 o'clock at night, much later than

01:09:49.440 --> 01:09:51.710
is usual for door to door salesman.

01:09:51.710 --> 01:09:55.390
And second, the knock hadn't come from Mrs.
Yeats' front door.

01:09:55.390 --> 01:09:58.520
It was coming from the door to her bathroom.

01:09:58.520 --> 01:10:01.530
Has your home ever been visited by a door-to-door
salesman?

01:10:01.530 --> 01:10:05.560
If you were born in the last forty years,
then your answer to that question is probably

01:10:05.560 --> 01:10:06.560
'no'.

01:10:06.560 --> 01:10:11.239
In the age of online shopping, the idea of
a salesperson going from house to house hawking

01:10:11.239 --> 01:10:16.000
vacuum cleaners or encyclopedia sets feels
like a relic from the past.

01:10:16.000 --> 01:10:20.890
It's highly unlikely you'd ever see one walking
the streets nowadays, and equally unlikely

01:10:20.890 --> 01:10:23.210
that one would knock on your front door.

01:10:23.210 --> 01:10:28.570
However, if you live in Washington State,
you might need to be wary of a certain salesman

01:10:28.570 --> 01:10:31.510
who is still doing the rounds.

01:10:31.510 --> 01:10:38.040
SCP - 1879, also known as the Indoor Salesman
and the Door Man, is a phenomenon that manifests

01:10:38.040 --> 01:10:40.930
randomly in homes throughout Washington.

01:10:40.930 --> 01:10:44.960
Subjects will hear persistent knocking from
the interior doors of their homes, and the

01:10:44.960 --> 01:10:50.010
affected door becomes classified as SCP - 1879
- 1.

01:10:50.010 --> 01:10:54.080
The knocking doesn't stop until the door is
opened, at which point the subject will be

01:10:54.080 --> 01:11:01.970
greeted by SCP - 1879 - 2, a Caucasian man
of indeterminate age, standing around 170

01:11:01.970 --> 01:11:03.469
cm tall.

01:11:03.469 --> 01:11:08.360
The man will claim to be a salesman, and immediately
try to pitch a bizarre product to the subject

01:11:08.360 --> 01:11:10.560
whose home he's just invaded.

01:11:10.560 --> 01:11:15.630
The SCP Foundation was first alerted to the
existence of the Indoor Salesman when they

01:11:15.630 --> 01:11:19.790
intercepted a 911 call coming from the home
of Mrs. Shirley Yeats.

01:11:19.790 --> 01:11:24.480
She had opened the door to her bathroom in
an attempt to get the salesman to stop knocking,

01:11:24.480 --> 01:11:28.100
and once he was in her home, he refused to
leave.

01:11:28.100 --> 01:11:32.969
According to Yeats, he kept disappearing in
and out of random doors in her house.

01:11:32.969 --> 01:11:37.171
Foundation Field Agent Rogers was equipped
with a recording device and sent to investigate

01:11:37.171 --> 01:11:39.690
the case with several other agents.

01:11:39.690 --> 01:11:44.470
When he arrived at the home, he found Mrs.
Yeats inconsolable.

01:11:44.470 --> 01:11:50.350
SCP-1879-2 was still rapidly talking at her,
and strangely enough, the product he was holding

01:11:50.350 --> 01:11:53.780
and trying to sell to her was a border collie
puppy.

01:11:53.780 --> 01:11:58.590
As soon as Agent Rogers entered the room,
the man shifted his attention away from Mrs.

01:11:58.590 --> 01:11:59.590
Yeats and towards him.

01:11:59.590 --> 01:12:03.179
He then started trying to sell the puppy to
Agent Rogers.

01:12:03.179 --> 01:12:07.240
Agent Rogers did not want to purchase this
puppy, but he found that the man spoke so

01:12:07.240 --> 01:12:11.480
quickly and urgently, he couldn't get a word
in edgewise.

01:12:11.480 --> 01:12:16.250
The man was begging Rogers to take the puppy,
practically shoving it in his face, saying

01:12:16.250 --> 01:12:20.560
that he didn’t need any money, and that
the only payment he needed would be 'some

01:12:20.560 --> 01:12:21.850
of your time'.

01:12:21.850 --> 01:12:25.930
Rogers grew so annoyed at being talked over
and interrupted that he ordered the other

01:12:25.930 --> 01:12:28.510
Field Agents to apprehend the Indoor Salesman.

01:12:28.510 --> 01:12:33.989
They did so, but as soon as the agents walked
him out the front door of the house, he disappeared

01:12:33.989 --> 01:12:35.340
without a trace.

01:12:35.340 --> 01:12:41.550
The agents remained in the area to monitor
the situation, and sure enough, SCP-1879-2

01:12:41.550 --> 01:12:46.350
manifested again in Mrs. Yeats' home six hours
later, still trying to trade the puppy for

01:12:46.350 --> 01:12:49.420
no money, just a little of her time.

01:12:49.420 --> 01:12:52.060
12 years to be precise.

01:12:52.060 --> 01:12:56.720
After hours and hours of being worn down by
this supernaturally pushy salesman, Yeats

01:12:56.720 --> 01:13:01.510
relented and agreed to take the puppy… and
immediately disappeared.

01:13:01.510 --> 01:13:05.650
The Indoor Salesman then disappeared himself
through the closest door before he could be

01:13:05.650 --> 01:13:06.880
apprehended again.

01:13:06.880 --> 01:13:12.810
At a loss for what to do, the agents administered
Class-A amnestics to Mrs. Yeats' family and

01:13:12.810 --> 01:13:13.810
left.

01:13:13.810 --> 01:13:19.230
The reason for her disappearance wasn't fully
known until 12 years later in 2015, when she

01:13:19.230 --> 01:13:24.560
reappeared in the same spot she'd disappeared
from, having no concept of how much time had

01:13:24.560 --> 01:13:25.560
passed.

01:13:25.560 --> 01:13:29.910
The puppy really had just cost her 12 years
of her life.

01:13:29.910 --> 01:13:34.270
Stories like that of Shirley Yeats have popped
up all over the state in the years since,

01:13:34.270 --> 01:13:38.190
from Everett to Walla Walla and everywhere
in between.

01:13:38.190 --> 01:13:44.290
Due to the random nature of SCP-1879 events
and the way that the Indoor Salesman can disappear

01:13:44.290 --> 01:13:50.510
instantly in and out of any door in a building,
the SCP Foundation has been unable to capture

01:13:50.510 --> 01:13:51.510
him.

01:13:51.510 --> 01:13:55.900
The best they’ve been able to do is monitor
911 calls from across the state, listening

01:13:55.900 --> 01:14:02.020
for key words that might indicate another
SCP-1879 infestation.

01:14:02.020 --> 01:14:08.040
When such an event is reported, the foundation
deploys Mobile Task Force Rho-4, aka “Shoos

01:14:08.040 --> 01:14:09.040
Salesmen.”

01:14:09.040 --> 01:14:13.550
This task force's entire purpose is to minimize
the amount of harm the Indoor Salesman is

01:14:13.550 --> 01:14:17.550
able to cause by intercepting him before he
can make a sale.

01:14:17.550 --> 01:14:22.710
This is a very important task, as evidenced
by the story of Mrs. Yeats, since while the

01:14:22.710 --> 01:14:28.580
products this salesman sells might be innocent,
he doesn't accept payment in any normal currency.

01:14:28.580 --> 01:14:32.800
The prices he asks for his products are always
bizarre, and often deadly.

01:14:32.800 --> 01:14:37.370
If all someone loses is 12 years of their
life, they could be considered to be getting

01:14:37.370 --> 01:14:38.440
off easy.

01:14:38.440 --> 01:14:43.870
In one instance, the product being sold was
a single red rose, in exchange for the subject's

01:14:43.870 --> 01:14:44.870
heart.

01:14:44.870 --> 01:14:49.340
Once the deal was sealed, the subject dropped
dead on the spot, with an autopsy revealing

01:14:49.340 --> 01:14:54.150
that his heart and circulatory system vanished
from inside his body.

01:14:54.150 --> 01:14:59.560
In another, the Indoor Salesman offered 220
bananas, and told the subject to simply 'give

01:14:59.560 --> 01:15:00.810
him some sugar'.

01:15:00.810 --> 01:15:05.030
The subject agreed, and all candied goods
in the home disappeared.

01:15:05.030 --> 01:15:09.680
In a third, the Indoor Salesman was trying
to sell a thermonuclear warhead, the price

01:15:09.680 --> 01:15:12.080
of which was the subject's soul.

01:15:12.080 --> 01:15:15.719
The subject accepted, and at first, nothing
seemed to have happened.

01:15:15.719 --> 01:15:20.179
The Foundation confiscated the warhead and
placed it into non-anomalous containment.

01:15:20.179 --> 01:15:24.840
Later that day, the subject went to listen
to some music, only to find that two of her

01:15:24.840 --> 01:15:30.730
vinyl records had gone missing - Lady Soul
and Almighty Fire, by world-famous soul singer

01:15:30.730 --> 01:15:32.060
Aretha Franklin.

01:15:32.060 --> 01:15:38.120
So, even though he's incredibly invasive,
annoying, and his transactions can be deadly,

01:15:38.120 --> 01:15:41.360
the Indoor Salesman still maintains a sense
of humor.

01:15:41.360 --> 01:15:45.750
The fact that the Foundation can't capture
the Indoor Salesman means that a lot of questions

01:15:45.750 --> 01:15:48.179
about him remain unanswered.

01:15:48.179 --> 01:15:51.760
The biggest by far is why he does what he
does.

01:15:51.760 --> 01:15:58.830
In most SCP-1879 events, the Indoor Salesman
seems frantic and desperate to make a sale.

01:15:58.830 --> 01:16:03.699
Often he will refer to having quotas and deadlines
to meet, which implies some other, unseen

01:16:03.699 --> 01:16:06.560
entity that he has to answer to.

01:16:06.560 --> 01:16:11.219
These questions remain unanswered, because
all attempts to interrogate the Indoor Salesman

01:16:11.219 --> 01:16:12.889
have been unsuccessful.

01:16:12.889 --> 01:16:17.060
When he manifests in a location, it's impossible
to get him to stray from his sales pitch,

01:16:17.060 --> 01:16:21.900
and he disappears as soon as he successfully
sells his wares.

01:16:21.900 --> 01:16:28.850
However, there was one instance where, after
an SCP-1879 event took place, Foundation agents

01:16:28.850 --> 01:16:34.560
were there to witness a rare interaction between
the Indoor Salesman and his mysterious employers.

01:16:34.560 --> 01:16:39.590
Agent Rogers and the rest of the Shoos Salesmen
were called out to a home in Spokane where

01:16:39.590 --> 01:16:42.840
rapid knocking had begun to emanate from the
bedroom door.

01:16:42.840 --> 01:16:48.000
Equipped with recording devices, Rogers was
able to record the voice of the Indoor Salesman

01:16:48.000 --> 01:16:50.060
coming from inside the bedroom.

01:16:50.060 --> 01:16:54.170
In the recording, the salesman grumbled to
himself about not being able to meet his quota

01:16:54.170 --> 01:16:59.380
by tomorrow, saying that if he didn't, he'd
be stuck in this world for the next century.

01:16:59.380 --> 01:17:03.440
He started knocking again, yelling through
the door that he knew that he knew they were

01:17:03.440 --> 01:17:04.440
home.

01:17:04.440 --> 01:17:07.949
He kept knocking until he was interrupted
by the sound of a phone ringing.

01:17:07.949 --> 01:17:13.270
The Indoor Salesman was heard picking it up,
and Rogers managed to record the conversation.

01:17:13.270 --> 01:17:18.680
The person calling was, apparently, the Indoor
Salesman’s boss, who was calling to complain

01:17:18.680 --> 01:17:20.420
about his performance.

01:17:20.420 --> 01:17:25.060
Only one side of the conversation was heard,
but evidently the Indoor Salesman’s boss

01:17:25.060 --> 01:17:30.179
wasn't too happy about receiving two Aretha
Franklin albums as payment instead of an actual

01:17:30.179 --> 01:17:31.449
human soul.

01:17:31.449 --> 01:17:35.760
The Indoor Salesman apologized for the joke,
then told his boss - “It won't happen again.

01:17:35.760 --> 01:17:38.909
Please don't hurt it, I'll meet the quota
this time, I swear.”

01:17:38.909 --> 01:17:43.090
He hung up, grumbling to himself again, “I
better get to move up to at least Accounting

01:17:43.090 --> 01:17:44.090
this time....

01:17:44.090 --> 01:17:46.159
I've paid my dues and then some.”

01:17:46.159 --> 01:17:50.240
Rogers finally opened the door, to the apparent
disappointment of the Indoor Salesman, who

01:17:50.240 --> 01:17:54.210
was hoping to speak with the home’s owner
and was quite annoyed at having another one

01:17:54.210 --> 01:17:56.550
of his sales interrupted by MTF Rho-4.

01:17:56.550 --> 01:18:01.920
Rogers tried to ask the Indoor Salesman who
he'd just been speaking to on the phone, but

01:18:01.920 --> 01:18:04.690
as usual, the Salesman started talking over
him.

01:18:04.690 --> 01:18:07.190
“Now, see here, let's think logically,”
he said.

01:18:07.190 --> 01:18:09.030
“You know I'm not gonna tell you anything.

01:18:09.030 --> 01:18:11.730
I know you're not likely to buy what I'm selling.

01:18:11.730 --> 01:18:13.600
So let's just move on to greener pastures.

01:18:13.600 --> 01:18:17.090
I'm coming up close to a deadline, and I'm
sure you're swamped with making sure good

01:18:17.090 --> 01:18:20.710
people don't do their jobs, so I'll just be
on my way and let you do that.

01:18:20.710 --> 01:18:21.710
Ciao.”

01:18:21.710 --> 01:18:25.670
The Indoor Salesman tried to close the door,
but Agent Rogers blocked it with his arm.

01:18:25.670 --> 01:18:30.850
He was tired of this SCP giving him the runaround,
and he was going to keep the Indoor Salesman

01:18:30.850 --> 01:18:33.480
here if it was the last thing he did.

01:18:33.480 --> 01:18:38.330
He demanded the entity stay and be interviewed,
and other members of the task force apprehended

01:18:38.330 --> 01:18:41.560
the Salesman, making sure he couldn't leave
the room.

01:18:41.560 --> 01:18:46.909
The Indoor Salesman, now held in place by
several armed men, seemed to finally relent.

01:18:46.909 --> 01:18:49.560
He told Rogers - “I'm busy, so I'll tell
you what.

01:18:49.560 --> 01:18:53.360
I'm going to give you something, no money
out of your pocket, and we'll call it even.

01:18:53.360 --> 01:18:54.360
Sound good?”

01:18:54.360 --> 01:18:58.250
Rogers, just wanting to get this whole thing
over with, agreed to these terms.

01:18:58.250 --> 01:19:03.520
Three seconds later, every agent on the scene
was dead, and the Indoor Salesman was able

01:19:03.520 --> 01:19:08.340
to straighten his tie, pick up his briefcase
and walk through the door to the bathroom.

01:19:08.340 --> 01:19:13.980
When the bodies of Agent Rogers and the rest
of MTF Rho-4 were examined by Foundation scientists,

01:19:13.980 --> 01:19:19.310
the cause of death was found to be, in every
case, thousands of coins suddenly appearing

01:19:19.310 --> 01:19:25.520
in not only their pockets, but also inside
their stomachs, lungs, and even under their

01:19:25.520 --> 01:19:26.520
skin.

01:19:26.520 --> 01:19:30.699
Later that day, the Indoor Salesman was reported
at a home in the same neighborhood.

01:19:30.699 --> 01:19:36.340
He was seen trying to sell the house's owner
- 80-year-old retiree Alan Johnson - a Glock-18

01:19:36.340 --> 01:19:39.290
pistol in exchange for 'his attention.’

01:19:39.290 --> 01:19:44.290
As he had done so many times before, the Indoor
Salesman disappeared through another door

01:19:44.290 --> 01:19:49.620
before the Foundation were able to reach the
scene, and when the SCP arrived, they found

01:19:49.620 --> 01:19:55.730
Mr. Johnson, still alive but now missing his
prefrontal cortex - the part of the brain

01:19:55.730 --> 01:19:57.560
that controls attention.

01:19:57.560 --> 01:20:04.460
It's likely that, because of the nature of
the entity, SCP-1879 might be entirely impossible

01:20:04.460 --> 01:20:05.520
to contain.

01:20:05.520 --> 01:20:09.710
The Foundation might never find out anything
more than what they already know about the

01:20:09.710 --> 01:20:14.770
Indoor Salesman, the way he's able to manifest
behind closed doors, or the reason he has

01:20:14.770 --> 01:20:19.960
to keep filling quotas for an unseen boss
who, apparently, doesn't have a very good

01:20:19.960 --> 01:20:21.350
sense of humor.

01:20:21.350 --> 01:20:27.250
So, if you're ever in Washington state, be
careful who you open your doors to, especially

01:20:27.250 --> 01:20:32.770
if the knocking you hear is coming from inside
your house.

01:20:32.770 --> 01:20:37.440
In a remote part of Russia, a mysterious disease
outbreak was tearing through a tiny farming

01:20:37.440 --> 01:20:40.140
village with terrifying side effects.

01:20:40.140 --> 01:20:45.560
There was no cure, no clue to where it came
from, and worst of all, the disease’s terrifying

01:20:45.560 --> 01:20:47.980
impact didn’t end with death.

01:20:47.980 --> 01:20:54.040
No, it was after those carrying the disease
died, that the real horror started.

01:20:54.040 --> 01:20:58.440
After an agonizing fever that leaves the victims
writhing in pain, they quickly succumb to

01:20:58.440 --> 01:21:03.060
the disease, only to rise from their graves
to wreak havoc on the living.

01:21:03.060 --> 01:21:07.860
The virus continues to spread, until the corpses
outnumber those trying to hide from them,

01:21:07.860 --> 01:21:10.670
as the world spirals into almost certain ruin.

01:21:10.670 --> 01:21:15.320
It sounds like the plot of a zombie movie,
but for the SCP Foundation this is anything

01:21:15.320 --> 01:21:20.120
but fiction, and the terror that unfolded
in that little Siberian town is the first

01:21:20.120 --> 01:21:26.800
recorded encounter with SCP - 610, also known
as, The Flesh That Hates.

01:21:26.800 --> 01:21:29.550
First, livestock began to vanish from farms.

01:21:29.550 --> 01:21:34.790
Theft or wild animals were suspected, but
no suspects could be found, and no mutilated

01:21:34.790 --> 01:21:36.230
remains turned up.

01:21:36.230 --> 01:21:40.600
The animals weren’t being stolen, and they
weren’t being eaten, so…what happened

01:21:40.600 --> 01:21:41.600
to them?

01:21:41.600 --> 01:21:46.070
With no more animals left to lose, the farmers
themselves then began to disappear, but the

01:21:46.070 --> 01:21:49.679
authorities refused to take the missing persons
cases seriously.

01:21:49.679 --> 01:21:54.040
The missing farmers’ families would contact
the police, make a report, and then the whole

01:21:54.040 --> 01:21:55.550
thing was forgotten.

01:21:55.550 --> 01:22:00.050
It was written off just as another unsolved
disappearance, which wasn’t uncommon in

01:22:00.050 --> 01:22:02.270
the wild and unforgiving region.

01:22:02.270 --> 01:22:05.949
Then the police themselves began to disappear.

01:22:05.949 --> 01:22:10.280
The families of the missing farmers would
sometimes report strange sounds from the surrounding

01:22:10.280 --> 01:22:14.690
woods, describing moans and inhuman screeches
of pain.

01:22:14.690 --> 01:22:18.900
One young boy reported seeing a cow with what
he described as “tentacles” lurking around

01:22:18.900 --> 01:22:20.780
the edge of the trees.

01:22:20.780 --> 01:22:24.909
Regional police were dispatched to the location,
and ordered to investigate and report back

01:22:24.909 --> 01:22:27.020
on their findings within 24 hours.

01:22:27.020 --> 01:22:32.960
But the units sent to the area didn’t report
back, and were never heard from again.

01:22:32.960 --> 01:22:37.250
Upon learning of the reports, the Russian
government grew increasingly concerned, fearing

01:22:37.250 --> 01:22:41.219
domestic insurgency or foreign espionage of
some kind could be at play.

01:22:41.219 --> 01:22:47.679
They sent a small team of special agents to
the area, and, one by one, those agents disappeared,

01:22:47.679 --> 01:22:49.440
just like the others before them.

01:22:49.440 --> 01:22:53.630
It seemed no one who went into the village
after the disappearances started ever came

01:22:53.630 --> 01:22:54.940
out again.

01:22:54.940 --> 01:22:57.510
They had all simply vanished.

01:22:57.510 --> 01:23:00.989
Desperate for answers, the Russian government
contacted the only people in the world who

01:23:00.989 --> 01:23:03.370
could help - The SCP Foundation.

01:23:03.370 --> 01:23:07.880
What the Foundation found over the course
of their investigation would shock and unnerve

01:23:07.880 --> 01:23:12.159
them, going beyond anything they had previously
discovered.

01:23:12.159 --> 01:23:16.390
Before the investigation officially began,
the affected area was sealed off by the Russian

01:23:16.390 --> 01:23:17.409
government.

01:23:17.409 --> 01:23:21.960
Not knowing if it would be safe to send researchers
into the containment perimeter, the Foundation

01:23:21.960 --> 01:23:27.000
set up a small camera mounted unit, nicknamed
Herbie, to capture footage of whatever remained

01:23:27.000 --> 01:23:28.090
of the village.

01:23:28.090 --> 01:23:33.139
The images captured by Herbie revealed what
exactly had become of the people in this doomed

01:23:33.139 --> 01:23:37.929
village, and the true, nightmarish nature
of SCP-610.

01:23:37.929 --> 01:23:43.980
SCP-610 is a Keter-class entity, meaning it’s
an anomaly that’s exceedingly difficult

01:23:43.980 --> 01:23:48.790
to contain consistently or reliably, with
containment procedures often being extensive

01:23:48.790 --> 01:23:50.080
and complex.

01:23:50.080 --> 01:23:55.300
610 is a highly contagious skin disease that
initially manifests like an ordinary allergic

01:23:55.300 --> 01:23:59.889
reaction, with symptoms including increased
sensitivity, itching, and a rash.

01:23:59.889 --> 01:24:04.310
But within just three hours of those initial
symptoms appearing, the rash starts to turn

01:24:04.310 --> 01:24:07.790
into masses of scar tissue on the chest and
arms.

01:24:07.790 --> 01:24:12.100
These masses spread over the legs and back
of the victim, and completely consume them

01:24:12.100 --> 01:24:15.989
in thick, rubbery flesh within five hours.

01:24:15.989 --> 01:24:19.350
Once they’re covered, the victim will cease
all vital functions.

01:24:19.350 --> 01:24:24.070
Unfortunately for them, and doubly so for
those around them, they do not stay dead.

01:24:24.070 --> 01:24:28.239
About three minutes after expiring, the victim’s
vitals will restart at a heightened rate,

01:24:28.239 --> 01:24:32.470
and the masses of flesh encasing their body
will begin to move and multiply, mutating

01:24:32.470 --> 01:24:36.960
them into a form beyond anything resembling
the human they once were.

01:24:36.960 --> 01:24:41.510
The specific type of mutation varies from
case to case, but has included the head becoming

01:24:41.510 --> 01:24:47.920
massive and bulbous, the growth of extra limbs,
and, in especially gruesome cases, the victim’s

01:24:47.920 --> 01:24:53.060
body splitting apart to allow extra tendrils
of flesh to sprout from the open wound.

01:24:53.060 --> 01:24:57.199
Occasionally, an infected person will stop
moving and become rooted to the ground in

01:24:57.199 --> 01:24:58.900
a set location.

01:24:58.900 --> 01:25:03.580
Once it is settled, their flesh will spread
itself across the ground, encasing all nearby

01:25:03.580 --> 01:25:05.840
objects in flaps of scar tissue.

01:25:05.840 --> 01:25:10.389
The infected that maintain their mobility
are highly aggressive, even violent, and will

01:25:10.389 --> 01:25:14.449
attempt to infect any living thing that comes
into their line of sight.

01:25:14.449 --> 01:25:18.670
The disease does not only infect humans, and
can take over any living organism within a

01:25:18.670 --> 01:25:20.460
matter of hours.

01:25:20.460 --> 01:25:24.730
Due to the highly contagious and dangerous
nature of the disease, safe observation of

01:25:24.730 --> 01:25:30.200
infected specimens and areas is only possible
with drones and mounted cameras.

01:25:30.200 --> 01:25:34.910
This brings us back to Herbie, the first such
mounted camera to record footage of the infected

01:25:34.910 --> 01:25:35.929
area.

01:25:35.929 --> 01:25:40.739
Herbie was deployed into the infection site,
also known as Site A, without any damage.

01:25:40.739 --> 01:25:45.480
It remained at the outside perimeter of the
village for two hours, observing several infected

01:25:45.480 --> 01:25:50.199
humans, and fire damage to many of the homes,
before following an infected into an intact

01:25:50.199 --> 01:25:51.199
house.

01:25:51.199 --> 01:25:54.810
Herbie’s camera feed captured the infected
person entering the house and sitting down

01:25:54.810 --> 01:25:56.140
at the table inside.

01:25:56.140 --> 01:26:01.440
There were several other infected humans in
the house, and one unidentified infected creature

01:26:01.440 --> 01:26:04.120
that remained immobile under the table.

01:26:04.120 --> 01:26:08.170
After viciously assaulting one of the other
infected humans, the infected returned to

01:26:08.170 --> 01:26:11.550
the table and began to lay out plates on top
of it.

01:26:11.550 --> 01:26:16.790
Pieces of its flesh began to wriggle and tear
away from its body, before settling onto each

01:26:16.790 --> 01:26:17.790
plate.

01:26:17.790 --> 01:26:21.330
Once the plates were filled, the infected
sitting at the table began to grab at the

01:26:21.330 --> 01:26:27.409
flesh and crush it into their mouths, in a
perverse imitation of a normal mealtime gathering.

01:26:27.409 --> 01:26:31.630
After capturing this stomach-churning display,
Herbie left the house and continued to explore

01:26:31.630 --> 01:26:32.630
the village.

01:26:32.630 --> 01:26:36.540
It recorded footage of a large stack of bodies
that seemed to be made up of both Russian

01:26:36.540 --> 01:26:40.590
military and civilians, with an infected sitting
on top.

01:26:40.590 --> 01:26:44.560
As Herbie maneuvered toward the remains of
the town hall, an infected grabbed the rover

01:26:44.560 --> 01:26:45.699
off of the ground.

01:26:45.699 --> 01:26:49.710
Herbie’s camera was able to capture the
face of the infected that grabbed the rover.

01:26:49.710 --> 01:26:55.410
The face was that of a young girl around ten
years old, strangely intact atop a large,

01:26:55.410 --> 01:26:56.739
distorted body.

01:26:56.739 --> 01:27:01.190
The final moments of Herbie’s camera feed
captured the infected girl’s face bursting

01:27:01.190 --> 01:27:05.920
open, revealing tendrils of flesh that pulled
Herbie into the gaping maw.

01:27:05.920 --> 01:27:08.620
Then, the feed cut to black.

01:27:08.620 --> 01:27:13.500
Herbie was regarded as lost, but the video
feed briefly resumed five hours later, showing

01:27:13.500 --> 01:27:16.710
the camera covered with an unidentified slime.

01:27:16.710 --> 01:27:21.760
After this, the video feed was cut for good,
and Herbie abandoned in Site A.

01:27:21.760 --> 01:27:26.280
The Foundation has sent several manned expeditions
into Site A, where many expedition forces

01:27:26.280 --> 01:27:28.730
have fallen victim to the infected.

01:27:28.730 --> 01:27:33.100
Several operatives were also lost in an earthquake
that revealed a network of underground tunnels.

01:27:33.100 --> 01:27:37.340
A manned expedition into these tunnels was
attempted, and the video feed that was captured

01:27:37.340 --> 01:27:40.510
by the researchers on the expedition was deeply
disturbing.

01:27:40.510 --> 01:27:45.770
There were images of an abandoned church filled
with infected, and a mass of uninfected or

01:27:45.770 --> 01:27:48.440
partially infected human captives.

01:27:48.440 --> 01:27:52.630
The final moments of the video feed from this
expedition captured several operatives being

01:27:52.630 --> 01:27:57.920
murdered by an infected human wielding a farming
scythe, indicating that the infected are capable

01:27:57.920 --> 01:28:01.639
of using simple weaponry in addition to brute
force.

01:28:01.639 --> 01:28:06.430
The use of this weapon, paired with the presence
of captives in the underground tunnels, paints

01:28:06.430 --> 01:28:10.980
a terrifying picture of the kind of organization
the infected are capable of.

01:28:10.980 --> 01:28:17.070
No more manned expeditions have been attempted,
or, if they have, they have been highly classified.

01:28:17.070 --> 01:28:21.909
Ordinarily, once a new SCP is discovered,
it is placed in containment at the Foundation,

01:28:21.909 --> 01:28:25.949
with special procedures in place, so that
it can be studied or even neutralized in the

01:28:25.949 --> 01:28:28.480
rare occasions where it’s deemed necessary.

01:28:28.480 --> 01:28:33.460
When it comes to SCP-610 though, containment
might just be impossible.

01:28:33.460 --> 01:28:38.680
It simply covers too much area, and is too
dangerous to expose to human researchers.

01:28:38.680 --> 01:28:43.510
Instead, all infected areas have been isolated
with the permission of the Russian government.

01:28:43.510 --> 01:28:47.470
There is an official perimeter established
around these areas, and any civilians that

01:28:47.470 --> 01:28:51.730
approach them are told to leave under the
pretense of ongoing military operations.

01:28:51.730 --> 01:28:56.440
For once, a top secret military project is
the more innocent answer.

01:28:56.440 --> 01:29:00.480
Armed guards are placed at the perimeter of
every infected area, and any living thing

01:29:00.480 --> 01:29:06.000
with symptoms of SCP-610 spotted near the
perimeter is to be immobilized, killed, and

01:29:06.000 --> 01:29:08.550
burned from as far away as possible.

01:29:08.550 --> 01:29:13.119
Any living thing that comes in contact with
SCP-610, whether a soldier, a scientist, or

01:29:13.119 --> 01:29:19.110
a civilian, is immediately terminated, and
their remains destroyed.

01:29:19.110 --> 01:29:23.080
If someone comes within three meters of an
infected organism, they will be quarantined

01:29:23.080 --> 01:29:26.510
and remotely examined to determine if they
have been infected.

01:29:26.510 --> 01:29:31.639
While the spread of SCP-610 can be airborne,
it has been determined to be far less contagious

01:29:31.639 --> 01:29:35.880
when spread through air particles as opposed
to physical contact.

01:29:35.880 --> 01:29:40.909
The infection sites remain active to this
day, like modern day leper colonies.

01:29:40.909 --> 01:29:45.060
Though they are isolated from the general
population, and the military is doing everything

01:29:45.060 --> 01:29:51.110
in their power to contain the infected, SCP-610
is still very much alive.

01:29:51.110 --> 01:29:56.190
It is rare for an entity to exist that the
Foundation cannot truly contain, but can only

01:29:56.190 --> 01:30:01.310
try to guard against, and that makes this
infection all the more terrifying.

01:30:01.310 --> 01:30:06.070
Who knows how much it has mutated over the
years, growing, spreading, hungry for new

01:30:06.070 --> 01:30:07.070
hosts?

01:30:07.070 --> 01:30:11.590
There is still so much that the Foundation
does not know about the Flesh That Hates,

01:30:11.590 --> 01:30:16.650
such as how it works, what it can do, or even
where it came from, since the origin of the

01:30:16.650 --> 01:30:20.650
first infection is still, at this point, entirely
unknown.

01:30:20.650 --> 01:30:26.090
It has shown itself to be capable of learning,
planning, and protecting itself, so who is

01:30:26.090 --> 01:30:30.010
to say that it couldn’t figure out a way
to escape from its isolated area?

01:30:30.010 --> 01:30:35.830
It is so highly contagious, and spreads so
quickly, that just one tiny, infected rabbit,

01:30:35.830 --> 01:30:41.780
and one inattentive soldier, could be enough
for SCP-610 to reach the general population.

01:30:41.780 --> 01:30:48.960
If it did, its violent, destructive nature
and hatred for all life would mean that everything,

01:30:48.960 --> 01:30:55.560
not just the people but animals, plants, and
the world itself, could be at risk.

01:30:55.560 --> 01:30:57.940
And no one is ready for this kind of infection.

01:30:57.940 --> 01:31:03.890
A disease that turns the human body against
itself, turns our skin into a weapon and a

01:31:03.890 --> 01:31:09.260
tomb, stripping away identity, humanity, and
everything that isn’t made of that same

01:31:09.260 --> 01:31:10.409
hateful flesh.

01:31:10.409 --> 01:31:16.350
So, let’s hope that the perimeter holds,
and, the next time you feel a little itchy,

01:31:16.350 --> 01:31:19.389
try not to think about what might happen next.

01:31:19.389 --> 01:31:20.389
Addiction.

01:31:20.389 --> 01:31:26.010
It takes many forms and wears many faces,
like a demon walking among us.

01:31:26.010 --> 01:31:31.219
It takes over your life - crawling in and
changing you from the inside out.

01:31:31.219 --> 01:31:37.150
Breaking an addiction is hard, but oftentimes
not giving it up is much harder.

01:31:37.150 --> 01:31:42.870
That was a difficult lesson to learn for three
people: Joey Walker, Dolly McGregor, and Paul

01:31:42.870 --> 01:31:44.239
Ables.

01:31:44.239 --> 01:31:49.570
These three had never met one another, and
now, they never will, but each of them had

01:31:49.570 --> 01:31:51.929
two things in common.

01:31:51.929 --> 01:31:56.120
First was that they each had an addiction
they felt like they couldn’t shake, and

01:31:56.120 --> 01:32:00.810
the second was that they each had a run-in
with SCP-666.

01:32:00.810 --> 01:32:04.130
Joey Walker was at the end of his rope when
he encountered it.

01:32:04.130 --> 01:32:09.460
Everyone has bad days, but for Joey, every
day for the last fifteen years has been a

01:32:09.460 --> 01:32:10.560
bad day.

01:32:10.560 --> 01:32:15.890
He was pushing 40 with nothing to show for
it, except credit card debt, a scraggly beard,

01:32:15.890 --> 01:32:17.650
and a beat-up old Mustang.

01:32:17.650 --> 01:32:20.050
But booze had always been there for him.

01:32:20.050 --> 01:32:25.239
No matter how bad things got, he could always
count on a glass full of comfort at the end

01:32:25.239 --> 01:32:26.330
of the day.

01:32:26.330 --> 01:32:31.760
But to paraphrase a quote by Stephen King,
“Sometimes, when a man takes a drink, the

01:32:31.760 --> 01:32:33.350
drink takes the man.”

01:32:33.350 --> 01:32:36.630
And Joey Walker had been long since taken.

01:32:36.630 --> 01:32:41.980
He was a transient worker, doing jobs wherever
jobs needed doing, but he never expected that

01:32:41.980 --> 01:32:45.900
he would end up all the way to Tibet working
construction.

01:32:45.900 --> 01:32:50.040
Not that he was complaining - Sure, it was
cold, but there was plenty of Tibetan Chang

01:32:50.040 --> 01:32:51.260
to enjoy.

01:32:51.260 --> 01:32:57.139
It was a drink so good that legends even say
that Yetis would raid villages in the mountains

01:32:57.139 --> 01:32:59.210
to get a little taste.

01:32:59.210 --> 01:33:03.699
Joey had taken a liking to the Chang, and
it was what he had been drinking when he crashed

01:33:03.699 --> 01:33:07.590
his car up in the mountains, leaving him stranded
in the snow.

01:33:07.590 --> 01:33:12.690
Joey had survived the crash itself, but he
knew he wouldn’t last long in the cold.

01:33:12.690 --> 01:33:13.790
He needed shelter.

01:33:13.790 --> 01:33:17.760
That’s why he felt like he could hardly
believe his luck when he first saw the Yurt

01:33:17.760 --> 01:33:21.880
- a kind of traditional, Tibetan tent made
from animal skins.

01:33:21.880 --> 01:33:26.969
Joey had never seen anything quite like it,
but any refuge from the storm would do.

01:33:26.969 --> 01:33:30.390
He pushed forward through the snow and climbed
inside.

01:33:30.390 --> 01:33:32.910
But the inside of the Yurt was nothing like
the outside.

01:33:32.910 --> 01:33:39.150
In fact, it seemed like an exact replica of
his favorite sports bar back in Atlantic City.

01:33:39.150 --> 01:33:44.180
It was warm, there was all the old memorabilia
on the walls, and every screen was showing

01:33:44.180 --> 01:33:48.780
the Saints wiping the floor with the Colts
in the 2010 Superbowl.

01:33:48.780 --> 01:33:50.380
Joey didn’t even question it.

01:33:50.380 --> 01:33:52.710
He just smiled, and approached the bar.

01:33:52.710 --> 01:33:57.560
He even recognized the bartender - Malcolm,
a good old friend of his.

01:33:57.560 --> 01:34:02.280
Malcolm smiled back at him, but there was
something oddly menacing in his grin.

01:34:02.280 --> 01:34:03.429
“Welcome back,” he said.

01:34:03.429 --> 01:34:06.230
“I thought you’d hauled your sorry keister
off to Tibet.

01:34:06.230 --> 01:34:10.489
Guess you gave up on that too, just like everything
else.

01:34:10.489 --> 01:34:12.679
Well, except…”

01:34:12.679 --> 01:34:16.620
Malcolm pushed a glass of beer towards him
across the bar, and glared.

01:34:16.620 --> 01:34:21.630
Joey didn’t understand why Malcolm was being
so aggressive, but he didn’t question that,

01:34:21.630 --> 01:34:22.630
either.

01:34:22.630 --> 01:34:26.550
He grabbed the glass and drank up, guzzling
it down before slamming the empty glass down

01:34:26.550 --> 01:34:27.620
on the bar.

01:34:27.620 --> 01:34:31.820
Malcolm kept the drinks coming, round after
round after round, and Joey kept knocking

01:34:31.820 --> 01:34:32.889
them back.

01:34:32.889 --> 01:34:35.530
He didn’t notice when the TV screens turned
to static.

01:34:35.530 --> 01:34:40.280
He didn’t notice when the other patrons
at the bar began to jitter and twitch, turning,

01:34:40.280 --> 01:34:43.280
little by little, into something less than
human.

01:34:43.280 --> 01:34:48.330
He didn’t even notice when Malcolm’s face
started melting off his skull, as long as

01:34:48.330 --> 01:34:49.909
he kept pouring.

01:34:49.909 --> 01:34:54.900
Before he could even really understand what
was happening to him, Joey Walker was dead.

01:34:54.900 --> 01:34:57.220
His liver and kidneys had given out on him.

01:34:57.220 --> 01:35:01.949
His corpse would later be found, frozen on
the Tibetan mountainside, just thirty feet

01:35:01.949 --> 01:35:04.100
away from his crashed car.

01:35:04.100 --> 01:35:07.530
The coroner’s report would list his cause
of death as, “Accidental.”

01:35:07.530 --> 01:35:09.410
But this was no accident.

01:35:09.410 --> 01:35:16.330
He’d fallen victim to SCP-666, an anomalous
Yurt known to some as the Spirit House.

01:35:16.330 --> 01:35:22.800
The being he’d called Malcolm is known to
the Foundation as SCP-666-1, and Malcolm had

01:35:22.800 --> 01:35:25.010
failed its challenge.

01:35:25.010 --> 01:35:30.300
Sadly for our inebriated friend, the penalty
for failure is death.

01:35:30.300 --> 01:35:36.090
Next on our list of human tragedies comes
Dolly McGregor, a 62-year-old woman from Anaheim,

01:35:36.090 --> 01:35:37.090
California.

01:35:37.090 --> 01:35:42.730
Dolly was never averse to the drink, but she
knew how to enjoy her Mojitos in moderation.

01:35:42.730 --> 01:35:47.760
You rarely get to 62 if you don’t, and Dolly
could tell people with pride that she had

01:35:47.760 --> 01:35:53.000
two children, and six grandchildren, whom
she didn’t see nearly often enough for her

01:35:53.000 --> 01:35:54.000
liking.

01:35:54.000 --> 01:36:00.590
She also had over $100,000 in gambling debt
owed to a number of Casinos on the Vegas Strip.

01:36:00.590 --> 01:36:05.060
Ever since her husband, Albert, had passed
away several years prior, shooting craps,

01:36:05.060 --> 01:36:09.710
playing blackjack, and whiling away the hours
in front of the slot machines had been a welcome

01:36:09.710 --> 01:36:11.710
change from loneliness.

01:36:11.710 --> 01:36:17.840
But in Vegas, fortunes can change in an instant
- Dolly had gone from being on a hot winning

01:36:17.840 --> 01:36:19.980
streak to losing everything.

01:36:19.980 --> 01:36:24.400
The casinos extended her lines of credit until
she was gambling with money she’d never

01:36:24.400 --> 01:36:27.750
be able to pay back, but that didn’t stop
her.

01:36:27.750 --> 01:36:32.340
She’d been selling off everything, even
remortgaging the house that Albert had built

01:36:32.340 --> 01:36:36.410
with his own two hands to try and keep up
with her ballooning debts.

01:36:36.410 --> 01:36:40.080
Still, it wasn’t enough, but she couldn’t
stop, either.

01:36:40.080 --> 01:36:44.400
It wasn’t even that she felt good about
it anymore, it was just that she only ever

01:36:44.400 --> 01:36:49.739
felt normal among the flashing lights of slot
machines and the clatter of dice.

01:36:49.739 --> 01:36:53.550
She needed to get away; as far away as possible.

01:36:53.550 --> 01:36:57.670
She’d heard about people reaching spiritual
enlightenment in Tibet.

01:36:57.670 --> 01:37:03.639
They’d discovered God, or Gods, or sometimes
just a sense of inner peace.

01:37:03.639 --> 01:37:07.480
Whatever it was, she needed to find it and
to get this demon off her back.

01:37:07.480 --> 01:37:11.710
So she took the last of her savings and flew
off to Tibet to clear her head.

01:37:11.710 --> 01:37:15.800
She didn’t know if there were any casinos
in Lhasa, but if there were, her money would

01:37:15.800 --> 01:37:17.420
surely be no good there.

01:37:17.420 --> 01:37:20.280
It was exactly what she needed.

01:37:20.280 --> 01:37:23.320
But Tibet wasn’t the promised land she thought
it would be.

01:37:23.320 --> 01:37:28.780
Wherever Dolly went, there she was, with the
same vices and demons chasing her.

01:37:28.780 --> 01:37:33.420
The first night she spent in Lhasa, she used
the hotel wifi to download an online poker

01:37:33.420 --> 01:37:34.840
app on her phone.

01:37:34.840 --> 01:37:39.380
This culminated in another couple thousand
dollars lost, and a panic attack that caused

01:37:39.380 --> 01:37:44.409
Dolly to throw her phone into her toilet before
wandering off into the wilderness.

01:37:44.409 --> 01:37:46.560
She just needed to get away.

01:37:46.560 --> 01:37:51.520
But time and space got away from her, and
eventually, she was knee deep in the snow.

01:37:51.520 --> 01:37:53.000
Where had she come from?

01:37:53.000 --> 01:37:54.150
Where could she go?

01:37:54.150 --> 01:37:58.949
It quickly dawned on her that, if she didn’t
find some kind of shelter soon, she’d be

01:37:58.949 --> 01:37:59.949
done for.

01:37:59.949 --> 01:38:01.989
But all she could do was keep walking…

01:38:01.989 --> 01:38:06.119
That’s when she happened upon SCP-666.

01:38:06.119 --> 01:38:09.590
The Yurt was like an oasis on the barren mountainside.

01:38:09.590 --> 01:38:13.840
She didn’t expect comfort inside, but it
could at least provide her some shelter until

01:38:13.840 --> 01:38:16.650
the staff back at the hotel noticed she was
gone.

01:38:16.650 --> 01:38:19.369
Then they’d come and save her, right?

01:38:19.369 --> 01:38:20.369
Right?

01:38:20.369 --> 01:38:25.590
But when she passed through the yak-leather
flap into the Yurt, Dolly wasn’t in an ancient

01:38:25.590 --> 01:38:30.219
tent in the Tibetan wilderness, she was on
a casino floor.

01:38:30.219 --> 01:38:35.550
There was a big, beautiful roulette table
before her, attended to by a grinning, well-dressed

01:38:35.550 --> 01:38:36.550
croupier.

01:38:36.550 --> 01:38:41.250
They were flanked by an army of slot machines,
and all the pleasing, familiar sounds of cheerful

01:38:41.250 --> 01:38:43.369
gambling rang out through the air.

01:38:43.369 --> 01:38:47.710
She approached the table, and the croupier
shook his head in what seemed like disappointment.

01:38:47.710 --> 01:38:51.200
“Back again, eh, Dolly?” he said with
a sigh.

01:38:51.200 --> 01:38:53.500
“Of course, I should have expected it.

01:38:53.500 --> 01:38:57.550
After all, what else do you have in that empty
little life of yours, hmm?

01:38:57.550 --> 01:39:00.540
Without all this, you’d be nothing, right?

01:39:00.540 --> 01:39:01.710
Nothing at all.

01:39:01.710 --> 01:39:05.630
Since Albert died and the kids want nothing
to do with you, we’re all you’ve got.

01:39:05.630 --> 01:39:08.599
So, Dolly, what’ll it be - Red or black?

01:39:08.599 --> 01:39:10.440
Are you feeling lucky?”

01:39:10.440 --> 01:39:14.350
His words wounded Dolly, but that wouldn’t
stop her.

01:39:14.350 --> 01:39:17.440
She grabbed her chips, and put them all on
red.

01:39:17.440 --> 01:39:19.480
One last spin couldn’t hurt.

01:39:19.480 --> 01:39:21.290
What did she have to lose?

01:39:21.290 --> 01:39:24.760
She blinked, and she wasn’t sitting at the
table anymore.

01:39:24.760 --> 01:39:27.219
She was upright, but she wasn’t standing.

01:39:27.219 --> 01:39:34.060
Her wrists and ankles were bound to something
- to a wheel, a giant roulette wheel, like

01:39:34.060 --> 01:39:37.260
it was some medieval torture device.

01:39:37.260 --> 01:39:39.570
The croupier was standing across from her.

01:39:39.570 --> 01:39:42.500
Well, something that used to be a croupier.

01:39:42.500 --> 01:39:48.619
His face was flickering in and out; sometimes
it was human, sometimes it was a mess of eyes

01:39:48.619 --> 01:39:49.619
and teeth.

01:39:49.619 --> 01:39:54.130
More demons were sitting at all the slot machines
behind him, pulling levers made from human

01:39:54.130 --> 01:39:55.130
bones.

01:39:55.130 --> 01:39:58.230
“Good choice, Dolly,” the croupier said.

01:39:58.230 --> 01:39:59.349
“Red suits you.”

01:39:59.349 --> 01:40:01.510
He reached out and gave the wheel a spin.

01:40:01.510 --> 01:40:07.150
Dolly was lost in an overwhelming, pulsing
cascade of lights, colors, and sounds.

01:40:07.150 --> 01:40:12.130
The horrific, tinny noises of slot machines
and the laughter of the demonic croupier.

01:40:12.130 --> 01:40:17.880
She was lost in panic and terror as she just
kept spinning, and spinning, and spinning…

01:40:17.880 --> 01:40:23.260
When her body was eventually found, her muscles
were in the advanced stages of atrophy, as

01:40:23.260 --> 01:40:25.620
though she hadn’t been moving for years.

01:40:25.620 --> 01:40:30.770
Her brain was rotted, and the cause of death
was determined as sudden cardiac arrest after

01:40:30.770 --> 01:40:34.580
an extended period of sleep-deprivation and
malnutrition.

01:40:34.580 --> 01:40:38.780
Dolly’s family would never really know what
happened to her.

01:40:38.780 --> 01:40:45.320
The SCP Foundation had learned a lot about
SCP-666 after containing it in Site 73.

01:40:45.320 --> 01:40:50.830
Its anomalous effects namely, vivid, complex,
and potentially fatal hallucinatory experiences

01:40:50.830 --> 01:40:55.300
only affect those with some kind of addiction
or dependency.

01:40:55.300 --> 01:40:59.250
To anyone else entering the Yurt, it’s just
a normal tent.

01:40:59.250 --> 01:41:04.000
But any addicts who enter will fall under
its spell, and are generally transported back

01:41:04.000 --> 01:41:07.550
to the place they were when their addiction
was at its strongest.

01:41:07.550 --> 01:41:14.120
There, they’ll encounter SCP-666-1, an entity
that takes the form of a figure from the subject’s

01:41:14.120 --> 01:41:18.920
life - normally one heavily involved in facilitating
their addiction.

01:41:18.920 --> 01:41:25.190
Any kind of addiction seems to trigger it
- alcohol, drugs, gambling, pornography, food,

01:41:25.190 --> 01:41:28.890
self-destructive behavior, even video games.

01:41:28.890 --> 01:41:34.810
SCP-666 kills its victims with a twisted mockery
of the very thing they were dependent on in

01:41:34.810 --> 01:41:35.810
life.

01:41:35.810 --> 01:41:40.340
It was only with Paul Ables that the Foundation
started discovering the other side of the

01:41:40.340 --> 01:41:41.340
coin.

01:41:41.340 --> 01:41:45.730
By almost all accounts, Paul is a worse person
than anyone on this list.

01:41:45.730 --> 01:41:50.369
He got addicted to hard drugs early on in
life, and took up a life of violent crime

01:41:50.369 --> 01:41:51.980
to support his habit.

01:41:51.980 --> 01:41:56.730
He murdered two people during a liquor store
robbery, before being convicted and sentenced

01:41:56.730 --> 01:41:57.730
to death.

01:41:57.730 --> 01:42:02.790
He’d then been picked up as a D-Class by
the SCP Foundation, and selected as a test

01:42:02.790 --> 01:42:06.940
subject for SCP-666 due to his history of
drug abuse.

01:42:06.940 --> 01:42:11.520
The Foundation expected to be adding his body
to the incineration pile sometime soon.

01:42:11.520 --> 01:42:16.670
None of the researchers working on the case
predicted what actually ended up happening.

01:42:16.670 --> 01:42:19.110
Paul was forced to enter the Yurt.

01:42:19.110 --> 01:42:23.950
Not long after, he found himself standing
in a place he’d done everything to try to

01:42:23.950 --> 01:42:29.210
forget: The dark, graffiti-stained alley where
he’d been sold his first hit.

01:42:29.210 --> 01:42:30.860
This was the place.

01:42:30.860 --> 01:42:33.920
The place that destroyed his life.

01:42:33.920 --> 01:42:37.750
Every bad decision he’d ever made could
be traced back to here.

01:42:37.750 --> 01:42:40.630
And specifically to one man…

01:42:40.630 --> 01:42:41.730
Frank.

01:42:41.730 --> 01:42:48.380
Frank was his first dealer, and how here he
was, standing right across from him once more.

01:42:48.380 --> 01:42:49.820
Frank was grinning like a demon.

01:42:49.820 --> 01:42:51.680
“C’mon, Paulie,” he said.

01:42:51.680 --> 01:42:52.860
“You’re gutter trash.

01:42:52.860 --> 01:42:54.820
We both know what you’re going to do.

01:42:54.820 --> 01:42:55.920
Don’t you feel it?

01:42:55.920 --> 01:42:57.150
The itch?

01:42:57.150 --> 01:42:59.869
One more hit, Paulie, that’s all you need
to feel better.

01:42:59.869 --> 01:43:02.560
It’s time to take your medicine…”

01:43:02.560 --> 01:43:05.630
Frank - or this thing, pretending to be Frank
- was right.

01:43:05.630 --> 01:43:07.310
He did feel the itch.

01:43:07.310 --> 01:43:08.760
He did want it.

01:43:08.760 --> 01:43:10.360
Maybe he was no better than this.

01:43:10.360 --> 01:43:14.699
He began to reach out towards Frank, but then
he abruptly pulled his hand back.

01:43:14.699 --> 01:43:19.760
Frank’s eyes widened in genuine surprise,
as Paul replied, “I’m sorry.

01:43:19.760 --> 01:43:22.460
That’s not me anymore.”

01:43:22.460 --> 01:43:28.110
SCP-666-1 gave a smile, and said, “Maybe
it isn’t, Paulie, maybe it isn’t…”

01:43:28.110 --> 01:43:34.219
When Paul Ables was removed from the SCP-666
Yurt by one of the attending guards, the Foundation

01:43:34.219 --> 01:43:36.580
researchers discovered something amazing.

01:43:36.580 --> 01:43:42.659
Paul was very much alive, and more incredibly,
he didn’t feel the cravings anymore.

01:43:42.659 --> 01:43:44.909
His addiction was gone.

01:43:44.909 --> 01:43:49.349
And further tests showed that Paul wasn’t
a one-off event.In fact, anyone who denies

01:43:49.349 --> 01:43:56.300
the temptation of SCP-666 will see their addictions
miraculously disappear when they finally leave.

01:43:56.300 --> 01:44:01.210
After this it became clear to the Foundation
that SCP-666 isn’t just a way to punish

01:44:01.210 --> 01:44:04.200
addicts, it’s a kind of test.

01:44:04.200 --> 01:44:08.100
Those who want to change, who are willing
to truly confront their demons and resist

01:44:08.100 --> 01:44:13.580
the pull of temptation are rewarded with the
one thing they want most in life, freedom

01:44:13.580 --> 01:44:15.770
from their addiction.

01:44:15.770 --> 01:44:20.330
SCP-666 can be your doom or your salvation.

01:44:20.330 --> 01:44:24.630
And like most things in life, you get what
you give.

01:44:24.630 --> 01:44:30.510
In almost all respects, Kevin O’Reilly is
your average 50-something Irish Man.

01:44:30.510 --> 01:44:35.750
He lives in County Cork with his wife, Martha
where he spends his days working at a local

01:44:35.750 --> 01:44:42.230
accountancy firm, and during his free evenings,
he likes to take quiet walks through the nearby

01:44:42.230 --> 01:44:43.230
woods.

01:44:43.230 --> 01:44:48.080
There’s only one remarkable thing that can
be said about Kevin: He was the second human

01:44:48.080 --> 01:44:54.850
ever to encounter an example of SCP-3199,
a dangerous Keter-Class anomaly that has the

01:44:54.850 --> 01:45:00.210
power to knock humanity off the top of the
food chain if left unchecked.

01:45:00.210 --> 01:45:03.139
We know what you’re thinking: What about
the first human?

01:45:03.139 --> 01:45:09.800
Don’t worry, we’ll get to him, but we
can assure you: He’s anything but unremarkable.

01:45:09.800 --> 01:45:10.800
Back to Kevin.

01:45:10.800 --> 01:45:15.560
He was enjoying one of his nightly walks when
he heard a horrible shrieking sound in the

01:45:15.560 --> 01:45:16.560
distance.

01:45:16.560 --> 01:45:21.010
It sounded like a woman was being murdered
and just hearing it chilled poor Kevin to

01:45:21.010 --> 01:45:22.110
his core.

01:45:22.110 --> 01:45:27.230
His first instinct was to run to the woman’s
aid and do whatever he could, but there was

01:45:27.230 --> 01:45:30.260
a lurking anxiety under the surface.

01:45:30.260 --> 01:45:34.830
The echoing memory of an old childhood legend:
The Banshee.

01:45:34.830 --> 01:45:40.340
A monstrous, ghostly woman of Irish folklore,
whose blood-curdling screams always foretell

01:45:40.340 --> 01:45:41.619
death.

01:45:41.619 --> 01:45:44.400
But those were all just stories, surely?

01:45:44.400 --> 01:45:48.650
Grim omens to stop children from straying
too far from the path.

01:45:48.650 --> 01:45:53.770
Kevin took his first brave step in the direction
of that awful screaming, repeating the quiet

01:45:53.770 --> 01:45:59.740
mantra of “There’s no such thing as monsters”
to himself again and again.

01:45:59.740 --> 01:46:03.860
If only he knew just how wrong he was.

01:46:03.860 --> 01:46:08.120
He ran deeper into the forest, following the
awful sounds.

01:46:08.120 --> 01:46:13.030
Whoever this woman was, she certainly had
some pipes on her - the screaming had been

01:46:13.030 --> 01:46:19.080
going on for minutes on end now, and it didn’t
seem to show any signs of subsiding.

01:46:19.080 --> 01:46:23.630
The sky above had darkened from evening to
full on night by the time Kevin reached the

01:46:23.630 --> 01:46:25.530
source of the screaming.

01:46:25.530 --> 01:46:30.770
Kevin found himself in a clearing in the forest,
but in all his years of walking down here,

01:46:30.770 --> 01:46:32.960
he’d never seen it before.

01:46:32.960 --> 01:46:39.120
There was a ramshackle old cottage, rotten
with age and damp, and next to it, a rusty

01:46:39.120 --> 01:46:41.969
old hut made from corrugated iron.

01:46:41.969 --> 01:46:44.370
Like a kind of oversized chicken coop.

01:46:44.370 --> 01:46:49.690
From the tinny, echoing quality of the screams,
he knew that they were coming from inside

01:46:49.690 --> 01:46:50.690
the hut.

01:46:50.690 --> 01:46:53.020
Was a woman being held captive here?

01:46:53.020 --> 01:46:54.960
Kevin was a smart man.

01:46:54.960 --> 01:46:58.730
He approached the tin hut quietly, not saying
a word.

01:46:58.730 --> 01:47:04.270
If this woman had indeed been captured and
was now being held against her will, it wouldn’t

01:47:04.270 --> 01:47:08.440
help the situation to potentially alert her
captor to his presence.

01:47:08.440 --> 01:47:13.540
This quick thinking is the reason that Kevin
O’Reilly is still alive today.

01:47:13.540 --> 01:47:18.800
Because, when he arrived outside the tin hut
and peered in through the window, what he

01:47:18.800 --> 01:47:21.310
saw inside was not a woman.

01:47:21.310 --> 01:47:24.800
In fact, it wasn’t even human.

01:47:24.800 --> 01:47:29.440
The beast that Kevin saw inside the hut was
nothing short of a crime against nature.

01:47:29.440 --> 01:47:33.760
A twisted abomination that was only vaguely
humanoid.

01:47:33.760 --> 01:47:39.250
Its bloated, fleshy body, dripped with some
kind of viscous fluid, and it looked more

01:47:39.250 --> 01:47:42.460
like a plucked, rotten chicken than a person.

01:47:42.460 --> 01:47:47.469
The creature was shrieking and wailing, its
huge body convulsing in the coop.

01:47:47.469 --> 01:47:52.730
It was making a gurgling, gagging noise, like
something was strangling it.

01:47:52.730 --> 01:47:55.500
Kevin felt like he was going to be sick.

01:47:55.500 --> 01:47:56.781
But the monster beat him to it.

01:47:56.781 --> 01:48:02.850
It doubled over, its wretched, lipless mouth
stretching open to freakish proportions, and

01:48:02.850 --> 01:48:04.780
started to vomit something out.

01:48:04.780 --> 01:48:10.670
It was a gray, leathery mass, covered in dark
red blood, that soon flopped out onto the

01:48:10.670 --> 01:48:14.810
ground, among a number of other masses that
looked just like it.

01:48:14.810 --> 01:48:20.000
The creature then gave one final wail, and
spewed out a red stream of blood and bile

01:48:20.000 --> 01:48:21.430
onto the masses.

01:48:21.430 --> 01:48:25.710
That’s when Kevin realized what he was looking
at: Eggs.

01:48:25.710 --> 01:48:29.739
A pile of big, unnatural eggs.

01:48:29.739 --> 01:48:34.820
The foul-smelling bile that the creature had
just vomited up had no effect on the eggs,

01:48:34.820 --> 01:48:38.620
but it seemed to burn and corrode the surrounding
environment.

01:48:38.620 --> 01:48:43.449
It hissed against the metal as thin wisps
of steam rose from the scorch marks.

01:48:43.449 --> 01:48:49.090
Kevin was horrified but also entranced by
the bizarre sight - until the creature stood

01:48:49.090 --> 01:48:52.710
back up, and began to turn towards him.

01:48:52.710 --> 01:48:55.909
Kevin didn’t let his morbid curiosity get
the better of him.

01:48:55.909 --> 01:49:00.820
He turned and sprinted out of the forest,
knowing that if he lingered for even a second

01:49:00.820 --> 01:49:03.690
longer, he wouldn’t return home alive.

01:49:03.690 --> 01:49:09.900
He ran and ran, and finally heard the wailing
fade into the distance behind him.

01:49:09.900 --> 01:49:17.280
This was the first ever outside brush with
a specimen of SCP-3199, also known as “Humans,

01:49:17.280 --> 01:49:18.280
Refuted.”

01:49:18.280 --> 01:49:23.860
Sadly, it would be far from the last, and
would remain one of the rare few that wasn’t

01:49:23.860 --> 01:49:24.860
deadly.

01:49:24.860 --> 01:49:28.630
When Kevin got back to town he immediately
told everyone what he saw.

01:49:28.630 --> 01:49:32.020
There’s a monster in the woods, and it’s
breeding!

01:49:32.020 --> 01:49:37.960
He even told the local newspaper, which printed
the headline, “BEAST SIGHTED IN LOCAL FOREST.”

01:49:37.960 --> 01:49:41.440
It was enough to get the SCP Foundation’s
attention.

01:49:41.440 --> 01:49:45.650
Field Agents were sent to the town proper
to suppress the information leaking about

01:49:45.650 --> 01:49:50.520
the creature and gather any additional information
they needed to assess whether they were dealing

01:49:50.520 --> 01:49:54.760
with a real anomaly here, or just another
crank.

01:49:54.760 --> 01:49:59.070
Straight away though, the agents could tell
from Kevin’s demeanor that he’d seen something

01:49:59.070 --> 01:50:00.380
truly awful.

01:50:00.380 --> 01:50:05.760
He was given amnestics, and Mobile Task Force
Omega-19 were dispatched to secure and contain

01:50:05.760 --> 01:50:08.170
the creatures that Kevin had seen.

01:50:08.170 --> 01:50:13.070
They had twelve well-armed personnel, trained
and prepared to deal with anything.

01:50:13.070 --> 01:50:15.150
Or so they thought.

01:50:15.150 --> 01:50:19.980
They were led by Corporal Duncan, a seasoned
MTF operative, and they used state of the

01:50:19.980 --> 01:50:24.610
art night vision technology to gain a tactical
advantage in the dead of night.

01:50:24.610 --> 01:50:29.750
All they had to work on though was the visual
description provided by Mr. O’Reilly.

01:50:29.750 --> 01:50:33.710
It didn’t take long for them to find the
same clearing out in the woods.

01:50:33.710 --> 01:50:38.880
There was the rotten old cottage and the metal
“coop”, just like Kevin had described.

01:50:38.880 --> 01:50:43.940
Two younger MTF members, Private MacLeod and
Private Langley, were eager to take the lead

01:50:43.940 --> 01:50:48.590
and prove themselves as they explored the
dilapidated nightmare of a house.

01:50:48.590 --> 01:50:53.770
Once inside, they heard strange noises, what
they assumed must have been footsteps coming

01:50:53.770 --> 01:50:55.570
from deeper in the home.

01:50:55.570 --> 01:51:01.800
They crept further in, and that’s when Private
Macleod first noticed it: The shape of a large,

01:51:01.800 --> 01:51:07.460
pale, bulbous figure at the end of a long
hallway, shivering slightly in the cold.

01:51:07.460 --> 01:51:11.429
Compared to some of the hardened killers he’d
heard about in combat training, this creature

01:51:11.429 --> 01:51:13.530
looked like a piece of cake.

01:51:13.530 --> 01:51:17.860
This half-man, half-chicken - it was almost
a walking joke.

01:51:17.860 --> 01:51:21.560
He leveled his weapon and grinned as he approached
the creature.

01:51:21.560 --> 01:51:27.260
But Private Macleod had made a fatal mistake:
He underestimated his enemy.

01:51:27.260 --> 01:51:32.210
In a later Foundation debriefing interview,
Corporal Duncan would report with a dull horror

01:51:32.210 --> 01:51:35.940
what he saw happen to Private Macleod that
terrible day.

01:51:35.940 --> 01:51:41.869
He’d never seen a smile fade from someone’s
face so fast, as the creature turned, shrieked,

01:51:41.869 --> 01:51:45.179
and sprinted down the hallway towards Private
Macleod.

01:51:45.179 --> 01:51:50.310
The poor Private barely even had time to raise
his gun, his hands quivering with panic.

01:51:50.310 --> 01:51:55.130
Though even if Macleod had been quicker on
the draw, it probably wouldn’t have saved

01:51:55.130 --> 01:51:56.130
him.

01:51:56.130 --> 01:52:00.670
As the beast approached, it spewed its foul,
stinking red bile out onto Macleod’s face.

01:52:00.670 --> 01:52:06.150
It was a sudden burning sensation so powerful
that he passed out in an instant, his lower

01:52:06.150 --> 01:52:08.980
face dripping off of his own skull.

01:52:08.980 --> 01:52:11.210
He was dead in mere moments.

01:52:11.210 --> 01:52:16.270
Then, the beast leapt forwards and began attacking
Private Langley, biting and striking and spewing

01:52:16.270 --> 01:52:18.840
more of its deadly acidic liquid.

01:52:18.840 --> 01:52:24.320
By the time it was done, there was barely
any of Langley left to retrieve from the house.

01:52:24.320 --> 01:52:28.670
The ten surviving task force members opened
fire on the creature, but along with being

01:52:28.670 --> 01:52:33.159
surprisingly fast it could also apparently
take quite a licking.

01:52:33.159 --> 01:52:37.420
Even when Corporal Duncan managed a direct
hit on the creature’s chest, blowing a portion

01:52:37.420 --> 01:52:43.230
of it away, the monster just let out the most
awful scream and continued fighting.

01:52:43.230 --> 01:52:48.520
Corporal Duncan admits that, to this day,
that scream, and the moonlight shining through

01:52:48.520 --> 01:52:52.330
the hole in the creature’s chest continue
to haunt him.

01:52:52.330 --> 01:52:57.280
When the monster was finally subdued, they
were able to take it back to the nearby evac

01:52:57.280 --> 01:53:01.550
chopper and begin the journey to the nearest
containment facility.

01:53:01.550 --> 01:53:05.610
But things took another terrible turn during
that fateful flight.

01:53:05.610 --> 01:53:12.659
The creature’s body began to convulse, before
vomiting out a pair of large, leathery eggs.

01:53:12.659 --> 01:53:17.470
Without a moment’s hesitation, the eggs
began to bulge and tear open, and a pair of

01:53:17.470 --> 01:53:23.840
rapidly-growing SCP-3199 instances crawled
out, attacking the mobile task force members

01:53:23.840 --> 01:53:27.810
huddled together in the cramped confines of
the helicopter.

01:53:27.810 --> 01:53:33.060
Once the second onslaught was over, only four
of the remaining ten members of personnel

01:53:33.060 --> 01:53:34.470
were left alive.

01:53:34.470 --> 01:53:37.739
The Foundation had discovered a formidable
new foe.

01:53:37.739 --> 01:53:42.760
The specimens were brought back to Site-114,
and placed in a modified version of the standard

01:53:42.760 --> 01:53:44.940
Keter-Class containment chamber.

01:53:44.940 --> 01:53:50.150
It was fitted with acid-resistant steel walls,
and a series of transparent resin blocks to

01:53:50.150 --> 01:53:54.040
store the specimens inside for constant observation.

01:53:54.040 --> 01:53:58.880
But the creatures weren’t given Keter Class
for nothing: Escape attempts are frequent,

01:53:58.880 --> 01:54:03.430
and whenever they happen, the numbers of creatures
in containment increases.

01:54:03.430 --> 01:54:08.250
The most frightening detail of SCP-3199 is
the fact that it’s impossible to reduce

01:54:08.250 --> 01:54:10.800
the number of them in existence.

01:54:10.800 --> 01:54:16.600
Each creature has a unique, stomach-like organ
inside its body which holds an egg in reserve.

01:54:16.600 --> 01:54:21.699
While it’s possible to destroy one of the
creatures, the eggs have proven to be almost

01:54:21.699 --> 01:54:23.409
indestructible.

01:54:23.409 --> 01:54:29.190
As a result, when one of them dies, the egg
within it hatches and immediately grows into

01:54:29.190 --> 01:54:30.619
a replacement.

01:54:30.619 --> 01:54:36.290
And if the creatures are ever allowed to roam
free, they begin laying eggs in any unoccupied

01:54:36.290 --> 01:54:40.349
space they can find, causing their numbers
to grow.

01:54:40.349 --> 01:54:46.250
In theory, if left unchecked, they could supplant
the human race with their own species in hardly

01:54:46.250 --> 01:54:48.020
any time at all.

01:54:48.020 --> 01:54:53.040
The only solution that the Foundation has
found is submerging the creatures in sedative-laced

01:54:53.040 --> 01:54:59.130
water, as the beasts seem to inherently register
water-filled areas as “occupied space”,

01:54:59.130 --> 01:55:02.889
and therefore do not begin laying eggs while
submerged.

01:55:02.889 --> 01:55:07.740
But even the Foundation’s most optimistic
minds still admit this is only a temporary

01:55:07.740 --> 01:55:09.040
solution.

01:55:09.040 --> 01:55:12.159
But where did these awful creatures come from?

01:55:12.159 --> 01:55:16.520
After the chaos of the first mission, the
Foundation had dispatched an additional Mobile

01:55:16.520 --> 01:55:22.660
Task Force, Surface Team Delta-029-E, to perform
a second sweep of the house and figure out

01:55:22.660 --> 01:55:26.890
what had been going on during the two decades
of proceeding silence.

01:55:26.890 --> 01:55:31.840
Inside, the team managed to collect a number
of strange objects to bring back as evidence

01:55:31.840 --> 01:55:35.110
of the peculiar activities that had taken
place there

01:55:35.110 --> 01:55:40.440
Among these were a number of chicken carcasses
that bore evidence of surgical dissection,

01:55:40.440 --> 01:55:46.770
a pair of chicken feather quills, and an A5
hard-cover notebook labeled “NEW BREED MANIFESTO.”

01:55:46.770 --> 01:55:53.040
Its writer is believed to be deceased, most
likely as a result of SCP-3199, but the final

01:55:53.040 --> 01:55:59.500
note scrawled inside the book and dated 1973
provides some insight into what had occurred

01:55:59.500 --> 01:56:02.500
inside that dilapidated shack in Ireland.

01:56:02.500 --> 01:56:06.599
It reads:
“If you're reading this, then lucky, lucky

01:56:06.599 --> 01:56:07.599
you!

01:56:07.599 --> 01:56:13.400
400,000 hour from now and it'll be warm
and wet and warm, and the wonderful vursatilli

01:56:13.400 --> 01:56:19.000
vessa versatility of (INFERIOR) human DNA
will birth a better era.

01:56:19.000 --> 01:56:20.000
A stronger era.

01:56:20.000 --> 01:56:26.650
One where [ILLEGIBLE] and food and water will
be nothing but things of the passed as we

01:56:26.650 --> 01:56:32.449
make and make and make more until until
I REALLY HAVEN'T MUCH TIME

01:56:32.449 --> 01:56:36.460
TIME
THATS why i ENVY you so so so much.

01:56:36.460 --> 01:56:39.360
you'll have all the time you need.

01:56:39.360 --> 01:56:44.810
time will be a thing of the time will be on
and on and death will be life.

01:56:44.810 --> 01:56:46.880
life new life needs things to live.

01:56:46.880 --> 01:56:50.020
new life will be a part of life from now on.”

01:56:50.020 --> 01:56:57.230
These are the last words of the deranged mad
scientist who created SCP-3199, perhaps under

01:56:57.230 --> 01:57:02.420
the demented belief that somehow, they’d
make the world a better place.

01:57:02.420 --> 01:57:08.810
Personally, we don’t think SCP-3199 have
any interest in improving the world, but whether

01:57:08.810 --> 01:57:14.980
we like it or not, their insane creator is
right about one thing: They’re our problem

01:57:14.980 --> 01:57:16.340
now.

01:57:16.340 --> 01:57:22.150
Agent Carla Mendoza was one of the best field
agents that Site 41 had ever seen.

01:57:22.150 --> 01:57:26.929
She was professional, cool under pressure,
and when the situation demanded it, she could

01:57:26.929 --> 01:57:29.300
be a straight-up badass.

01:57:29.300 --> 01:57:34.010
During a Chaos Insurgency raid on the Site,
she’d single handedly killed four different

01:57:34.010 --> 01:57:38.210
insurgents - the last one with her bare hands.

01:57:38.210 --> 01:57:42.840
During containment breaches, she’d always
be the first one charging into the fray, her

01:57:42.840 --> 01:57:46.400
Foundation standard-issue Beretta drawn and
ready to fire.

01:57:46.400 --> 01:57:50.719
Agent Mendoza was so devoted to the job that
she took up the Site Director’s offer to

01:57:50.719 --> 01:57:56.900
start living onsite, so she could always be
there to help if an emergency situation unfolded.

01:57:56.900 --> 01:58:02.340
After all, when it all hits the fan, you want
someone as utterly unshakeable as Agent Mendoza

01:58:02.340 --> 01:58:03.550
on your side.

01:58:03.550 --> 01:58:08.270
The job had thrown the worst of the worst
at her, and she’d never even flinched.

01:58:08.270 --> 01:58:12.190
So surely, nothing could scare Agent Mendoza,
right?

01:58:12.190 --> 01:58:13.199
Right?

01:58:13.199 --> 01:58:17.570
After a long day of kicking ass, taking names,
and filling in the properly mandated amount

01:58:17.570 --> 01:58:24.000
of SCP Foundation debriefing paperwork, Agent
Mendoza retired to her Site 41 quarters.

01:58:24.000 --> 01:58:29.060
She felt exhausted and sweaty, so before heading
to bed to watch some wonderful SCP Explained

01:58:29.060 --> 01:58:33.619
videos on her phone, she decided to take a
quick shower.

01:58:33.619 --> 01:58:40.720
The last thing she expected was for this particular
shower to become...well, let’s say “Hitchcockian.”

01:58:40.720 --> 01:58:45.500
The water was running, hot and clean, filling
the air with steam.

01:58:45.500 --> 01:58:50.460
Agent Mendoza was lathering up her hair when
she first heard the noise: Heavy, wheezing

01:58:50.460 --> 01:58:54.250
breaths coming from just behind the shower
curtain.

01:58:54.250 --> 01:58:59.230
The second she heard it, Agent Mendoza felt
a kind of brutal, crushing anxiety that she’d

01:58:59.230 --> 01:59:01.440
never experienced before.

01:59:01.440 --> 01:59:06.090
Like a hand was reaching into her chest, and
squeezing her heart.

01:59:06.090 --> 01:59:10.360
The self-defense training that’d been encoded
into her muscle memory over years of working

01:59:10.360 --> 01:59:12.670
at the Foundation kicked into effect.

01:59:12.670 --> 01:59:17.860
In a blind panic, she struck out at the shower
curtain, causing it to sway outwards - and

01:59:17.860 --> 01:59:21.920
land directly on the face of Mendoza’s wheezing
voyeur.

01:59:21.920 --> 01:59:28.020
Who or whatever it was, it was standing right
there, less than a meter away from the shower.

01:59:28.020 --> 01:59:32.210
That wheezing carved into Mendoza’s ears
like a butcher’s knife.

01:59:32.210 --> 01:59:34.980
What an awful, monstrous sound.

01:59:34.980 --> 01:59:39.659
And despite the fact that the shower curtain
obscured its face, she could still somehow

01:59:39.659 --> 01:59:44.990
see it, the way a defenseless animal can sense
an approaching predator without ever locking

01:59:44.990 --> 01:59:50.710
eyes on it - and just somehow know that it’s
too late for them to escape now.

01:59:50.710 --> 01:59:55.760
Every training session, every achievement,
every piece of battle-hardening experience

01:59:55.760 --> 02:00:00.130
- it all evaporated in the presence of that
thing.

02:00:00.130 --> 02:00:03.880
Mendoza was so terrified, she might as well
have been a child.

02:00:03.880 --> 02:00:09.449
The monster just stood there beyond the curtain,
its raw, fleshy face parted into a freakishly

02:00:09.449 --> 02:00:10.910
wide, yellow-toothed grin.

02:00:10.910 --> 02:00:16.580
She didn’t know how, but on some deep, primal
level, she was aware that if this thing got

02:00:16.580 --> 02:00:21.500
its hands on her, something horrific beyond
description would happen to her.

02:00:21.500 --> 02:00:25.730
She was too terrified to even move a muscle
in its presence.

02:00:25.730 --> 02:00:30.670
She remained like that, standing in the shower
and sobbing quietly, for the next three solid

02:00:30.670 --> 02:00:34.130
hours until the creature finally disappeared.

02:00:34.130 --> 02:00:38.440
When her colleagues found her, she’d experienced
moderate scalding wounds from the hot water

02:00:38.440 --> 02:00:39.600
of the shower.

02:00:39.600 --> 02:00:44.480
It took another several hours for Agent Mendoza
to compose herself enough to share her story.

02:00:44.480 --> 02:00:49.380
A couple of days later, Tim Ellis, a junior-level
filing clerk, was found trapped in a Site

02:00:49.380 --> 02:00:50.780
41 supply closet.

02:00:50.780 --> 02:00:56.590
He’d urinated in his Foundation-issue slacks,
and was in a state of borderline catatonia.

02:00:56.590 --> 02:01:01.710
When his superiors asked him why he’d been
spending two hours in a supply closet on company

02:01:01.710 --> 02:01:05.940
time, he reported that it was because a monster
had appeared outside the door when he was

02:01:05.940 --> 02:01:08.770
searching for a replacement stapler.

02:01:08.770 --> 02:01:13.570
Despite never actually opening the door to
see what was outside or call for help - Mr.

02:01:13.570 --> 02:01:17.750
Ellis said that he felt as though he would
have had a heart attack if he actually opened

02:01:17.750 --> 02:01:21.900
that accursed door - he was able to provide
a clear description of the monster.

02:01:21.900 --> 02:01:28.450
He said it was tall and emaciated, with reddish-brown
skin that made it seem almost burnt or rotten.

02:01:28.450 --> 02:01:33.800
While it stood there and waited beyond the
supply closet door, it let out the most awful

02:01:33.800 --> 02:01:38.210
wheezing noise, like an old, rusty Iron Lung.

02:01:38.210 --> 02:01:44.900
But the image that Ellis seemed most fixated
on was the monster’s face, or lack thereof:

02:01:44.900 --> 02:01:50.820
Just a huge, grinning mouth that covered up
its entire head, stocked with an arsenal of

02:01:50.820 --> 02:01:52.000
massive, yellow teeth.

02:01:52.000 --> 02:01:55.120
Ellis was visibly shivering as he talked about
it.

02:01:55.120 --> 02:02:01.530
Two incidents are an unpleasant coincidence,
but three are a bonafide pattern, and it didn’t

02:02:01.530 --> 02:02:07.170
take long for more sightings of this strange
new anomaly - dubbed SCP-303, or The Doorman

02:02:07.170 --> 02:02:09.600
- to pop up across the site.

02:02:09.600 --> 02:02:14.750
It earned that name by always appearing behind
some kind of doorway, or at least a movable

02:02:14.750 --> 02:02:18.380
divider, in the case of Agent Mendoza’s
shower curtain.

02:02:18.380 --> 02:02:23.070
Whenever it appeared outside a doorway, nearby
Foundation personnel would report being struck

02:02:23.070 --> 02:02:28.639
with a sudden paralyzing terror that made
engaging with the creature impossible.

02:02:28.639 --> 02:02:32.630
Attempts to call for help were also often
stifled, as the very presence of the Doorman

02:02:32.630 --> 02:02:35.579
causes disruptions to electrical equipment.

02:02:35.579 --> 02:02:40.370
Whenever The Doorman manifests in your proximity,
it’s safe to say that it’ll be commanding

02:02:40.370 --> 02:02:43.500
your absolute, undivided attention.

02:02:43.500 --> 02:02:48.210
This was a particularly frightening case for
the SCP Foundation because it was one of the

02:02:48.210 --> 02:02:52.150
few anomalies bringing the fight directly
to them.

02:02:52.150 --> 02:02:57.590
Most sentient anomalous beings would do anything
to avoid getting captured by the SCP Foundation

02:02:57.590 --> 02:03:02.400
and contained in one of their high-security
sites, full of experienced researchers and

02:03:02.400 --> 02:03:06.840
state-of-the-art equipment designed specifically
to neutralize their effects.

02:03:06.840 --> 02:03:12.250
The Doorman, however, just seemed to take
this as a challenge, turning even the most

02:03:12.250 --> 02:03:16.460
hardcore personnel on the site into gibbering
wrecks with its mere presence.

02:03:16.460 --> 02:03:20.670
But The Doorman was just getting started.

02:03:20.670 --> 02:03:23.420
Agent Henderson had a frightening encounter
in the break room.

02:03:23.420 --> 02:03:27.719
He was pulling a long shift, and just wanted
to grab some coffee creamer from the cabinet.

02:03:27.719 --> 02:03:32.610
However, as he approached the cabinet, he
heard the telltale wheezing, and that terrible,

02:03:32.610 --> 02:03:35.360
overwhelming terror set in once more.

02:03:35.360 --> 02:03:41.480
The Doorman was sitting inside the cabinet
in the fetal position, he just knew it.

02:03:41.480 --> 02:03:46.670
Could this thing really just appear anywhere
it pleased, and keep people in or out until

02:03:46.670 --> 02:03:50.110
it decided to dematerialize and torment somebody
else?

02:03:50.110 --> 02:03:54.670
When the creature finally dematerialized and
the cabinet was examined, the coffee creamer

02:03:54.670 --> 02:03:59.179
was found to be missing, leaving Agent Henderson
distraught.

02:03:59.179 --> 02:04:03.840
This was the first recorded instance of The
Doorman stealing a physical item, but it would

02:04:03.840 --> 02:04:05.869
be far from the last.

02:04:05.869 --> 02:04:09.890
Henderson wondered whether the creature that’d
just humiliated him was sitting somewhere

02:04:09.890 --> 02:04:16.130
else now, sipping from a warm cup of joe with
its big, freakish mouth and laughing at him.

02:04:16.130 --> 02:04:22.139
But a few incidents after this, things would
become considerably more serious: The Doorman

02:04:22.139 --> 02:04:24.570
was about to take its first life.

02:04:24.570 --> 02:04:29.150
Well, it isn’t really that simple, if you
want to get into the semantics of the thing.

02:04:29.150 --> 02:04:33.900
When the body of Dr. Barker was found inside
the 2nd-floor storage room after a spree of

02:04:33.900 --> 02:04:39.210
SCP-303 incidents, the question was naturally
posed as to whether The Doorman had gotten

02:04:39.210 --> 02:04:43.750
more dangerous and finally directly attacked
one of its victims.

02:04:43.750 --> 02:04:44.750
Not quite.

02:04:44.750 --> 02:04:49.670
There had only been one way in and out of
the storage room: A secured decompression

02:04:49.670 --> 02:04:55.020
chamber, and the Doorman had appeared inside
this chamber while Dr. Barker was in the storage

02:04:55.020 --> 02:05:00.570
room, effectively trapping him inside with
the sheer terror it causes in its victims.

02:05:00.570 --> 02:05:05.190
He was trapped in the room for a grand total
of five days, at which point he finally died

02:05:05.190 --> 02:05:09.920
of dehydration, and the Doorman demanifested
shortly afterward.

02:05:09.920 --> 02:05:15.110
The staff of Site 41 scaled up their countermeasure
efforts, hoping to discover more about and

02:05:15.110 --> 02:05:18.610
perhaps even trap and contain the infamous
Doorman.

02:05:18.610 --> 02:05:24.920
Dr. Burroughs, Researcher Matthews, four members
of security personnel, and four D-Class operatives

02:05:24.920 --> 02:05:30.190
formed a kind of strike team, ready for quick
dispatches whenever The Doorman happened to

02:05:30.190 --> 02:05:31.260
manifest.

02:05:31.260 --> 02:05:35.380
It wasn’t long before the creature appeared
in a room on the first floor, but the team

02:05:35.380 --> 02:05:40.260
quickly intercepted its location, ready and
eager to gather more data on the mysterious

02:05:40.260 --> 02:05:43.060
being that’d been terrorizing all of them
for weeks.

02:05:43.060 --> 02:05:47.900
Dr. Burroughs ordered one of the D-Classes
to open the door and look inside, but the

02:05:47.900 --> 02:05:49.820
D-Class refused out of fear.

02:05:49.820 --> 02:05:53.760
The doctor told him that if he didn’t open
the door, he’d be transferred to SCP-682

02:05:53.760 --> 02:05:54.760
duty.

02:05:54.760 --> 02:05:58.520
The D-Class frantically shook his head and
said, “I’d rather take my chances with

02:05:58.520 --> 02:06:00.150
the reptile than go in there.”

02:06:00.150 --> 02:06:02.020
The doctor was getting frustrated.

02:06:02.020 --> 02:06:06.030
He told the D-Class that if he didn’t open
the door immediately, he’d be terminated

02:06:06.030 --> 02:06:08.000
right there on the spot.

02:06:08.000 --> 02:06:12.239
The D-Class still refused, saying that he’d
take death over what the Doorman would do

02:06:12.239 --> 02:06:14.820
to him if he stepped inside.

02:06:14.820 --> 02:06:18.829
Without hesitation, Dr. Burroughs ordered
one of the security officers to shoot the

02:06:18.829 --> 02:06:20.239
D-Class then and there.

02:06:20.239 --> 02:06:21.800
The shot was fired.

02:06:21.800 --> 02:06:23.660
The D-Class was terminated.

02:06:23.660 --> 02:06:28.119
Dr. Burroughs then ordered a female D-Class
who’d just witnessed this callous execution

02:06:28.119 --> 02:06:32.120
to open the door, or the same abrupt death
would befall her.

02:06:32.120 --> 02:06:36.560
She still refused, then began to describe
the awful things she believed The Doorman

02:06:36.560 --> 02:06:39.420
would do to her if she went inside.

02:06:39.420 --> 02:06:42.230
Researcher Matthews was visibly shaken by
the descriptions.

02:06:42.230 --> 02:06:46.150
Dr. Burroughs decided not to terminate this
D-Class immediately.

02:06:46.150 --> 02:06:50.770
He instead wanted to see just how much pressure
the Doorman’s anomalous fear-based resistance

02:06:50.770 --> 02:06:52.849
mechanisms could take.

02:06:52.849 --> 02:06:57.380
Another D-Class was given a combat knife and
also given the order to cut the female D-Class

02:06:57.380 --> 02:07:00.890
with it every time she refused an order to
go inside.

02:07:00.890 --> 02:07:05.530
After two hours of repeated asking from Dr.
Burroughs, the female D-Class dropped dead

02:07:05.530 --> 02:07:06.650
from blood loss.

02:07:06.650 --> 02:07:10.679
At no point did she ever attempt to open the
door.

02:07:10.679 --> 02:07:16.010
It seemed that, in all cases for those in
the thrall of the Doorman’s anomalous effects,

02:07:16.010 --> 02:07:19.780
death is a truly preferable alternative to
ever facing it head-on.

02:07:19.780 --> 02:07:25.170
It’s worth mentioning that these tests were
conducted back in the 1970s, before the formation

02:07:25.170 --> 02:07:30.500
of the Foundation’s Ethics Committee, which
explains why their methods feel a little needlessly

02:07:30.500 --> 02:07:31.500
cruel.

02:07:31.500 --> 02:07:35.670
Since then, The Doorman has fully commandeered
the second-floor storage room, the same one

02:07:35.670 --> 02:07:37.770
where it caused Dr. Barker’s death.

02:07:37.770 --> 02:07:41.929
It only ever leaves the room to steal more
items from around the site.

02:07:41.929 --> 02:07:46.580
These items have included a cryotube, three
sets of standard Foundation surgical equipment,

02:07:46.580 --> 02:07:51.960
two D-Class research cadavers, one gasoline-powered
generator, a variety of chemicals from the

02:07:51.960 --> 02:07:57.380
chemical storage areas, and of course, poor
Agent Henderson’s can of powdered coffee

02:07:57.380 --> 02:07:58.380
creamer.

02:07:58.380 --> 02:08:02.960
The reason for the Doorman taking an interest
in these particular items remains unknown,

02:08:02.960 --> 02:08:06.070
but we can only assume that nothing good can
come of it.

02:08:06.070 --> 02:08:10.699
And there you have it, folks, the strange,
frightening, and eerily inconclusive tale

02:08:10.699 --> 02:08:12.000
of The Doorman.

02:08:12.000 --> 02:08:16.500
All we can really say is that we’re awfully
glad he’s fixated on bothering Site 41,

02:08:16.500 --> 02:08:20.640
because who knows what would happen if he
widened his net to the rest of us?

02:08:20.640 --> 02:08:22.780
Thankfully, we won’t need to think about
that.

02:08:22.780 --> 02:08:24.110
Oh, that’s odd.

02:08:24.110 --> 02:08:25.110
Can you hear that?

02:08:25.110 --> 02:08:26.480
I thought I was imagining it.

02:08:26.480 --> 02:08:29.610
Though come to think of it, I can’t help
but feel a little uneasy right now.

02:08:29.610 --> 02:08:32.210
Do you ever get that feeling you’re being
watched?

02:08:32.210 --> 02:08:35.340
Wait...The door, there’s something behind
the door.

02:08:35.340 --> 02:08:36.340
Can you feel it?

02:08:36.340 --> 02:08:42.239
Can you feel its red flesh and rotten teeth
pressing up against it, breathing, waiting?

02:08:42.239 --> 02:08:44.860
Can you feel it staring at you without eyes?

02:08:44.860 --> 02:08:46.810
Looking deep into your very soul?

02:08:46.810 --> 02:08:47.810
No?

02:08:47.810 --> 02:08:48.810
Well, that’s good.

02:08:48.810 --> 02:08:50.690
But just stay cautious, okay?

02:08:50.690 --> 02:08:56.840
After all, life has many doors, and you never
know who or what will be waiting for you behind

02:08:56.840 --> 02:08:58.210
the next one...

02:08:58.210 --> 02:09:03.920
It was an old factory in the middle of nowhere,
long-abandoned but still standing.

02:09:03.920 --> 02:09:08.380
In the past, it had been filled with workers,
but now nothing ran through it besides the

02:09:08.380 --> 02:09:10.449
occasional wildlife.

02:09:10.449 --> 02:09:17.170
One July night in 1949 though, four teenagers
decided it would be a good place to explore.

02:09:17.170 --> 02:09:22.590
The entrance to the factory was a large, old-fashioned
looking wooden door that was locked tightly

02:09:22.590 --> 02:09:23.590
shut.

02:09:23.590 --> 02:09:27.370
The teens looked around for another way in,
but couldn’t find one.

02:09:27.370 --> 02:09:31.650
What they did find though, was an old iron
lockbox.

02:09:31.650 --> 02:09:36.520
After some effort, they managed to get the
box open and found a ring of twelve old, rusted

02:09:36.520 --> 02:09:39.200
steel keys sitting inside.

02:09:39.200 --> 02:09:41.440
Would these old keys open the wooden door?

02:09:41.440 --> 02:09:45.730
Would they find something inside that would
make their night of breaking and entering

02:09:45.730 --> 02:09:46.730
worth it?

02:09:46.730 --> 02:09:53.290
If only they knew that by unlocking the door
all they would find was true horror… because

02:09:53.290 --> 02:10:00.829
they had just found SCP-004, better known
as The 12 Keys and the Door

02:10:00.829 --> 02:10:05.820
Not long after the local Sheriff received
a call from three of the panicked teens.

02:10:05.820 --> 02:10:09.850
They explained that while trying to get into
the factory, one of their friends had gone

02:10:09.850 --> 02:10:10.850
missing.

02:10:10.850 --> 02:10:15.469
The local authorities were quickly deployed,
taking the three teens into custody and beginning

02:10:15.469 --> 02:10:18.000
a full search of the factory grounds.

02:10:18.000 --> 02:10:21.960
The searching sheriff’s department officers
did eventually manage to find a clue as to

02:10:21.960 --> 02:10:26.690
what happened to the missing teen, but it
wasn’t a good sign.

02:10:26.690 --> 02:10:32.619
It was their severed hand, and even more disturbing
is that it wasn’t discovered outside the

02:10:32.619 --> 02:10:37.750
factory, no, it was found over eight kilometers
away.

02:10:37.750 --> 02:10:42.920
Soon other body parts were also found, some
as far as thirty-two kilometers away, but

02:10:42.920 --> 02:10:47.550
how could the parts of the dead teenager’s
body have been scattered so quickly and so

02:10:47.550 --> 02:10:49.170
far from each other?

02:10:49.170 --> 02:10:54.770
When the surviving teens were interrogated,
they all repeated the same wild story.

02:10:54.770 --> 02:10:59.530
The now dead teen had taken one of the keys
out of the old box they had found and used

02:10:59.530 --> 02:11:04.130
it to unlock the strange, old-fashioned wooden
door that led into the factory.

02:11:04.130 --> 02:11:09.920
They opened the door and stepped inside, and
the moment they did, they were immediately

02:11:09.920 --> 02:11:13.250
torn into pieces that suddenly vanished.

02:11:13.250 --> 02:11:18.409
These were no ordinary keys, and this was
no ordinary door.

02:11:18.409 --> 02:11:22.230
It was clear this was a job for the SCP Foundation.

02:11:22.230 --> 02:11:27.449
An SCP agent was deployed to the site to begin
investigating this anomaly.

02:11:27.449 --> 02:11:32.290
After getting the keys from local authorities,
the agent brought in a group of twelve D-class

02:11:32.290 --> 02:11:35.380
personnel to test them - one for each key.

02:11:35.380 --> 02:11:40.179
And it soon became clear that there was one
effect that was common - ten of the keys seemed

02:11:40.179 --> 02:11:44.090
to cause an effect that was completely unsurvivable.

02:11:44.090 --> 02:11:48.449
Upon trying the key in the door, the test
subject was immediately torn apart just like

02:11:48.449 --> 02:11:50.360
the unfortunate teenager.

02:11:50.360 --> 02:11:54.780
While one key caused the body parts to be
scattered in the immediate vicinity, all the

02:11:54.780 --> 02:11:57.860
others seemed to vanish into thin air.

02:11:57.860 --> 02:12:03.440
But it was the other two keys that proved
to be of even greater interest to the Foundation.

02:12:03.440 --> 02:12:09.590
Unlike with all the other tests, the D-class
using the key designated SCP-004-7 was able

02:12:09.590 --> 02:12:12.440
to enter the door and return completely unharmed.

02:12:12.440 --> 02:12:18.590
But the D-class using SCP-004-12 was a different
story.

02:12:18.590 --> 02:12:24.010
Physically, he returned unharmed - but he
seemed barely able to stagger out of the room.

02:12:24.010 --> 02:12:29.389
He collapsed, and then began trying to claw
his eyes out in panic and terror.

02:12:29.389 --> 02:12:33.520
He was quickly restrained and interrogated,
but he wasn’t coherent enough to give the

02:12:33.520 --> 02:12:37.480
Foundation any idea of what lurked behind
the door.

02:12:37.480 --> 02:12:44.320
The first D-class to enter using SCP-004-7,
the one who returned intact and sane, only

02:12:44.320 --> 02:12:49.140
said that it was a massive room inside - far
bigger than the building appeared from the

02:12:49.140 --> 02:12:50.140
outside.

02:12:50.140 --> 02:12:54.420
It was determined that the use of this key
was safe enough for further testing.

02:12:54.420 --> 02:12:59.080
The door was opened again using the same key
and the Foundation researchers propped it

02:12:59.080 --> 02:13:03.099
open so that an armed team could go in and
hopefully come out.

02:13:03.099 --> 02:13:08.280
A brief exploration of the massive room showed
some clear anomalous properties - not only

02:13:08.280 --> 02:13:13.929
was the room impossible to measure and possibly
limitless in size, it also seemed impossible

02:13:13.929 --> 02:13:18.809
to shine any light in the room beyond the
entry and the people inside were the only

02:13:18.809 --> 02:13:22.290
objects that could be felt or illuminated.

02:13:22.290 --> 02:13:25.929
Whatever this room was, it was keeping its
secrets.

02:13:25.929 --> 02:13:28.520
It was clear the site needed to be locked
down.

02:13:28.520 --> 02:13:31.679
All the initial witnesses who knew too much
were terminated…

02:13:31.679 --> 02:13:32.780
the Foundation was a little

02:13:32.780 --> 02:13:37.790
more trigger happy with terminations in the
40s, and the site was quickly locked down

02:13:37.790 --> 02:13:42.580
under the auspices of it being dangerous due
to unexploded ordinances.

02:13:42.580 --> 02:13:47.380
Fences were placed around the site so that
there would be no more teenage explorations.

02:13:47.380 --> 02:13:51.800
The records are spotty and incomplete, but
whatever happened behind those doors during

02:13:51.800 --> 02:13:58.659
the initial testing between 1949 and 1950,
the Foundation decided it had learned enough.

02:13:58.659 --> 02:14:04.840
The space-time anomalies at play inside of
SCP-004 were deemed too dangerous to explore

02:14:04.840 --> 02:14:09.070
further, and the site was sealed off with
all testing suspended.

02:14:09.070 --> 02:14:14.960
Whatever was lurking behind those doors, it
would keep its secrets - and the site seemed

02:14:14.960 --> 02:14:17.679
easy to secure and contain.

02:14:17.679 --> 02:14:24.139
But this was far from the end of SCP-004,
and fifty years later, it made its presence

02:14:24.139 --> 02:14:25.880
known again.

02:14:25.880 --> 02:14:31.559
It was another July night, many decades after
the unfortunate teenager first opened the

02:14:31.559 --> 02:14:34.469
doors to SCP-004.

02:14:34.469 --> 02:14:39.159
Only a few pieces of their body had been found,
but suddenly, the rest of the corpse appeared

02:14:39.159 --> 02:14:44.820
exactly where they had last been seen - outside
the old wooden door.

02:14:44.820 --> 02:14:49.409
Even odder was the fact that even though the
subject had died many years ago their body

02:14:49.409 --> 02:14:53.949
was still fresh, as if they had been killed
that same day.

02:14:53.949 --> 02:14:56.710
And this wouldn’t be the only sudden reappearance.

02:14:56.710 --> 02:15:02.020
Two days later, a second body missing parts
appeared in front of the door.

02:15:02.020 --> 02:15:06.510
This was quickly identified as one of the
original twelve test subjects who opened the

02:15:06.510 --> 02:15:07.510
door.

02:15:07.510 --> 02:15:11.460
Foundation scientists were once again sent
to the site to explore the space-time anomalies,

02:15:11.460 --> 02:15:16.520
and it was becoming clear that what went inside
the door didn’t stay there.

02:15:16.520 --> 02:15:22.070
It seemed like it went somewhere that didn’t
exist on the same plane as our reality.

02:15:22.070 --> 02:15:25.440
And if it could be understood, it could be
used.

02:15:25.440 --> 02:15:33.540
On March 21st, 1999 the Foundation began establishing
a site inside of SCP-004, but not for testing

02:15:33.540 --> 02:15:35.580
or research purposes.

02:15:35.580 --> 02:15:39.829
Nuclear weapons around the world were proliferating
fast, and evidence was mounting that World

02:15:39.829 --> 02:15:41.850
War 3 could happen soon.

02:15:41.850 --> 02:15:46.710
The Foundation needed a site that could survive
anything - and the mysterious room opened

02:15:46.710 --> 02:15:51.090
by the rusted keys seemed like it could be
their salvation.

02:15:51.090 --> 02:15:55.369
Supplies would go in the room and would be
preserved there indefinitely, safe from even

02:15:55.369 --> 02:15:57.360
nuclear annihilation.

02:15:57.360 --> 02:16:01.150
But getting the site set up would pose its
own challenges.

02:16:01.150 --> 02:16:07.060
Now dubbed Site 62, the facility was soon
expanded to house certain SCPs as well, in

02:16:07.060 --> 02:16:10.909
addition to a super-computer to house all
Foundation data.

02:16:10.909 --> 02:16:15.040
This would make it another invaluable backup
in the event of an end-of-the-world event

02:16:15.040 --> 02:16:16.980
that necessitated a reboot.

02:16:16.980 --> 02:16:21.650
The site was completed over the next year,
during which time they added high-tech containment

02:16:21.650 --> 02:16:26.180
units that could hold even the most dangerous
SCP specimens.

02:16:26.180 --> 02:16:30.380
Entering and exiting the facility seemed to
pose a risk to those working on it though.

02:16:30.380 --> 02:16:35.809
Time no longer behaved like it should, even
when using the one safe key.

02:16:35.809 --> 02:16:39.479
People would spend weeks in the site, then
exit claiming they had only been there a few

02:16:39.479 --> 02:16:40.590
days.

02:16:40.590 --> 02:16:45.340
It was highly unpredictable, and the Foundation
determined that it would be better to eliminate

02:16:45.340 --> 02:16:46.929
this X-factor.

02:16:46.929 --> 02:16:52.240
All personnel working at Site 62 would now
live on-site permanently, with their families

02:16:52.240 --> 02:16:55.600
being told they had died in an accident.

02:16:55.600 --> 02:17:02.349
It was August 18th, 2003 when the United States
and Canada were hit with a massive power outage,

02:17:02.349 --> 02:17:05.819
knocking out power to many of the Northeast’s
biggest population centers.

02:17:05.819 --> 02:17:11.859
While the SCP Foundation has backups on every
site, multiple generators failed, and it was

02:17:11.859 --> 02:17:14.290
53 minutes before power could be restored.

02:17:14.290 --> 02:17:20.269
During that time, those inside the mysterious
room were plunged into total darkness.

02:17:20.269 --> 02:17:24.609
And it soon became clear they weren’t alone.

02:17:24.609 --> 02:17:28.550
In the darkened room, the personnel reported
feeling like they were surrounded by people

02:17:28.550 --> 02:17:32.820
that shouldn’t be there - and creatures
that shouldn’t exist.

02:17:32.820 --> 02:17:37.969
While they couldn’t see anything and nothing
touched them, they were adamant that something

02:17:37.969 --> 02:17:43.370
was lurking in that room, and likely had been
for a very long time.

02:17:43.370 --> 02:17:48.410
It seemed the limited sources of light may
be the only thing keeping these entities - whatever

02:17:48.410 --> 02:17:50.500
they are - at bay.

02:17:50.500 --> 02:17:56.040
When testing had resumed on SCP-004 after
the bodies had reappeared outside the door,

02:17:56.040 --> 02:18:02.260
the Foundation decided to start exploring
the effects of SCP-004-12 as well.

02:18:02.260 --> 02:18:06.559
What about this key caused such psychological
horror that subjects would try to tear out

02:18:06.559 --> 02:18:08.130
their own eyes?

02:18:08.130 --> 02:18:14.349
This key seemed to drive them insane, and
of the sixteen subjects, only four were still

02:18:14.349 --> 02:18:17.810
alive for any length of time after their return.

02:18:17.810 --> 02:18:22.580
Most remained in a catatonic state, but one
was given extensive therapy and regained the

02:18:22.580 --> 02:18:27.010
ability to communicate, which allowed him
to give the Foundation their best picture

02:18:27.010 --> 02:18:29.660
yet of what lurked inside the room.

02:18:29.660 --> 02:18:34.230
While the D-Class personnel was still severely
affected by his time in the room and suffered

02:18:34.230 --> 02:18:38.229
near-total amnesia, he did remember a few
things.

02:18:38.229 --> 02:18:43.760
He remembered deep terror, and memories being
forced into his mind that made no sense as

02:18:43.760 --> 02:18:46.040
if they were artificially implanted.

02:18:46.040 --> 02:18:49.269
And he remembered not being alone.

02:18:49.269 --> 02:18:54.519
He described a massive green being, large
enough that he couldn’t see where it began

02:18:54.519 --> 02:18:56.490
and where it ended.

02:18:56.490 --> 02:18:58.620
The Foundation didn’t know what it was either.

02:18:58.620 --> 02:19:03.719
But what they do know for certain is that
when ten of the keys are used, the door is

02:19:03.719 --> 02:19:09.960
opened to a dimension where the laws of physics
are so different that it is completely unsurvivable.

02:19:09.960 --> 02:19:14.470
Studies are ongoing as to what makes this
effect so fatal and if there is a way to survive

02:19:14.470 --> 02:19:19.929
it, but no answers have been found - and with
only three bodies of victims recovered so

02:19:19.929 --> 02:19:23.219
far, there is little evidence

02:19:23.219 --> 02:19:27.520
But one object found on-site is of additional
interest.

02:19:27.520 --> 02:19:32.099
Discovered roughly a year after the initial
anomaly, in a manager’s office on the factory

02:19:32.099 --> 02:19:37.980
grounds, SCP-004-14 seems to be a miniature
version of the anomaly.

02:19:37.980 --> 02:19:42.970
It’s a large box made out of wood, and it
is the only other object opened by the one

02:19:42.970 --> 02:19:49.150
safe key - as well as five of the other keys
that lead to death when used on the main door.

02:19:49.150 --> 02:19:52.760
And this box has unusual properties as well.

02:19:52.760 --> 02:20:00.229
It opens automatically, and much like SCP-004’s
room, it seems to be much larger on the inside

02:20:00.229 --> 02:20:01.620
than the outside.

02:20:01.620 --> 02:20:04.600
It is possible to come in and out safely.

02:20:04.600 --> 02:20:08.910
But when the box is locked again, it’s a
different story.

02:20:08.910 --> 02:20:13.400
Objects placed in the box don’t seem to
affect its weight, and when the box is closed

02:20:13.400 --> 02:20:16.380
and locked, they vanish completely.

02:20:16.380 --> 02:20:20.990
Unlike the main room, nothing that’s gone
inside and locked in has ever been recovered.

02:20:20.990 --> 02:20:23.460
This includes living beings.

02:20:23.460 --> 02:20:28.090
Few answers have been found about where they
go, and it’s possible the box could be used

02:20:28.090 --> 02:20:33.069
to dispose of specimens deemed to be too dangerous
- but with no answers about where they go

02:20:33.069 --> 02:20:37.560
and when they might come back, this may be
too risky.

02:20:37.560 --> 02:20:43.040
Because SCP-004 is fixed in place, special
containment procedures focus on making sure

02:20:43.040 --> 02:20:44.689
it stays that way.

02:20:44.689 --> 02:20:49.140
It is strictly forbidden to take any of the
other keys through the door, for fear of losing

02:20:49.140 --> 02:20:52.370
them or causing it to react in an unpredictable
way.

02:20:52.370 --> 02:20:58.350
If the site should be breached, or anything
contained in Site 62 manages escape containment,

02:20:58.350 --> 02:21:01.630
the Foundation is ready to activate the on-site
warhead.

02:21:01.630 --> 02:21:06.301
Only employees with level 1 clearance can
access the site, and only Level 4s and above

02:21:06.301 --> 02:21:11.130
can use the keys - with all knowing that any
attempt to remove the keys from the site will

02:21:11.130 --> 02:21:15.540
result in immediate termination.

02:21:15.540 --> 02:21:20.750
For now, SCP-004 remains fenced off, with
only select experiments continuing, as the

02:21:20.750 --> 02:21:23.590
Foundation tries to unravel its mysteries.

02:21:23.590 --> 02:21:28.899
But whatever lurks behind that old wooden
door, it keeps its secrets well.

02:21:28.899 --> 02:21:32.890
The SCP Foundation contains a lot of monsters.

02:21:32.890 --> 02:21:40.260
From SCP-682, the lizard that refuses to die,
to SCP-939, a species of pack hunters that

02:21:40.260 --> 02:21:45.180
steal the voices of their victims – the
dangerous predators that occupy the hundreds

02:21:45.180 --> 02:21:51.510
of containment cells of the Foundation make
it their job to hunt and kill innocent people

02:21:51.510 --> 02:21:52.510
– or worse.

02:21:52.510 --> 02:21:56.180
But have you ever wondered where some of those
monsters come from?

02:21:56.180 --> 02:22:03.110
The first encounter that the SCP Foundation
had with SCP-4049 was on July 14th of 2010.

02:22:03.110 --> 02:22:07.740
The Foundation operates a massive surveillance
network around the entire world – through

02:22:07.740 --> 02:22:14.840
the use of AI, delegated duties, and compartmentalized
information, they’re able to have 911 operators

02:22:14.840 --> 02:22:19.761
report any calls that seem anomalous in nature
while knowing nothing about the Foundation

02:22:19.761 --> 02:22:21.000
itself.

02:22:21.000 --> 02:22:26.000
This way, they’re able to constantly be
aware of anything anomalous going on in the

02:22:26.000 --> 02:22:28.550
country that gets reported to 911.

02:22:28.550 --> 02:22:33.840
On July 14th, the Foundation was alerted of
a call that likely had an anomalous component.

02:22:33.840 --> 02:22:36.090
At first, it didn’t seem like much.

02:22:36.090 --> 02:22:41.420
It was to a remote address in Wyoming, outside
of a small town called Gardnerville.

02:22:41.420 --> 02:22:47.280
The vacation home of one Richard Samson, a
wealthy businessman in the area, placed right

02:22:47.280 --> 02:22:48.460
on the slopes.

02:22:48.460 --> 02:22:52.689
The call was made late in the afternoon, by
someone purporting to be the groundskeeper

02:22:52.689 --> 02:22:55.530
of the home while Mr. Samson was away.

02:22:55.530 --> 02:23:00.939
He was screaming into the phone, terrified
and largely incoherent, but the operator made

02:23:00.939 --> 02:23:03.900
out something about a monster attacking the
house.

02:23:03.900 --> 02:23:09.149
There was a lot of noise in the background,
sounds of shouting, destruction, and what

02:23:09.149 --> 02:23:11.860
sounded like animalistic roars and grunts.

02:23:11.860 --> 02:23:16.650
The 911 operator moved the call up, and it
didn’t take long for the Foundation to determine

02:23:16.650 --> 02:23:19.029
that something strange was going on here.

02:23:19.029 --> 02:23:23.670
They dispatched a handful of agents, deep
undercover as officers with the Wyoming Highway

02:23:23.670 --> 02:23:27.790
Patrol, to the address of the home where the
call had come from.

02:23:27.790 --> 02:23:33.040
After about half an hour, the agents called
back in to HQ - the scene they had found was

02:23:33.040 --> 02:23:35.141
nothing short of gruesome.

02:23:35.141 --> 02:23:39.609
Upon arrival, they were greeted with what
appeared to be the aftermath of a particularly

02:23:39.609 --> 02:23:41.939
violent and brief tornado.

02:23:41.939 --> 02:23:46.800
The entire front section of the ground floor
had been shredded, the gardens trampled, and

02:23:46.800 --> 02:23:49.180
the interior utterly destroyed.

02:23:49.180 --> 02:23:54.439
The agents picked their way between the wreckage
of the home – it functionally didn’t exist

02:23:54.439 --> 02:23:55.439
anymore.

02:23:55.439 --> 02:23:59.810
The walls were collapsed from being rammed
and torn through, and the roof had collapsed

02:23:59.810 --> 02:24:01.080
in on itself.

02:24:01.080 --> 02:24:05.930
The broken shards and pieces of furniture
and wreckage were everywhere.

02:24:05.930 --> 02:24:11.109
Despite appearances, this wasn’t a tornado
– a tornado would have thrown the entire

02:24:11.109 --> 02:24:12.400
house around.

02:24:12.400 --> 02:24:20.760
No, this was as the groundskeeper had said
– something alive, monstrous, and very angry.

02:24:20.760 --> 02:24:25.080
Speaking of the groundskeeper, the Foundation
agents began to look for him once they took

02:24:25.080 --> 02:24:26.610
stock of the damage to the home.

02:24:26.610 --> 02:24:31.710
At first, they couldn’t find him among the
massive pieces of debris and assumed the worst.

02:24:31.710 --> 02:24:36.399
Even if whatever had destroyed the house decided
to not kill him, he could easily have been

02:24:36.399 --> 02:24:41.070
killed by the collapsing house, buried under
rubble, or a dozen other things.

02:24:41.070 --> 02:24:45.470
They picked through the ruins, calling out
that they were from the police and were here

02:24:45.470 --> 02:24:46.510
to help.

02:24:46.510 --> 02:24:50.510
Eventually, after another half hour of searching,
they heard something.

02:24:50.510 --> 02:24:54.680
What sounded like crying and whispering became
audible as the wind died down.

02:24:54.680 --> 02:24:58.870
The agents honed in on the noise and found
it was coming from one of the larger piles

02:24:58.870 --> 02:24:59.920
of rubble.

02:24:59.920 --> 02:25:04.080
After getting some equipment, they were able
to heft up the piece of the collapsed roof,

02:25:04.080 --> 02:25:09.890
and found the groundskeeper underneath, curled
into a ball and talking to himself.

02:25:09.890 --> 02:25:14.029
He seemed to be in some kind of a panicked
fugue state, not responding to the agents

02:25:14.029 --> 02:25:15.479
trying to get through to him.

02:25:15.479 --> 02:25:20.200
They wrapped him in a shock blanket and put
him in the back of one of their patrol cars,

02:25:20.200 --> 02:25:24.880
but even after that they couldn’t get anything
of use out of him - he was just shaking and

02:25:24.880 --> 02:25:27.479
muttering something about monsters.

02:25:27.479 --> 02:25:32.820
Eventually, he was given amnestics to forget
about the incident entirely and recovered.

02:25:32.820 --> 02:25:37.840
After the agents reported back to HQ, a new
issue popped up - they weren’t the only

02:25:37.840 --> 02:25:39.640
ones who knew about this.

02:25:39.640 --> 02:25:42.910
A news website a few counties away had the
story.

02:25:42.910 --> 02:25:46.820
The Foundation quickly put out a cover story
- the house had probably been destroyed by

02:25:46.820 --> 02:25:49.760
a group of grizzly bears, possibly rabid.

02:25:49.760 --> 02:25:54.200
They had the local government issue a warning
advising local residents to stay inside and

02:25:54.200 --> 02:25:58.270
out of the wilderness until the animals could
be tracked and euthanized.

02:25:58.270 --> 02:26:01.689
And that’s exactly what the Foundation did.

02:26:01.689 --> 02:26:07.550
Mobile Task Force Epsilon-6, the Village Idiots
an MTF that specializes in taking on anomalous

02:26:07.550 --> 02:26:13.140
threats in remote, rural areas and small towns
- were dispatched to track and contain or

02:26:13.140 --> 02:26:16.270
terminate whatever had destroyed that mansion.

02:26:16.270 --> 02:26:21.550
The creature had left a strong trail of tracks,
scent, and general destruction, and the troopers

02:26:21.550 --> 02:26:26.420
followed it north for hours, into another
dense forest – where they discovered the

02:26:26.420 --> 02:26:31.180
gigantic, hulking creature while it was asleep
and shot it.

02:26:31.180 --> 02:26:36.640
It was huge, with rippling muscles on all
four legs and no fur to speak of – but the

02:26:36.640 --> 02:26:41.120
most striking feature was a frighteningly
human face.

02:26:41.120 --> 02:26:45.399
The agents resolved to let the researchers
handle the autopsy, and busied themselves

02:26:45.399 --> 02:26:49.840
with the other thing in that forest: there
was an old, abandoned arms factory that the

02:26:49.840 --> 02:26:51.950
creature seemed to have come from.

02:26:51.950 --> 02:26:56.600
The agents descended into the decrepit, abandoned
building, following the creature’s trail

02:26:56.600 --> 02:26:57.990
right into the basement.

02:26:57.990 --> 02:27:03.069
There, they found a large steel door, and
behind it, the anomaly that would eventually

02:27:03.069 --> 02:27:06.140
be called SCP-4049.

02:27:06.140 --> 02:27:12.030
It was strange – it seemed to be some kind
of massive, empty room looking up into the

02:27:12.030 --> 02:27:15.180
sky, even though they were deep underground.

02:27:15.180 --> 02:27:20.190
Not entirely empty - the dirt ground had a
series of concentric rings of gravestones

02:27:20.190 --> 02:27:22.490
in it, all facing inward.

02:27:22.490 --> 02:27:26.649
The agents retreated once they realized they
had walked into a spatial anomaly and called

02:27:26.649 --> 02:27:27.670
for backup.

02:27:27.670 --> 02:27:31.550
The Foundation quickly flew in researchers
and a containment team to figure out what

02:27:31.550 --> 02:27:36.290
the anomaly was and to ensure no one else
got into the factory while they figured that

02:27:36.290 --> 02:27:37.290
out.

02:27:37.290 --> 02:27:40.690
The basement of the factory became a sort
of base of operations for the large crew of

02:27:40.690 --> 02:27:45.560
research and security personnel assigned to
SCP-4049.

02:27:45.560 --> 02:27:50.819
After making sure there were no other of the
monsters, designated SCP-4049-1 instances,

02:27:50.819 --> 02:27:55.990
in the nearby forest, the researchers began
to experiment on it.

02:27:55.990 --> 02:28:00.729
They determined that the room on the other
side of the hallway was in an extradimensional

02:28:00.729 --> 02:28:01.729
space.

02:28:01.729 --> 02:28:05.760
Members of D-Class personnel were sent in
with GPS trackers and even though they could

02:28:05.760 --> 02:28:09.899
still be heard fine on the radio, the GPS
trackers failed totally.

02:28:09.899 --> 02:28:15.080
Obviously, the fact that you could see the
sky from an underground room was anomalous,

02:28:15.080 --> 02:28:19.550
but attempts to dig into where the room should’ve
been from the surface also led to nothing

02:28:19.550 --> 02:28:21.029
but more dirt.

02:28:21.029 --> 02:28:24.580
From inside, the D-Class members were able
to give a detailed report on the room as they

02:28:24.580 --> 02:28:25.670
walked around.

02:28:25.670 --> 02:28:31.109
It was perfectly circular and pretty large
- about 30 feet across, give or take.

02:28:31.109 --> 02:28:36.340
A tall white wall ringed the room’s border
and was perfectly smooth and impossible to

02:28:36.340 --> 02:28:39.830
get a grip on enough to climb – cold, hard
marble.

02:28:39.830 --> 02:28:45.170
The floor of the room wasn’t marble, though
– it seemed to be regular dirt.

02:28:45.170 --> 02:28:48.971
The D-Classes were ordered by researchers
to get samples of what they could, and they

02:28:48.971 --> 02:28:51.189
scooped a little dirt into sample bags.

02:28:51.189 --> 02:28:57.300
But as soon as the subjects stepped back over
the threshold into the corridor of SCP-4049,

02:28:57.300 --> 02:29:03.130
the sample bags they collected spontaneously
combusted, going up in flames.

02:29:03.130 --> 02:29:08.010
Any chemical analysis of its composition was,
of course, impossible.

02:29:08.010 --> 02:29:12.060
The researchers resolved to get what information
they could out of just looking at SCP-4049

02:29:12.060 --> 02:29:13.060
first.

02:29:13.060 --> 02:29:16.090
And there was still a lot to look at.

02:29:16.090 --> 02:29:21.840
The D-class inspected the rings of gravestones
inside SCP-4049 – there were just two at

02:29:21.840 --> 02:29:25.340
the moment, a larger ring containing a smaller
ring.

02:29:25.340 --> 02:29:29.689
Inside the smaller ring, there was a circular
empty space a few feet wide.

02:29:29.689 --> 02:29:34.689
Most of the graves were unfilled and unmarked
– just a patch of dirt turned over.

02:29:34.689 --> 02:29:39.460
But about a dozen of them had a gravestone
at their head, made of that same white marble

02:29:39.460 --> 02:29:41.460
substance the walls were made from.

02:29:41.460 --> 02:29:47.439
They weren’t fancy – just a simple white
rectangle, stamped with some strange symbols.

02:29:47.439 --> 02:29:52.109
The D-class took photos and sent them to the
researchers, who recognized the markings as

02:29:52.109 --> 02:29:54.851
a word in Ancient Greek: “hound”.

02:29:54.851 --> 02:30:00.430
The researchers were admittedly baffled by
what this could mean for SCP-4049, but decided

02:30:00.430 --> 02:30:07.850
to figure out the connection using the evidence
they had: the corpse of the SCP-4049-1 instance.

02:30:07.850 --> 02:30:13.090
The researchers placed the huge corpse inside
the factory, creating a secure space to perform

02:30:13.090 --> 02:30:14.090
the autopsy.

02:30:14.090 --> 02:30:19.729
Then, a team of doctors began cutting into
it with scalpels - or they tried, anyway.

02:30:19.729 --> 02:30:23.689
They quickly realized that the skin of the
creature was far too thick to be breached

02:30:23.689 --> 02:30:27.300
with scalpels, and resorted to long, sharpened
knives.

02:30:27.300 --> 02:30:32.120
They discovered quite a few things about the
instance's anatomy, along with why and how

02:30:32.120 --> 02:30:35.399
it was able to do and absorb so much damage.

02:30:35.399 --> 02:30:38.640
It was a quadruped, walking on four limbs.

02:30:38.640 --> 02:30:43.270
The forward ones seemed to be in the shape
of arms with elbows and wrists, but also had

02:30:43.270 --> 02:30:45.560
clawed paws like a dog’s.

02:30:45.560 --> 02:30:51.399
The back legs were thick and heavily muscled,
and digitigrade - again, just like a dog,

02:30:51.399 --> 02:30:55.180
so they could be used to leap and jump great
distances.

02:30:55.180 --> 02:30:59.359
Once they cut away the skin, the researchers
noticed that it was indeed much thicker than

02:30:59.359 --> 02:31:05.590
they expected it to be – human skin is only
about 2mm thick, but this was a full centimeter

02:31:05.590 --> 02:31:09.170
throughout, as well as incredibly tough and
gamey.

02:31:09.170 --> 02:31:14.300
Internally, the structure was all wrong – it
seemed almost human-like, but with a few key

02:31:14.300 --> 02:31:18.279
differences to suit the vastly-changed exterior
body.

02:31:18.279 --> 02:31:23.680
The spine was much thicker and wider, as well
as being curved to fit the four-legged structure.

02:31:23.680 --> 02:31:28.470
There seemed to be redundant organs – the
researchers theorized they were backups, like

02:31:28.470 --> 02:31:31.890
the secondary heart they found inside the
creature’s innards.

02:31:31.890 --> 02:31:36.610
It could serve as a backup if the main heart
stopped working or was damaged, or it could

02:31:36.610 --> 02:31:41.160
work together with the main heart to improve
the instance’s performance during physical

02:31:41.160 --> 02:31:42.160
activity.

02:31:42.160 --> 02:31:47.040
There didn’t seem to be any kind of reproductive
system – it wasn’t surgically removed,

02:31:47.040 --> 02:31:51.010
it just wasn’t there at all, like it had
magically disappeared.

02:31:51.010 --> 02:31:54.500
And inside the thing’s head, the skull was
different.

02:31:54.500 --> 02:31:58.900
The mouth was much wider and larger, and it
didn’t take long for the researchers to

02:31:58.900 --> 02:32:00.000
figure out why.

02:32:00.000 --> 02:32:05.990
When rooting around in its mouth, they quickly
discovered it had an extra set of sharp teeth

02:32:05.990 --> 02:32:08.090
behind its main set.

02:32:08.090 --> 02:32:12.771
All unnerving, slightly disturbing discoveries,
but the most frightening wasn’t something

02:32:12.771 --> 02:32:14.859
they found inside the instance.

02:32:14.859 --> 02:32:20.420
It was something they noticed immediately
upon containing it – its face was human.

02:32:20.420 --> 02:32:25.660
It had been morphed, of course, to fit the
altered skull, but there were two eyes, a

02:32:25.660 --> 02:32:31.240
forehead, a nose, lips – it was inarguably
a human face.

02:32:31.240 --> 02:32:36.390
When the researchers sent for a DNA test,
they were disturbed but not surprised to discover

02:32:36.390 --> 02:32:41.391
what they had already been expecting: the
instance was entirely genetically human.

02:32:41.391 --> 02:32:47.540
Not a changed species or close relative – this
creature had once been a regular human being,

02:32:47.540 --> 02:32:49.399
like you or I.

02:32:49.399 --> 02:32:53.490
The researchers had just sent the DNA sample
off to check if there was a match in the criminal

02:32:53.490 --> 02:32:58.380
database when suddenly, the lights went red,
the doors sealed, and the site’s alarms

02:32:58.380 --> 02:32:59.670
began to sound

02:32:59.670 --> 02:33:07.090
At that moment, the steel door leading to
SCP-4049 flung open, and another SCP-4049-1

02:33:07.090 --> 02:33:10.570
instance bounded out into the corridor on
all fours.

02:33:10.570 --> 02:33:14.771
It set its beady eyes on three members of
the Mobile Task Force, standing on the far

02:33:14.771 --> 02:33:15.930
side of the long corridor.

02:33:15.930 --> 02:33:21.540
For a moment, it didn’t do anything – then
it let out a long screech that echoed around

02:33:21.540 --> 02:33:23.290
the entire factory.

02:33:23.290 --> 02:33:27.370
Its rear legs tensed up, and it began to bound
down the hallway towards them.

02:33:27.370 --> 02:33:31.250
All of the security guards opened fire with
their machine guns on the anomaly, trying

02:33:31.250 --> 02:33:32.870
to bring it down.

02:33:32.870 --> 02:33:37.450
It shrugged off the bullets like they were
raindrops and didn’t so much as slow down.

02:33:37.450 --> 02:33:41.609
Meanwhile, the two dozen other security personnel
in the facility were rapidly grabbing their

02:33:41.609 --> 02:33:46.649
weapons and armor from their lockers before
rocketing down the stairs to the corridor.

02:33:46.649 --> 02:33:51.460
By the time they made it down, it was too
late – the instance was using its claws

02:33:51.460 --> 02:33:56.620
and jaws to tear two of the three poor members
of the Task Force to shreds.

02:33:56.620 --> 02:34:01.649
It wasn’t eating them - but it was attacking
them with enough anger and malice that there

02:34:01.649 --> 02:34:04.130
wasn’t going to be much left when it was
done.

02:34:04.130 --> 02:34:08.960
The third member of the task force had fallen
and was backing away from the anomaly in fear.

02:34:08.960 --> 02:34:14.300
The remaining members of the Task Force opened
fire, smothering the SCP-4049-1 instance in

02:34:14.300 --> 02:34:15.800
a hail of bullets.

02:34:15.800 --> 02:34:20.530
The sudden, overwhelming firepower caught
it off-guard, and after a few seconds of sustained

02:34:20.530 --> 02:34:23.660
gunfire, it fell to the ground, dead.

02:34:23.660 --> 02:34:28.830
Once the Foundation realized the active danger
that SCP-4049 presented, they decided not

02:34:28.830 --> 02:34:31.310
to take any chances with containment.

02:34:31.310 --> 02:34:36.979
The 50 meter long corridor leading to SCP-4049
from the basement elevator was fortified - an

02:34:36.979 --> 02:34:41.479
airlock was installed on the far side, separating
it from the rest of the factory.

02:34:41.479 --> 02:34:46.300
Then motion detectors were set every few meters
throughout the hallway, attached to a series

02:34:46.300 --> 02:34:48.280
of ‘deterrents’.

02:34:48.280 --> 02:34:54.060
If an SCP-4049-1 instance smashed out of the
steel door, it would trip the alarms and activate

02:34:54.060 --> 02:34:59.650
everything from a supersonic sound cannon
to sentry guns and a machine gun emplacement.

02:34:59.650 --> 02:35:05.070
And if none of those worked, the entire corridor
could be pumped full of nerve gas, guaranteeing

02:35:05.070 --> 02:35:09.021
the death of the instance without risking
the lives of any personnel.

02:35:09.021 --> 02:35:15.990
This ‘kill corridor’ was to be guarded
by the Applied Task Force Iota-9 to ensure

02:35:15.990 --> 02:35:19.120
that no SCP-4049-1 instance would survive
its escape.

02:35:19.120 --> 02:35:23.819
But after the corridor was retrofitted, the
Foundation had a bigger problem: where were

02:35:23.819 --> 02:35:28.819
these SCP-4049-1 instances coming from to
begin with?

02:35:28.819 --> 02:35:33.640
They performed another DNA test on the new
instance – its face was different, so it

02:35:33.640 --> 02:35:35.859
seemed logical that it was a different person.

02:35:35.859 --> 02:35:40.750
When the results came back, the researchers
were surprised to find that not just one but

02:35:40.750 --> 02:35:45.069
both of the samples had DNA matches in the
national database.

02:35:45.069 --> 02:35:49.760
Both were men from the tri-state area who
had mysteriously died or disappeared in the

02:35:49.760 --> 02:35:53.100
past few months, while at some kind of religious
service.

02:35:53.100 --> 02:35:57.740
They were both avid big game hunters, with
an interest in shooting moose, bears, and

02:35:57.740 --> 02:35:58.740
elk.

02:35:58.740 --> 02:36:03.229
And most important, they had both been the
subject of a fire-related incident – one

02:36:03.229 --> 02:36:06.080
had been presumed dead when his house burned
down.

02:36:06.080 --> 02:36:10.910
The other had simply vanished, with his car
being found hours later on fire by the side

02:36:10.910 --> 02:36:11.910
of the highway.

02:36:11.910 --> 02:36:17.170
In both cases, a body was never recovered
- but the authorities did find a strange stone-tipped

02:36:17.170 --> 02:36:19.790
arrow driven into the ground nearby.

02:36:19.790 --> 02:36:23.420
Over the following months, the Foundation
observed a number of these strange events

02:36:23.420 --> 02:36:29.689
happen in Wyoming, Idaho, and Montana, and
like clockwork, every time it happened, a

02:36:29.689 --> 02:36:37.750
new headstone appeared over one of the previously-unmarked
graves inside SCP-4049, saying the same Greek

02:36:37.750 --> 02:36:39.540
word: “hound”.

02:36:39.540 --> 02:36:44.080
On top of all of that, almost every time a
man in the area disappeared under these specific

02:36:44.080 --> 02:36:52.660
circumstances and a grave was created, an
SCP-4049-1 instance would appear inside SCP-4049

02:36:52.660 --> 02:36:57.280
sometime in the following two months, buried
within the soil circle in the center of the

02:36:57.280 --> 02:36:58.280
room.

02:36:58.280 --> 02:37:02.610
It would claw its way out of the dirt, smash
open the steel door to SCP-4049, and race

02:37:02.610 --> 02:37:08.720
down the hallway trying to kill and destroy
whatever was in front of it until it was gunned

02:37:08.720 --> 02:37:09.720
down.

02:37:09.720 --> 02:37:12.470
But in one instance, that didn’t happen.

02:37:12.470 --> 02:37:19.300
On September 17th of 2015, the Foundation
had gotten into the rhythm of containing SCP-4049,

02:37:19.300 --> 02:37:23.160
so they weren’t startled or caught off guard
when an agent with the Highway Patrol reported

02:37:23.160 --> 02:37:28.100
finding a flaming truck near a hunting ground
– in the bed was an elk carcass, with a

02:37:28.100 --> 02:37:31.050
stone-tipped arrow lodged deep into the meat.

02:37:31.050 --> 02:37:35.450
Applied Task Force Iota-9 at the factory began
to prepare for an imminent appearance from

02:37:35.450 --> 02:37:41.240
an SCP-4049-1 entity within the following
weeks, and established a round-the-clock guard

02:37:41.240 --> 02:37:42.609
in the kill corridor.

02:37:42.609 --> 02:37:43.609
But…

02:37:43.609 --> 02:37:44.939
it never came.

02:37:44.939 --> 02:37:47.420
By December, nothing had happened at all.

02:37:47.420 --> 02:37:53.020
The Foundation made the decision – a D-class
would be sent into SCP-4049 with a camera

02:37:53.020 --> 02:37:57.670
and radio, in the hopes of manually initiating
the event to occur.

02:37:57.670 --> 02:38:02.520
The D-class subject wasn’t given very specific
instructions - just fitted with a body camera,

02:38:02.520 --> 02:38:07.110
a two-way radio, and told to listen to all
instructions on his headset.

02:38:07.110 --> 02:38:11.340
The researchers ordered him forward until
he reached the other side of the hallway,

02:38:11.340 --> 02:38:17.149
where he was to open the steel door leading
to SCP-4049 and enter.

02:38:17.149 --> 02:38:22.130
When he entered, everything looked the same
as the Foundation expected it to - the same

02:38:22.130 --> 02:38:23.630
gravestones, walls, and dirt.

02:38:23.630 --> 02:38:28.359
He moved towards the center of the room, to
the dirt circle, but suddenly stopped, looking

02:38:28.359 --> 02:38:29.359
around.

02:38:29.359 --> 02:38:33.860
When the researchers asked why, he reported
hearing the sounds of dogs barking for a moment,

02:38:33.860 --> 02:38:36.590
before the researchers told him to keep walking.

02:38:36.590 --> 02:38:41.210
When he stopped in the center of the room,
he again radioed in, feeling that someone

02:38:41.210 --> 02:38:42.260
was there.

02:38:42.260 --> 02:38:47.370
The camera didn’t pick anyone up, but he
insisted that there was an odd feeling, just

02:38:47.370 --> 02:38:50.050
before his audio stream suddenly cut out.

02:38:50.050 --> 02:38:55.590
A burst of static interference drowned everything
else out, and slowly winded down.

02:38:55.590 --> 02:39:01.689
The D-class couldn’t be heard anymore – but
a strange female voice was on the line, speaking

02:39:01.689 --> 02:39:03.109
to the Foundation.

02:39:03.109 --> 02:39:08.180
She mentioned that the Foundation had been
ruining her pets for far too long.

02:39:08.180 --> 02:39:13.080
The Foundation demanded the speaker identify
themself, but she just scoffed, indignant

02:39:13.080 --> 02:39:15.529
at what she called ‘human arrogance’.

02:39:15.529 --> 02:39:19.830
Right after that, all audio feeds were cut
out permanently.

02:39:19.830 --> 02:39:25.280
This mysterious woman was designated SCP-4049-2.

02:39:25.280 --> 02:39:33.770
Seven seconds after they cut out, the largest
SCP-4049-1 instance ever recorded exited SCP-4049,

02:39:33.770 --> 02:39:36.100
standing at almost 11 meters high.

02:39:36.100 --> 02:39:41.439
All of the deterrents were activated, but
even then, it still took all of them combined

02:39:41.439 --> 02:39:45.750
with machine-gun fire from the Applied Task
Force to bring the creature down.

02:39:45.750 --> 02:39:50.050
No remains of the D-class and no traces of
whoever was speaking on the radio were ever

02:39:50.050 --> 02:39:51.561
found by the Researchers.

02:39:51.561 --> 02:39:57.050
It can be dangerous to stand between someone
and their beloved pets…

02:39:57.050 --> 02:39:59.649
Did you ever have to perform a dissection
in school?

02:39:59.649 --> 02:40:05.020
Maybe you had to carve up a fetal pig or slice
into a frog while nightmarish visions of Kermit

02:40:05.020 --> 02:40:08.140
and a widowed Miss Piggy danced in your head.

02:40:08.140 --> 02:40:13.010
Though it’s rarely a pleasant experience,
unless your tastes are on the morbid side,

02:40:13.010 --> 02:40:17.779
most biology teachers would agree that the
best way to learn how something works is to

02:40:17.779 --> 02:40:19.120
take it apart.

02:40:19.120 --> 02:40:23.970
As distasteful as it can be to hold a frog’s
tiny liver in your hands, it definitely does

02:40:23.970 --> 02:40:27.620
give you a better sense of the pieces that
make up the complete creature.

02:40:27.620 --> 02:40:32.580
But what if there was an easier way to look
at the individual parts of a living thing?

02:40:32.580 --> 02:40:36.930
What if you could take it apart without ever
having to prep a scalpel or stain your hands

02:40:36.930 --> 02:40:39.260
with the blood of innocent frogs?

02:40:39.260 --> 02:40:44.080
Like most of the seemingly impossible things
in our world, the SCP Foundation discovered

02:40:44.080 --> 02:40:47.180
something that allows its users to do just
that.

02:40:47.180 --> 02:40:52.149
In fact, it can handle a lot more than just
a frog, and its applications go far beyond

02:40:52.149 --> 02:40:55.550
the confines of a high school science lab.

02:40:55.550 --> 02:41:00.940
SCP-291 is a small, plain steel building with
a larger door on one side.

02:41:00.940 --> 02:41:05.970
The door has no handle or knob, and functions
similarly to a garage door.

02:41:05.970 --> 02:41:11.410
The door cannot be pried open by any ordinary
means, and the inside of SCP-291 can only

02:41:11.410 --> 02:41:15.660
be accessed if the structure is connected
to a suitable power source.

02:41:15.660 --> 02:41:20.370
Once a power source has been connected, the
door raises and exposes the room inside.

02:41:20.370 --> 02:41:23.320
It is small, about 4x2 meters.

02:41:23.320 --> 02:41:29.771
It contains a console board, a large screen,
and a plexiglass container resembling a coffin.

02:41:29.771 --> 02:41:31.710
How very sinister.

02:41:31.710 --> 02:41:36.979
The coffin is large enough to contain a human
under 7 feet tall - so sorry, Fernand the

02:41:36.979 --> 02:41:39.760
Cannibal, you’re going to need to sit this
one out.

02:41:39.760 --> 02:41:44.570
The coffin sits on a conveyor belt, with several
tubes connected to the wall above it.

02:41:44.570 --> 02:41:49.140
On the opposite side of the room, there are
holes of varying sizes, each containing a

02:41:49.140 --> 02:41:51.939
small door that can be opened or closed.

02:41:51.939 --> 02:41:57.370
Because initial observation indicated that
SCP-291 was intended for some kind of human

02:41:57.370 --> 02:42:01.340
testing, a D-class test subject was selected
for experimentation.

02:42:01.340 --> 02:42:05.700
The subject was instructed to lie down in
the coffin, and wait to see what would happen

02:42:05.700 --> 02:42:06.700
next.

02:42:06.700 --> 02:42:10.850
The display screen lit up, depicting a grid-lined
image of the test subject.

02:42:10.850 --> 02:42:15.210
Buttons along the console board adjusted the
image, showing the skin, muscles, and organ

02:42:15.210 --> 02:42:17.630
systems of the person in the coffin.

02:42:17.630 --> 02:42:21.870
There were no words or numbers on the screen,
and all of the buttons appeared to have only

02:42:21.870 --> 02:42:24.940
two settings: on and off.

02:42:24.940 --> 02:42:28.600
When one of the researchers pressed the first
button on the console, the tubes above the

02:42:28.600 --> 02:42:31.370
coffin began pouring a blue liquid into it.

02:42:31.370 --> 02:42:36.439
The test subject reacted with confusion, but
did not experience any adverse effects.

02:42:36.439 --> 02:42:40.550
They quickly lost consciousness, indicating
that the liquid was some sort of sedative.

02:42:40.550 --> 02:42:45.420
The liquid continued to pour into the coffin
until the vessel was completely filled, at

02:42:45.420 --> 02:42:47.860
which point it congealed into a thick gel.

02:42:47.860 --> 02:42:52.010
The test subject’s breathing and heartbeat
slowed to a stop, and the conveyor belt suddenly

02:42:52.010 --> 02:42:53.420
creaked to life.

02:42:53.420 --> 02:42:57.649
The coffin was carried, test subject inside,
through a small door that immediately locked

02:42:57.649 --> 02:42:58.649
behind it.

02:42:58.649 --> 02:43:02.870
The small room was filled with the sounds
of gears turning, machinery clinking, and

02:43:02.870 --> 02:43:03.979
motors whirring.

02:43:03.979 --> 02:43:08.819
The display screen was taken over by a large
rectangle, resembling a traditional “loading”

02:43:08.819 --> 02:43:09.819
screen.

02:43:09.819 --> 02:43:15.090
After thirty minutes, the process was complete,
and the back door of the room unlocked itself.

02:43:15.090 --> 02:43:18.840
When a researcher walked through the back
door, they found another room with a conveyor

02:43:18.840 --> 02:43:21.960
belt and a row of two dozen lockers.

02:43:21.960 --> 02:43:28.189
Each locker was opened, one at a time, and
its contents removed for examination.

02:43:28.189 --> 02:43:33.211
Inside each, the research team found a different
portion of the test subject’s body, in a

02:43:33.211 --> 02:43:36.380
block of some unidentified clear substance.

02:43:36.380 --> 02:43:41.960
The body was divided in the lockers into these
separate parts: brain, lungs and diaphragm,

02:43:41.960 --> 02:43:47.590
heart, digestive system, reproductive organs,
left eye, right eye, upper left torso and

02:43:47.590 --> 02:43:52.060
arm, upper right torso and arm, lower left
torso and upper leg, lower right torso and

02:43:52.060 --> 02:43:57.359
upper leg, lower left leg and foot, lower
right leg and foot, lower left arm and hand,

02:43:57.359 --> 02:44:02.500
lower right arm and hand, neck and head, upper
skeletal system, lower skeletal system, lymphatic

02:44:02.500 --> 02:44:05.460
and circulatory system, and skin.

02:44:05.460 --> 02:44:08.300
Phew, the miracle of the human body, right?

02:44:08.300 --> 02:44:11.250
Boundless in its fascinating complexities...

02:44:11.250 --> 02:44:15.641
Each block of body parts was placed back in
its designated locker, and the second button

02:44:15.641 --> 02:44:17.149
on the console was pressed.

02:44:17.149 --> 02:44:21.500
At this point, the doors to the organ lockers
sealed themselves shut, and the sound of the

02:44:21.500 --> 02:44:24.700
machinery working filled the small space once
again.

02:44:24.700 --> 02:44:28.470
This continued for a duration of approximately
45 minutes.

02:44:28.470 --> 02:44:34.050
When the machinery went silent, a new plexiglass
coffin emerged into the main room, with the

02:44:34.050 --> 02:44:35.439
test subject inside.

02:44:35.439 --> 02:44:39.450
He looked identical to how he had looked at
the start of the experiment, with no evidence

02:44:39.450 --> 02:44:41.870
that he had previously been disassembled.

02:44:41.870 --> 02:44:46.660
The blue liquid slowly evaporated from the
container, and the test subject opened his

02:44:46.660 --> 02:44:47.680
eyes.

02:44:47.680 --> 02:44:52.020
The lead researcher conducted an immediate
interview with the reassembled subject, who

02:44:52.020 --> 02:44:56.120
reported no memory of the process after initial
exposure to the blue liquid.

02:44:56.120 --> 02:45:00.650
They insisted that the process had been like
a good night’s sleep - which honestly makes

02:45:00.650 --> 02:45:02.899
us pretty eager to take it for a spin.

02:45:02.899 --> 02:45:07.149
A medical examination determined that there
were only a few changes to the test subject

02:45:07.149 --> 02:45:12.460
during the disassembly and reassembly: when
they returned to consciousness, the test subject’s

02:45:12.460 --> 02:45:16.890
stomach was empty, they were naked, and all
of their hair was gone.

02:45:16.890 --> 02:45:21.960
With this new understanding of SCP-291’s
anomalous properties, the Foundation decided

02:45:21.960 --> 02:45:24.189
to continue their experimentation.

02:45:24.189 --> 02:45:30.609
With each new test, the experiments became
more creative, and unsurprisingly, more depraved.

02:45:30.609 --> 02:45:34.800
First, a D-Class subject was placed in the
coffin and disassembled.

02:45:34.800 --> 02:45:38.950
Then, instead of placing the various body
parts in their designated lockers, the vital

02:45:38.950 --> 02:45:43.120
organs were removed from their storage before
reassembly was attempted.

02:45:43.120 --> 02:45:45.840
This resulted in the equipment shutting down
completely.

02:45:45.840 --> 02:45:51.100
A researcher pressed the third button, which
forced a hard reset of the entire process,

02:45:51.100 --> 02:45:54.670
causing all of the blocks of body parts to
eject via an exit hatch.

02:45:54.670 --> 02:46:00.230
During the next experiment, non-vital organs
were removed before the subject’s body was

02:46:00.230 --> 02:46:01.230
reassembled.

02:46:01.230 --> 02:46:05.140
The appendix and gallbladder were left out,
and when the subject regained consciousness,

02:46:05.140 --> 02:46:06.930
these organs were still gone.

02:46:06.930 --> 02:46:10.740
However, there was no visible damage or scar
tissue in their place.

02:46:10.740 --> 02:46:14.500
They were simply gone, as if they had never
been there in the first place.

02:46:14.500 --> 02:46:19.920
So, if body parts could be removed from a
test subject, could new body parts be added?

02:46:19.920 --> 02:46:22.810
Could existing body parts be replaced with
different ones?

02:46:22.810 --> 02:46:27.110
A D-class subject in need of a skin graft
following a flamethrower-based accident was

02:46:27.110 --> 02:46:29.819
placed in SCP-291.

02:46:29.819 --> 02:46:35.270
Once taken apart, a portion of healthy skin
donated by another, somewhat unwilling, D-class

02:46:35.270 --> 02:46:39.430
subject was placed in the locker along with
the skin already present there.

02:46:39.430 --> 02:46:43.510
Once the subject was put back together, the
healthy skin had replaced the damaged skin

02:46:43.510 --> 02:46:45.750
with no adverse effects.

02:46:45.750 --> 02:46:50.700
Repeat attempts at this test showed it was
effective for limb transplants, heart transplants,

02:46:50.700 --> 02:46:55.729
and kidney transplants, with a 0 percent failure
rate across all tests.

02:46:55.729 --> 02:47:00.710
After determining that SCP-291 could be used
for an untold amount of good, making organ

02:47:00.710 --> 02:47:05.420
donations easier and safer than ever, the
Foundation naturally had to pivot to something

02:47:05.420 --> 02:47:09.470
more useless but interesting and likely horrifying.

02:47:09.470 --> 02:47:13.300
After all, it’s not like they could ever
just make anomalous technology available to

02:47:13.300 --> 02:47:14.311
the public.

02:47:14.311 --> 02:47:20.370
Two D-class subjects, one man and one woman,
were disassembled by SCP-291.

02:47:20.370 --> 02:47:24.380
The brains of the test subjects were swapped,
and then they were reassembled.

02:47:24.380 --> 02:47:28.390
When they awoke, the subjects had the personalities
and memories of the brain placed in their

02:47:28.390 --> 02:47:29.390
body.

02:47:29.390 --> 02:47:33.620
In a turn of events previously only seen in
blockbuster comedies like Freaky Friday and

02:47:33.620 --> 02:47:39.260
the live-action Scooby-Doo movie, the subjects
had swapped bodies.

02:47:39.260 --> 02:47:43.660
They were subsequently disassembled - their
requests to look at their new bodies naked

02:47:43.660 --> 02:47:48.890
having been swiftly denied - and the brains
were returned to their rightful bodies.

02:47:48.890 --> 02:47:52.609
After the experiment was finished, the subjects
appeared mostly normal.

02:47:52.609 --> 02:47:56.850
However, they did complain of disorientation
as well as mental and physical discomfort

02:47:56.850 --> 02:47:58.910
over the next several days.

02:47:58.910 --> 02:48:02.700
After going through two brain transplants
in one day, though, that’s really the least

02:48:02.700 --> 02:48:04.300
you can expect.

02:48:04.300 --> 02:48:08.520
After perfecting the practice of swapping
body parts between different human subjects,

02:48:08.520 --> 02:48:14.160
the ghoulishly curious research team decided
to take things in an interspecies direction.

02:48:14.160 --> 02:48:20.330
A variety of test subjects, including cats,
dogs, lizards, fish, mice, and of course,

02:48:20.330 --> 02:48:23.670
humans, were selected for this next round
of experimentation.

02:48:23.670 --> 02:48:28.479
Twenty tests were performed using these new
subjects, and only three of the experiments

02:48:28.479 --> 02:48:33.450
were successful in transferring body parts
from an animal of one species to another animal

02:48:33.450 --> 02:48:35.109
of a different one.

02:48:35.109 --> 02:48:39.311
Attempts to swap body parts between mammals
and reptiles or fish proved disastrous.

02:48:39.311 --> 02:48:44.210
When a fish and a human were both disassembled,
and the fish’s gills were placed with the

02:48:44.210 --> 02:48:48.620
human’s body parts, neither creature survived
the reassembly process.

02:48:48.620 --> 02:48:53.350
The human awoke, with a new set of gills embedded
in their neck, and immediately began gasping

02:48:53.350 --> 02:48:55.920
for the oxygen they could not take in.

02:48:55.920 --> 02:48:58.180
Within minutes, they had suffocated.

02:48:58.180 --> 02:48:59.950
The fish’s fate was even worse.

02:48:59.950 --> 02:49:06.170
It did not reassemble so much as it became
a pile of goo, scales, and two floating eyeballs.

02:49:06.170 --> 02:49:10.229
Experimentation with a human and a lizard
yielded similar results, turning the lizard

02:49:10.229 --> 02:49:15.780
into a puddle of organic matter and killing
the human test subject after only a few moments.

02:49:15.780 --> 02:49:20.239
As disastrous as the failed cross-species
tests were, the successful ones were almost

02:49:20.239 --> 02:49:21.239
as bad.

02:49:21.239 --> 02:49:24.240
Trial 001 involved a cat and a human.

02:49:24.240 --> 02:49:29.790
Not wanting to attempt too much at once, the
research team opted to just swap out one organ:

02:49:29.790 --> 02:49:31.149
the left eye.

02:49:31.149 --> 02:49:35.060
Both subjects survived this transfer and were
able to use their new eye.

02:49:35.060 --> 02:49:39.470
The human subject reported full use of the
cat eye, with improved night vision in addition

02:49:39.470 --> 02:49:41.149
to trouble seeing color.

02:49:41.149 --> 02:49:45.680
The cat did not enjoy its new eye nearly as
much as the human subject, and had clawed

02:49:45.680 --> 02:49:49.550
its human eye out of its head by the end of
the following week.

02:49:49.550 --> 02:49:55.000
In trial 007, a successful brain transfer
was performed between an adult human man and

02:49:55.000 --> 02:49:56.489
an English mastiff.

02:49:56.489 --> 02:50:00.660
The man in the mastiff’s body expressed
discomfort with walking on all fours, and

02:50:00.660 --> 02:50:03.319
asked to be returned to his body as soon as
possible.

02:50:03.319 --> 02:50:08.050
The mastiff in the man’s body adjusted to
bipedal locomotion in a few hours, but was

02:50:08.050 --> 02:50:11.339
disassembled after urinating on a researcher’s
shoes.

02:50:11.339 --> 02:50:15.609
The final successful trial, and the most unnerving,
was trial 016.

02:50:15.609 --> 02:50:21.050
A female D-class test subject’s reproductive
organs were swapped with those of a pregnant

02:50:21.050 --> 02:50:22.550
Labrador retriever.

02:50:22.550 --> 02:50:26.830
An ultrasound conducted after the transfer
indicated that the Labrador fetuses survived

02:50:26.830 --> 02:50:31.950
the procedure, and could conceivably be carried
to term by the human subject.

02:50:31.950 --> 02:50:35.240
Several members of the research team began
to take bets on whether or not she would end

02:50:35.240 --> 02:50:40.251
up giving birth to puppies, but the transfer
was reversed within the day, so we’ll never

02:50:40.251 --> 02:50:42.689
know what exactly would have happened.

02:50:42.689 --> 02:50:44.120
Perhaps that’s for the best.

02:50:44.120 --> 02:50:48.060
Personally, we hope the Foundation’s Ethics
Committee gives some of these scientists a

02:50:48.060 --> 02:50:51.810
very stern talking to about their behavior
on this one.

02:50:51.810 --> 02:50:57.470
When not in use for testing, SCP-291 is to
be disconnected from any power sources.

02:50:57.470 --> 02:51:02.390
At least two personnel are positioned outside
of its containment at all times, standing

02:51:02.390 --> 02:51:05.460
guard, and these personnel must be swapped
out every week.

02:51:05.460 --> 02:51:11.359
When it is not connected to any power sources,
SCP-291 is considered harmless, though it

02:51:11.359 --> 02:51:13.260
should still be treated with caution.

02:51:13.260 --> 02:51:18.000
The main entryway remains closed and locked
when there is no available power source, but

02:51:18.000 --> 02:51:22.750
the door can be opened manually from the inside
in the event of an emergency.

02:51:22.750 --> 02:51:27.310
Any disassembled organisms are stored in a
locker in the containment facility, labeled

02:51:27.310 --> 02:51:31.620
with a sharpie marker in order to keep track
of what specimens are stored where.

02:51:31.620 --> 02:51:36.380
Whether this is the same sharpie used to label
food in the break room fridge is unknown,

02:51:36.380 --> 02:51:41.859
but just like Dr. DiRamio’s ham sandwich,
it’s best to leave these items untouched.

02:51:41.859 --> 02:51:45.920
Any personnel found to be responsible for
missing specimens will be transferred to another

02:51:45.920 --> 02:51:48.940
project, and receive a strongly worded email.

02:51:48.940 --> 02:51:52.170
Hey, do you have a favorite reality show?

02:51:52.170 --> 02:51:55.240
Oh come on, don't lie, everyone has one.

02:51:55.240 --> 02:51:59.819
Dr. Clef loves some American Ninja Warrior,
and I’ve got it on good authority that Dr.

02:51:59.819 --> 02:52:03.250
Bright can’t get enough of The Bachelor,
so how about you, huh?

02:52:03.250 --> 02:52:07.780
Do you obsessively follow the romantic highs
and lows of Love Island, or are you more the

02:52:07.780 --> 02:52:12.510
type who likes to curl up with a mug of hot
cocoa and enjoy a nice, wholesome episode

02:52:12.510 --> 02:52:14.670
of The Great British Baking Show?

02:52:14.670 --> 02:52:19.210
Do you ever yell at the TV when the contestants
on Jeopardy just can't get the answer right?

02:52:19.210 --> 02:52:23.670
Do you get a kick out of seeing what crazy
collectibles will show up on this week's episode

02:52:23.670 --> 02:52:25.210
of Pawn Stars?

02:52:25.210 --> 02:52:30.010
If you answered yes to any of these, you're
not alone - Millions of people around the

02:52:30.010 --> 02:52:33.630
world still tune in to all kinds of reality
TV.

02:52:33.630 --> 02:52:38.110
Personally, I just can't get enough of my
favorite hidden camera show: Laugh is Fun.

02:52:38.110 --> 02:52:39.320
What's that?

02:52:39.320 --> 02:52:42.120
You've never heard of Laugh is Fun?

02:52:42.120 --> 02:52:45.250
Oh, boy.

02:52:45.250 --> 02:52:46.800
You're really missing out.

02:52:46.800 --> 02:52:51.760
If you like reality TV, you're gonna love
Laugh is Fun.

02:52:51.760 --> 02:52:56.899
Laugh is Fun, also known as SCP-2030, isn't
a show that you can watch on TV.

02:52:56.899 --> 02:53:02.069
Instead, it appears as the most popular form
of media distribution in the current year.

02:53:02.069 --> 02:53:07.130
Today, you can find it on file-sharing and
streaming websites, but in the 2000's, you

02:53:07.130 --> 02:53:11.720
could rent it from the DVD kiosk at the mall,
and back in the ‘90s, it used to show up

02:53:11.720 --> 02:53:15.170
as multi-tape sets in video rental stores.

02:53:15.170 --> 02:53:20.591
Even though the SCP foundation has only been
aware of Laugh is Fun since 1993, it has a

02:53:20.591 --> 02:53:27.050
recorded 38 seasons as of 2014, meaning that
it may have existed in some form as far back

02:53:27.050 --> 02:53:29.130
as the 1970s.

