As we were saying,
Laugh is Fun is a prank show that puts unknowing

02:55:22.070 --> 02:55:26.550
everyday people into ridiculous scenarios
and films their reactions.

02:55:26.550 --> 02:55:31.640
Each episode is about 10 to 12 minutes long
and features an opening and closing monologue

02:55:31.640 --> 02:55:39.330
from beloved, supposedly human TV presenter
Laughy McLaugherson, aka SCP-2030-1.

02:55:39.330 --> 02:55:44.420
You've probably seen him before, he's never
seen without his blue three-piece suit and

02:55:44.420 --> 02:55:46.610
black wing-tipped shoes.

02:55:46.610 --> 02:55:50.690
Funniest guy on TV, seriously, I think he
should replace James Corden on the Late Late

02:55:50.690 --> 02:55:51.690
Show.

02:55:51.690 --> 02:55:56.359
And maybe even take up a hosting gig on SNL,
if he’s still got time after.

02:55:56.359 --> 02:56:00.220
He had this amazing monologue at the end of
an episode in season 32.

02:56:00.220 --> 02:56:01.220
“Ha!

02:56:01.220 --> 02:56:02.520
What a ride, eh, folks?

02:56:02.520 --> 02:56:05.800
We've seen printers that eat, eaters that
print, and everything in between!

02:56:05.800 --> 02:56:09.540
Makes you appreciate the old clunker you have
back the office, doesn't it?

02:56:09.540 --> 02:56:13.489
No, printers may not always work when you
want or need them to, but they sure make for

02:56:13.489 --> 02:56:15.590
some excellent comedy.

02:56:15.590 --> 02:56:16.842
And that's what we're about here: comedy.

02:56:16.842 --> 02:56:19.560
We're here to make you laugh.

02:56:19.560 --> 02:56:20.580
We hope you laughed.

02:56:20.580 --> 02:56:22.450
Thank you for laughing with us.

02:56:22.450 --> 02:56:24.479
That's what we're about here, doesn't it,
folks?

02:56:24.479 --> 02:56:26.170
Come laugh with us again next time!

02:56:26.170 --> 02:56:29.020
And remember: LAUGH … IS … FUN!

02:56:29.020 --> 02:56:30.279
Good night!

02:56:30.279 --> 02:56:31.540
And laugh!

02:56:31.540 --> 02:56:32.800
And laugh!

02:56:32.800 --> 02:56:33.800
Just laugh!

02:56:33.800 --> 02:56:34.902
We love the make laugh.

02:56:34.902 --> 02:56:37.410
Make more for laughter so as to for laugh.

02:56:37.410 --> 02:56:38.410
Laugh with us.

02:56:38.410 --> 02:56:39.410
Laugh with us.

02:56:39.410 --> 02:56:40.410
Laugh with us!

02:56:40.410 --> 02:56:41.410
Laugh with us!

02:56:41.410 --> 02:56:42.410
Laugh with us!

02:56:42.410 --> 02:56:43.520
Laugh with us!

02:56:43.520 --> 02:56:44.520
Laugh!

02:56:44.520 --> 02:56:45.520
Laugh!

02:56:45.520 --> 02:56:46.520
Laugh and let us in!”

02:56:46.520 --> 02:56:47.520
Hmmm.

02:56:47.520 --> 02:56:50.960
I couldn't tell you what his face looks like,
though, because he's always framed from the

02:56:50.960 --> 02:56:52.160
neck down.

02:56:52.160 --> 02:56:55.780
Once the pranks are done for the episode,
he'll step up on that bright yellow stage

02:56:55.780 --> 02:57:00.550
and deliver his closing monologue, which always
ends with a pan over the audience as everyone

02:57:00.550 --> 02:57:02.290
chants “Laugh with us!”

02:57:02.290 --> 02:57:05.350
Then the show always just cuts to black.

02:57:05.350 --> 02:57:10.010
The closest thing the show ever has to credits
is a title card that says “Filmed in front

02:57:10.010 --> 02:57:15.260
of a studio audience in partnership with YWTGTHFT.”

02:57:15.260 --> 02:57:21.149
For a show that doesn't advertise or even
air on TV, Laugh is Fun is still a beloved

02:57:21.149 --> 02:57:25.120
classic, and when you watch it, it's easy
to see why it's been around so long.

02:57:25.120 --> 02:57:29.330
Laughy and the team pull off some really classic
pranks on Laugh is Laugh!

02:57:29.330 --> 02:57:33.001
There's this one episode in season 13, where
an unsuspecting family is sitting down to

02:57:33.001 --> 02:57:34.001
dinner.

02:57:34.001 --> 02:57:36.970
The father starts choking, and the family
reacts with horror, until suddenly a pair

02:57:36.970 --> 02:57:40.061
of slits appear on the father's neck, allowing
him to breathe.

02:57:40.061 --> 02:57:43.439
Those slits soon become nostrils, and before
you know it, a full second head grows out

02:57:43.439 --> 02:57:44.450
of his neck.

02:57:44.450 --> 02:57:48.460
That head then grows its own neck, which grows
a nose, then a face, then another head, then

02:57:48.460 --> 02:57:49.490
another neck.

02:57:49.490 --> 02:57:53.270
This keeps happening a total of 18 times while
the rest of the family looks on in horror.

02:57:53.270 --> 02:57:57.570
But don't worry, before things go too far,
Laughy pops out from under the table and tells

02:57:57.570 --> 02:57:59.060
the family that they're on Laugh is Fun.

02:57:59.060 --> 02:58:03.950
Laughy points out the cameras, and the whole
family starts laughing, including all 18 of

02:58:03.950 --> 02:58:05.330
the father's heads.

02:58:05.330 --> 02:58:08.660
There's another great season 13 episode called
“Squirrels.”

02:58:08.660 --> 02:58:11.939
Oh, man, that one had me in stitches!

02:58:11.939 --> 02:58:16.050
Alright, so there's this couple lying in bed,
and the wife wakes up because she hears this

02:58:16.050 --> 02:58:17.390
squeaking noise.

02:58:17.390 --> 02:58:21.250
She taps her husband on the shoulder to wake
him up, but she draws her hand back in horror

02:58:21.250 --> 02:58:24.950
because she can feel something moving under
her husband's skin.

02:58:24.950 --> 02:58:27.100
Before she can ask if he's okay, boom!

02:58:27.100 --> 02:58:30.490
Hundreds of squirrels explode out of his skin
and start running around the room while the

02:58:30.490 --> 02:58:31.569
wife screams.

02:58:31.569 --> 02:58:35.420
Then Laughy walks in and turns the lights
on, accompanied by the husband, who is perfectly

02:58:35.420 --> 02:58:38.470
okay even though he's been skinned from head
to toe.

02:58:38.470 --> 02:58:39.750
Everyone laughs.

02:58:39.750 --> 02:58:43.210
Then there's a more recent episode from season
24, called “Swelling.”

02:58:43.210 --> 02:58:46.880
There's this old lady sitting on a park bench,
feeding the pigeons, and a couple walks past

02:58:46.880 --> 02:58:47.880
her.

02:58:47.880 --> 02:58:50.609
While they walk past, the old lady gets swarmed
by the pigeons she's feeding.

02:58:50.609 --> 02:58:54.260
The pigeons force themselves into her mouth
and keep swarming until her stomach cavity

02:58:54.260 --> 02:58:55.330
bursts open.

02:58:55.330 --> 02:58:59.680
The couple, who get sprayed with guts as all
the pigeons fly off, are extremely distressed

02:58:59.680 --> 02:59:02.050
by this until Laughy shows up.

02:59:02.050 --> 02:59:05.990
Some people say that this episode is too similar
to Squirrels and that the show was starting

02:59:05.990 --> 02:59:10.590
to get stale at this point, but I think the
joke is unique enough to stand on its own.

02:59:10.590 --> 02:59:14.500
Plus, with a prank show as long-running as
Laugh, it's inevitable that you're gonna see

02:59:14.500 --> 02:59:16.200
some jokes get reused.

02:59:16.200 --> 02:59:20.720
Really, it's not about the prank itself, it's
about the reactions of the people, which are

02:59:20.720 --> 02:59:21.830
always priceless!

02:59:21.830 --> 02:59:25.399
And man, the way that Laughy McLaugherson
comes into the frame by climbing out of the

02:59:25.399 --> 02:59:26.739
old lady's open ribcage?

02:59:26.739 --> 02:59:28.979
I was rolling on the floor!

02:59:28.979 --> 02:59:33.340
Oh, you don't think the old “animals exploding
out of people” bit is funny?

02:59:33.340 --> 02:59:34.340
That's fair enough.

02:59:34.340 --> 02:59:38.180
Let me think - what are some of my other favorite
episodes of Laugh is Fun?

02:59:38.180 --> 02:59:41.670
Oh - the Margaret Thatcher episode from season
21!

02:59:41.670 --> 02:59:45.500
That's another great thing about Laugh is
Fun, it's not afraid to get a little political.

02:59:45.500 --> 02:59:49.700
So, this woman walks into her kitchen and
opens the cabinet, but instead of food being

02:59:49.700 --> 02:59:52.020
in there, it's just a big blob of flesh.

02:59:52.020 --> 02:59:55.450
The flesh blob rolls out onto the counter
and morphs into a misshapen caricature of

02:59:55.450 --> 02:59:58.359
Margaret Thatcher with a disproportionately
big head.

02:59:58.359 --> 03:00:01.780
The woman starts screaming, but the Thatcher
creature jumps onto her, pinning her down

03:00:01.780 --> 03:00:03.750
and shoving its tongue into her mouth.

03:00:03.750 --> 03:00:07.210
The deeper the tongue goes, the more Margaret
Thatcher faces start appearing all over the

03:00:07.210 --> 03:00:08.460
woman's skin.

03:00:08.460 --> 03:00:12.540
All of the faces start reciting Thatcher's
April 1986 speech on the bombing of Libya

03:00:12.540 --> 03:00:14.060
in perfect unison.

03:00:14.060 --> 03:00:17.150
You might watch it and think the woman's going
to choke based on how long the creature's

03:00:17.150 --> 03:00:22.500
tongue is down her throat, but good ol' Laughy
comes in, and the studio audience goes nuts!

03:00:22.500 --> 03:00:26.850
Laughy points out the cameras, says “You're
on Laugh is Fun!” and the woman starts laughing

03:00:26.850 --> 03:00:29.020
too, with the creature's tongue still in her
mouth.

03:00:29.020 --> 03:00:33.850
But I think my favorite prank I've ever seen
on Laugh is Fun was this one from season 37.

03:00:33.850 --> 03:00:35.430
So, it's in a hospital.

03:00:35.430 --> 03:00:38.880
There's a woman getting a c-section and all
the doctors are gathered around.

03:00:38.880 --> 03:00:42.569
One of the doctors makes a comment on how
much hair the baby has, then he screams and

03:00:42.569 --> 03:00:44.020
drops his surgical tools.

03:00:44.020 --> 03:00:47.370
The rest of the team all start screaming as
well, and then- this is where it gets really

03:00:47.370 --> 03:00:53.029
funny- you see Ryan Seacrest's head pop up
out from the woman.

03:00:53.029 --> 03:00:56.891
This is causing her a lot of pain, obviously,
so she starts screaming and crying as the

03:00:56.891 --> 03:01:01.680
Ryan Seacrest head fully emerges, at which
point you can tell that it's his head on an

03:01:01.680 --> 03:01:03.350
octopus' body!

03:01:03.350 --> 03:01:04.350
Classic bait-and-switch, right?

03:01:04.350 --> 03:01:09.120
But that's not the end- the Ryan Seacrest
octopus starts singing 'Row Row Row Your Boat'

03:01:09.120 --> 03:01:13.890
as it emerges, then three more octopi with
celebrities' heads come out of this woman.

03:01:13.890 --> 03:01:17.210
There's one that looks like Jack Nicholson,
one that looks like Johnny Cash, and one who

03:01:17.210 --> 03:01:21.130
looks like Martin Freeman, and when they've
all come out of her they start singing together

03:01:21.130 --> 03:01:22.620
in four-part harmony.

03:01:22.620 --> 03:01:23.739
It's hilarious!

03:01:23.739 --> 03:01:26.830
Laughy walks in to point out the cameras,
and all the doctors start laughing.

03:01:26.830 --> 03:01:29.150
Even the woman on the operating table is laughing.

03:01:29.150 --> 03:01:31.489
In fact, she laughs so hard she passes out!

03:01:31.489 --> 03:01:34.980
It's a real shame that there are never any
end credits because it would be so cool to

03:01:34.980 --> 03:01:37.040
find out more about the people who make this
show.

03:01:37.040 --> 03:01:41.130
I mean, they're total comedic geniuses, and
special effects wizards, too.

03:01:41.130 --> 03:01:43.779
I couldn't even guess how they do some of
those pranks!

03:01:43.779 --> 03:01:47.580
But sadly, there's very little information
about the show online, and you can't even

03:01:47.580 --> 03:01:51.439
ask the victims of the pranks about it, because
all of them are dead.

03:01:51.439 --> 03:01:52.439
What?

03:01:52.439 --> 03:01:54.520
No, no, not because of Laugh is Fun!

03:01:54.520 --> 03:01:56.569
That's just a prank show, it's all jokes.

03:01:56.569 --> 03:02:00.120
They always show everyone laughing and perfectly
okay at the end, no matter how badly they

03:02:00.120 --> 03:02:02.040
got mutilated in the episode.

03:02:02.040 --> 03:02:05.899
You can even see some people who had been
on previous episodes among the studio audience

03:02:05.899 --> 03:02:07.149
if you look hard enough!

03:02:07.149 --> 03:02:13.370
But, by total coincidence, everyone who features
on Laugh is Fun eventually dies, or is already

03:02:13.370 --> 03:02:16.060
dead, of totally unrelated causes.

03:02:16.060 --> 03:02:20.400
Like the Turman family- the dad, Gary Turman,
was the one who had 18 extra heads grow out

03:02:20.400 --> 03:02:21.400
of his neck.

03:02:21.400 --> 03:02:25.460
Gary, his wife Lindsey, and their two kids
tragically passed away in a car wreck on the

03:02:25.460 --> 03:02:27.660
28th of April, 1989.

03:02:27.660 --> 03:02:31.700
Melissa and Travis Englund- the couple from
the squirrel prank went missing and were last

03:02:31.700 --> 03:02:34.189
seen on the 12th of May, 1989.

03:02:34.189 --> 03:02:38.630
The couple from the pigeon prank- Macey Gersham
and Kyle Parker- were both killed by a hit

03:02:38.630 --> 03:02:40.580
and run driver in September of 2000.

03:02:40.580 --> 03:02:44.620
Doris Carter, the woman from the Thatcher
prank, passed away from ovarian cancer in

03:02:44.620 --> 03:02:49.609
1997, and Rebecca Nash, the woman who gave
birth to all those singing celebrity cephalopods,

03:02:49.609 --> 03:02:52.340
died in childbirth in 2013.

03:02:52.340 --> 03:02:56.720
You might think that last one had something
to do with her Laugh is Fun episode, due to

03:02:56.720 --> 03:03:00.700
the hospital connection, but the surgeons
present when she died didn't report anything

03:03:00.700 --> 03:03:02.640
strange happening at the time.

03:03:02.640 --> 03:03:06.229
All of these deaths happen in roughly the
same years that all of these people had their

03:03:06.229 --> 03:03:11.149
appearances on Laugh, but because it's only
available on streaming and video, it can't

03:03:11.149 --> 03:03:15.970
really be said what the connection is since
there aren't air dates for any of the episodes.

03:03:15.970 --> 03:03:20.109
While you might assume that these people died
after their appearances on Laugh, and the

03:03:20.109 --> 03:03:24.770
show is actually some kind of death curse,
it's just as likely that they died before,

03:03:24.770 --> 03:03:28.720
and Laugh is Fun is somehow filmed and distributed
from the great beyond.

03:03:28.720 --> 03:03:32.649
Some people even think that the people who
film Laugh actually kidnap all the people

03:03:32.649 --> 03:03:37.090
who appear on the show and fake their deaths
in some kind of big sinister conspiracy.

03:03:37.090 --> 03:03:41.971
Sure, I have heard that all of the people
who supposedly 'died' after being on the show

03:03:41.971 --> 03:03:46.380
have inconsistencies in their death records
and that many of their graves actually just

03:03:46.380 --> 03:03:50.660
hold empty coffins, but still, that feels
totally unrealistic to me.

03:03:50.660 --> 03:03:55.420
I mean, come on, can you really picture TV's
own Laughy Laugherson kidnapping anyone?

03:03:55.420 --> 03:03:57.870
He has such a friendly attitude!

03:03:57.870 --> 03:04:03.170
Like I said before, no information whatsoever
exists about the way this show is made.

03:04:03.170 --> 03:04:07.590
Not even the SCP foundation has any answers
- they're still actively investigating the

03:04:07.590 --> 03:04:12.280
ways in which people get chosen to be on Laugh
is Fun, as well as where it's filmed, and

03:04:12.280 --> 03:04:13.649
who produces it.

03:04:13.649 --> 03:04:15.520
Talk about a really niche cult hit!

03:04:15.520 --> 03:04:17.700
I hope I've sold you on Laugh is Fun.

03:04:17.700 --> 03:04:22.630
It may not be that well known, and you might
have trouble finding it, but trust me- it's

03:04:22.630 --> 03:04:25.239
the funniest prank show you'll probably ever
watch.

03:04:25.239 --> 03:04:30.279
I guarantee, once you get into it, it'll make
you laugh, and laugh, and laugh.

03:04:30.279 --> 03:04:31.620
Laugh with us!

03:04:31.620 --> 03:04:32.790
Laugh with us!

03:04:32.790 --> 03:04:34.170
Laugh with us!

03:04:34.170 --> 03:04:35.600
Laugh with us!

03:04:35.600 --> 03:04:42.109
On April 16th, 1999, the Raleigh Ripper was
finally brought to justice, after a reign

03:04:42.109 --> 03:04:46.950
of terror across the state of North Carolina
that left fourteen women dead.

03:04:46.950 --> 03:04:52.529
The killer’s true identity had been Kevin
Gruber, a local gas station attendant originally

03:04:52.529 --> 03:04:57.529
from West Virginia, who was arrested at work
in the early hours of the morning.

03:04:57.529 --> 03:05:02.779
His face was plastered all over the media
when he was cuffed and dragged in to be questioned

03:05:02.779 --> 03:05:04.279
and processed.

03:05:04.279 --> 03:05:09.239
Like many serial killers, the most frightening
thing about Kevin was the fact that he just

03:05:09.239 --> 03:05:11.640
seemed so...normal.

03:05:11.640 --> 03:05:16.430
The idea that a person like this could have
committed the atrocities of the Raleigh Ripper

03:05:16.430 --> 03:05:20.580
raised a frightening question we all need
to contend with.

03:05:20.580 --> 03:05:24.010
What turns a person into a monster?

03:05:24.010 --> 03:05:29.340
This question was particularly prescient for
Dr. James Whitington, a criminal psychologist

03:05:29.340 --> 03:05:33.930
tasked with conducting the first official
psychological evaluation on Gruber.

03:05:33.930 --> 03:05:38.970
Ever since the true identity of the killer
had come to light, the case had held a particular

03:05:38.970 --> 03:05:40.960
fascination for him.

03:05:40.960 --> 03:05:46.790
Mainly because Gruber The Man and Gruber The
Killer seemed to almost be two entirely separate

03:05:46.790 --> 03:05:47.790
people.

03:05:47.790 --> 03:05:53.390
According to all evidence, The Raleigh Ripper
was an insidious, methodical criminal genius.

03:05:53.390 --> 03:05:59.649
He’d stalked some of his victims - all women
who lived alone - for weeks before striking,

03:05:59.649 --> 03:06:04.310
conducting detailed surveillance of their
homes that allowed him to isolate them, bypass

03:06:04.310 --> 03:06:08.910
their security systems, and remove any means
of getting help.

03:06:08.910 --> 03:06:14.120
He blocked doors, cut phone lines, and always
selected vulnerable targets.

03:06:14.120 --> 03:06:19.109
Despite being a seasoned criminal psychologist,
the actual details of Gruber’s crimes had

03:06:19.109 --> 03:06:20.640
kept Whitington awake at night.

03:06:20.640 --> 03:06:24.890
He had a wife and a young son at home, and
the thought of a man like Gruber prowling

03:06:24.890 --> 03:06:27.620
out there made him fear for both of them.

03:06:27.620 --> 03:06:33.601
This was no thrill killer - He was a sadistic
torturer, who seemed to delight in the pain

03:06:33.601 --> 03:06:35.470
and terror of his prey.

03:06:35.470 --> 03:06:38.890
He’d chosen victims he could take his time
with.

03:06:38.890 --> 03:06:43.229
Infiltrated their homes like a gust of cold
air through an open window and slipped out

03:06:43.229 --> 03:06:45.710
through darkness like a shadow.

03:06:45.710 --> 03:06:47.910
Perfectly controlled crime scenes.

03:06:47.910 --> 03:06:49.790
No stray evidence.

03:06:49.790 --> 03:06:52.260
Nothing but death left behind.

03:06:52.260 --> 03:06:54.700
For months, he’d run circles around the
police.

03:06:54.700 --> 03:06:58.819
Thousands of people who fit the Raleigh Ripper
profile were interviewed.

03:06:58.819 --> 03:07:01.021
Sting operations were conducted.

03:07:01.021 --> 03:07:05.080
Communities formed neighborhood watches to
keep each other safe from the killer’s next

03:07:05.080 --> 03:07:06.080
move.

03:07:06.080 --> 03:07:07.900
And none of it did any good.

03:07:07.900 --> 03:07:14.120
From seasoned detectives to legions of beat
cops, nobody could get the jump on Kevin Gruber.

03:07:14.120 --> 03:07:19.890
The fact he was even caught came out of pure
chance: A local hiker, Mike Fletcher, just

03:07:19.890 --> 03:07:24.700
so happened to hear the screaming coming from
a nearby home in the woods and made the heroic

03:07:24.700 --> 03:07:27.610
decision to run in and intervene.

03:07:27.610 --> 03:07:32.109
When he walked in on Gruber committing the
attack, the killer panicked, and fled through

03:07:32.109 --> 03:07:33.540
an open window.

03:07:33.540 --> 03:07:36.800
In his haste, he’d left a partial print
on the window frame.

03:07:36.800 --> 03:07:41.220
That, combined with Mike’s description of
the assailant, was enough to finally link

03:07:41.220 --> 03:07:44.630
Kevin to the fourteen murders of the Raleigh
Ripper.

03:07:44.630 --> 03:07:50.021
The problem, from Dr. Whitington’s perspective,
was that, by all accounts, Kevin Gruber seemed

03:07:50.021 --> 03:07:51.319
to be an idiot.

03:07:51.319 --> 03:07:54.390
This was no suave, charismatic Ted Bundy type.

03:07:54.390 --> 03:07:59.040
In all the prior photos and interviews, Kevin
had that deer-in-the-headlights look of a

03:07:59.040 --> 03:08:01.870
man who’s just in way over his head.

03:08:01.870 --> 03:08:05.610
Dr. Whitington had also pored over Kevin’s
school records.

03:08:05.610 --> 03:08:08.830
The only thing he seemed to excel at was being
mediocre.

03:08:08.830 --> 03:08:11.650
He even got held back a year in fifth grade.

03:08:11.650 --> 03:08:15.641
Since graduating high school, he’d been
kicked out by his parents for freeloading,

03:08:15.641 --> 03:08:19.700
and hadn’t been able to consistently hold
down a job for more than eight months.

03:08:19.700 --> 03:08:25.271
His only prior criminal convictions had been
one drunk and disorderly conduct charge, and

03:08:25.271 --> 03:08:30.561
possession of an ounce of pot back in 1991,
for which he got a suspended sentence due

03:08:30.561 --> 03:08:32.470
to being a minor at the time.

03:08:32.470 --> 03:08:38.050
It just didn’t make sense to Dr. Whitington
that this man and the diabolically brilliant

03:08:38.050 --> 03:08:43.779
Raleigh Ripper were the same person, despite
all the incontrovertible evidence proving

03:08:43.779 --> 03:08:45.229
it so.

03:08:45.229 --> 03:08:50.360
Despite his reservations, he needed to meet
this man, and find out why and how he committed

03:08:50.360 --> 03:08:55.979
all these horrific murders, despite being
such an unremarkable individual.

03:08:55.979 --> 03:09:00.399
Sitting across from Gruber in the secure interview
chamber, Whitington was once again struck

03:09:00.399 --> 03:09:03.680
with how incredibly disappointing he was.

03:09:03.680 --> 03:09:08.570
Thin and wiry, with glazed-over eyes, messy
hair, and a pathetic tuft of weak stubble

03:09:08.570 --> 03:09:09.570
on his chin.

03:09:09.570 --> 03:09:14.109
He looked more like Shaggy from Scooby-Doo
than a cold-blooded killer.

03:09:14.109 --> 03:09:18.930
His answers to most of Dr. Whitington’s
questions were also insubstantial - with him

03:09:18.930 --> 03:09:23.910
often losing his train of thought, or even
needing to ask the psychologist to carefully

03:09:23.910 --> 03:09:26.181
explain the question to him.

03:09:26.181 --> 03:09:30.860
Most of the time, Gruber tried to make irritating,
slow-motion small talk, concerning everything

03:09:30.860 --> 03:09:33.300
from the weather to movies he enjoyed.

03:09:33.300 --> 03:09:36.170
The interview had been utterly worthless.

03:09:36.170 --> 03:09:43.040
Until, four hours in, Gruber mentioned something
that awakened a strange memory in Dr. Whitington.

03:09:43.040 --> 03:09:47.851
He said, “Say, Doc, you remember that TV
show, Bobble the Clown?

03:09:47.851 --> 03:09:49.490
I loved that show as a kid.

03:09:49.490 --> 03:09:50.750
It was like my religion.

03:09:50.750 --> 03:09:52.370
Your kid ever watch it?”

03:09:52.370 --> 03:09:57.030
There were a number of unsettling things about
this, from the fact that, for some reason,

03:09:57.030 --> 03:10:01.660
Dr. Whitington could remember something about
Bobble the Clown, to the fact that Kevin Gruber

03:10:01.660 --> 03:10:05.540
had no way of knowing that Dr. Whitington
even had a kid.

03:10:05.540 --> 03:10:10.300
But still, he didn’t let his concern show
and instead asked Gruber what he remembered

03:10:10.300 --> 03:10:11.430
about Bobble the Clown.

03:10:11.430 --> 03:10:15.400
Gruber smiled, and replied: “Bobble taught
me everything I know, Doc.”

03:10:15.400 --> 03:10:19.040
To which Dr. Whitington asked the million-dollar
question, “Like what, Kevin?”

03:10:19.040 --> 03:10:22.480
Gruber shrugged and said, “All kinds of
stuff, Doc.

03:10:22.480 --> 03:10:24.729
Like how to watch without being seen.

03:10:24.729 --> 03:10:27.450
How to jimmy open a window without making
a sound.

03:10:27.450 --> 03:10:32.130
How to make ‘em hurt real bad without ‘em
dying, see, so you can make it last longer.

03:10:32.130 --> 03:10:33.819
So it can be more fun.

03:10:33.819 --> 03:10:37.450
And of course, he taught me to get out without
leaving anything behind.

03:10:37.450 --> 03:10:38.820
Bobble made all this possible, Doc.

03:10:38.820 --> 03:10:41.090
And he told me all about you, too.

03:10:41.090 --> 03:10:43.080
That all this was gonna happen someday.

03:10:43.080 --> 03:10:45.939
All good things have to come to an end eventually,
right?

03:10:45.939 --> 03:10:49.010
Tell the wife and kid he says hi, by the way.”

03:10:49.010 --> 03:10:50.760
Dr. Whitington was astounded.

03:10:50.760 --> 03:10:55.710
Gruber seemed to stare vacantly off into space
for a moment, before suddenly claiming that

03:10:55.710 --> 03:10:59.450
he had a terrible headache, and he needed
to go back to his cell.

03:10:59.450 --> 03:11:03.319
In any other situation, Whitington might have
just written off “Bobble the Clown” as

03:11:03.319 --> 03:11:08.960
one of two things - A psychotic delusion,
or a sophisticated psychopath faking a psychotic

03:11:08.960 --> 03:11:12.561
delusion in hopes of getting the insanity
plea.

03:11:12.561 --> 03:11:17.420
Like the Son of Sam Killer, David Berkowitz,
pretending a demonic talking dog possessed

03:11:17.420 --> 03:11:20.570
by Satan made him commit all of his murders.

03:11:20.570 --> 03:11:25.229
But Whitington had heard of this Bobble the
Clown before, and it wasn’t in a scenario

03:11:25.229 --> 03:11:29.020
that a gas station clerk like Kevin Gruber
ever would have heard of.

03:11:29.020 --> 03:11:33.370
It took half a day of research into his own
archived notes to remember exactly where he’d

03:11:33.370 --> 03:11:38.880
heard it before: A child he’d interviewed
almost a decade ago, who’d shoved gasoline

03:11:38.880 --> 03:11:43.689
and fireworks through the letterbox of an
old woman’s home, leading to a fire that

03:11:43.689 --> 03:11:46.070
left the woman and her dog dead.

03:11:46.070 --> 03:11:50.250
When Dr. Whitington interviewed the crying
child about his motives, he’d said that

03:11:50.250 --> 03:11:55.479
it wasn’t his fault; Bobble the Clown had
told him to do it on the TV.

03:11:55.479 --> 03:12:00.100
Given that there were no records of a Bobble
the Clown show ever airing on any local networks,

03:12:00.100 --> 03:12:05.460
Whitington had written it off at the time
as the overactive imagination of a very frightened,

03:12:05.460 --> 03:12:07.939
very disturbed young child.

03:12:07.939 --> 03:12:12.979
That same child would later go into psychiatric
care, before reoffending as a serial arsonist

03:12:12.979 --> 03:12:14.340
upon release.

03:12:14.340 --> 03:12:20.120
The last building he ever burned down had
only one occupant: Himself.

03:12:20.120 --> 03:12:24.890
Fire investigators would later state that
he just sat there, legs crossed, placidly

03:12:24.890 --> 03:12:28.310
waiting for the flames to lick his bones clean.

03:12:28.310 --> 03:12:32.590
It was becoming incredibly clear that this
“Bobble the Clown” fantasy - if it were

03:12:32.590 --> 03:12:37.120
even a fantasy at all - seemed to be much
more than an isolated phenomenon.

03:12:37.120 --> 03:12:41.830
He used his credentials to start exploring
other strange crimes of passion committed

03:12:41.830 --> 03:12:46.490
by children and young adults, even asking
some of his friends in the criminal psychology

03:12:46.490 --> 03:12:51.490
community - off the record - if they’d ever
heard of such a concept before.

03:12:51.490 --> 03:12:56.069
Frighteningly, it didn’t take Dr. Whitington
very long at all to hit paydirt.

03:12:56.069 --> 03:13:01.239
There was the case of the Orfeo Family Murders
in 1985, out in Arkansas.

03:13:01.239 --> 03:13:06.790
Nine-year-old Donnie Orfeo had taken his dad’s
rifle out of the cabinet in the dead of night,

03:13:06.790 --> 03:13:12.529
and walked room to room, shooting his mother,
father, and two older sisters in their beds.

03:13:12.529 --> 03:13:15.180
Neighbors had heard the gunshots and called
the police.

03:13:15.180 --> 03:13:20.649
By the time they arrived at the scene, the
only survivor was Donnie Orfeo himself, drenched

03:13:20.649 --> 03:13:23.140
in blood, sitting in front of the TV.

03:13:23.140 --> 03:13:26.290
His hollow eyes stared, zombie-like, into
the static.

03:13:26.290 --> 03:13:28.561
He did not resist arrest.

03:13:28.561 --> 03:13:33.080
When Donnie was taken in for questioning,
his emotional responses were cold and flat.

03:13:33.080 --> 03:13:38.000
When he was asked why he murdered his family,
he said that it was because his father told

03:13:38.000 --> 03:13:40.470
him he was watching too much TV.

03:13:40.470 --> 03:13:45.230
His favorite TV character, Bobble the Clown,
had told him that if he murdered his family

03:13:45.230 --> 03:13:50.130
with daddy’s gun, he could watch as much
TV as he liked.

03:13:50.130 --> 03:13:54.120
Just reading this, Dr. Whitington could feel
sweat beading on his brow.

03:13:54.120 --> 03:13:58.000
Two cases were a coincidence, but three were
a pattern.

03:13:58.000 --> 03:14:02.819
And oh, how he wished it had stopped at just
three.

03:14:02.819 --> 03:14:07.390
From four days of searching, he’d discovered
no fewer than seventeen different seemingly

03:14:07.390 --> 03:14:11.790
isolated crimes with mentions of Bobble the
Clown attached to the file.

03:14:11.790 --> 03:14:15.680
A five-year-old boy from New Jersey who’d
drowned his neighbors’ cat in a river with

03:14:15.680 --> 03:14:19.890
a gym bag full of heavy stones told police
that he’d learned the technique from Bobble

03:14:19.890 --> 03:14:20.890
the Clown.

03:14:20.890 --> 03:14:25.380
An eight-year-old girl, arrested for tying
up and torturing her sister with a rusty coat

03:14:25.380 --> 03:14:31.141
hanger in Texas, had, of course, gotten the
idea from watching an episode of Bobble the

03:14:31.141 --> 03:14:32.141
Clown.

03:14:32.141 --> 03:14:33.141
Murder.

03:14:33.141 --> 03:14:34.141
Assault.

03:14:34.141 --> 03:14:35.141
Vandalism.

03:14:35.141 --> 03:14:36.141
Torture.

03:14:36.141 --> 03:14:41.649
An extensive, country-wide rap sheet all led
back to that one recurring factor: They all

03:14:41.649 --> 03:14:44.310
learned it from watching Bobble the Clown.

03:14:44.310 --> 03:14:49.220
Dr. Whitington had gotten in contact with
a few friends who knew people in broadcasting.

03:14:49.220 --> 03:14:53.980
While carefully omitting some of the grislier
details, he implored them for any new information

03:14:53.980 --> 03:14:58.620
on whether a TV show with Bobble the Clown
had ever gone out, anywhere.

03:14:58.620 --> 03:15:02.800
But despite their best efforts, they didn’t
find any records of Bobble the Clown or any

03:15:02.800 --> 03:15:05.900
similar educational clown shows airing.

03:15:05.900 --> 03:15:08.940
Was it possibly some complex shared hallucination?

03:15:08.940 --> 03:15:14.859
Dr. Whitington simultaneously felt burdened
by all this terrifying knowledge, and utterly

03:15:14.859 --> 03:15:17.170
powerless to do anything useful with it.

03:15:17.170 --> 03:15:21.460
If he started blowing the whistle to the media
or his superiors that a spate of horrible

03:15:21.460 --> 03:15:26.440
crimes were all being caused by a violent,
imaginary clown, he’d look just as deranged

03:15:26.440 --> 03:15:28.939
as any of the people he’d been studying.

03:15:28.939 --> 03:15:33.689
There seemed to be nothing he could do to
stop or help any of this.

03:15:33.689 --> 03:15:37.920
He returned home that night with a heavy heart,
hanging up his coat.

03:15:37.920 --> 03:15:42.439
He needed someone to talk to about all this,
but he couldn’t burden his wife with the

03:15:42.439 --> 03:15:47.770
horrors he encountered daily on the job - Much
less a living nightmare like this mysterious

03:15:47.770 --> 03:15:49.370
Bobble The Clown.

03:15:49.370 --> 03:15:54.729
As he walked towards the kitchen to pour himself
a stiff drink, he heard strange, jaunty music

03:15:54.729 --> 03:15:56.529
coming from the living room.

03:15:56.529 --> 03:16:02.220
He stepped back, and saw his seven-year-old
son, Ben, watching something on TV.

03:16:02.220 --> 03:16:06.390
As he stepped closer, he could scarcely believe
his eyes.

03:16:06.390 --> 03:16:13.819
Ben entranced, eyes fixed on a dancing, grinning,
animated clown on the screen.

03:16:13.819 --> 03:16:18.979
Ben slowly turned his head towards Dr. Whitington,
eyes wide and bulging, and said, “I’ve

03:16:18.979 --> 03:16:21.330
been waiting for you to get home, Daddy.

03:16:21.330 --> 03:16:24.189
Bobble says he got tired of playing with Kevin.

03:16:24.189 --> 03:16:26.500
He wants to play with us now.”

03:16:26.500 --> 03:16:30.260
Dr. Whitington turned and looked at the clown
on the screen again.

03:16:30.260 --> 03:16:33.290
He could swear it was smiling right at him.

03:16:33.290 --> 03:16:38.700
That was the last thing he remembered before
the sudden intense headache, and the ground

03:16:38.700 --> 03:16:40.830
standing up to embrace him.

03:16:40.830 --> 03:16:46.230
When he woke up, he was in bed with his wife,
and neither of them could move - Thanks to

03:16:46.230 --> 03:16:49.380
the heavy ropes binding their body to the
frame.

03:16:49.380 --> 03:16:53.050
Bobble is very good at teaching children to
tie knots.

03:16:53.050 --> 03:16:58.940
They tried to scream, but a shiny flash of
duct tape held both of their mouths closed.

03:16:58.940 --> 03:17:04.090
Dr. Whitington’s eyes swiveled in his head
to Ben, standing at his bedside.

03:17:04.090 --> 03:17:10.600
The boy was holding a kitchen knife, and he
was very eager to show his mom and dad the

03:17:10.600 --> 03:17:14.410
fun new trick Bobble the Clown had taught
him.

03:17:14.410 --> 03:17:21.660
To the SCP Foundation, this terrifying anomalous
TV show is known as SCP-993 - Known to cause

03:17:21.660 --> 03:17:26.090
blackouts in adults and violent, antisocial
behavior in children.

03:17:26.090 --> 03:17:30.540
They do their best to keep the broadcasts
contained, but if ever a child in your life

03:17:30.540 --> 03:17:36.779
seems to be acting strangely, perhaps ask
yourself very carefully what they’re watching

03:17:36.779 --> 03:17:48.280
when you’re not around...

